	chapter.4EBBE730662AEE77.title: "Immersive Engineering"
	chapter.4F8BDDA81B610A6E.title: "Builder's Guide"
	chapter.558CA78B43A1AB58.title: "Chapter I: The Primal Age"
	chapter.5ECD77B1CFE80E47.title: "Chapter VI: The Steel Age"
	chapter.5F52D8A9F8E1917A.title: "Miner's Guide"
	chapter.6297E5687F69BB17.title: "Artisan's Guide"
	chapter.63A52A33C8BCC3E0.title: "Storage \\& Logistics"
	chapter.67F400134F02AEF7.title: "Before You Play"
	chapter.6B17A41CA8B64EFB.title: "Chef's Guide"
	chapter.6E436A1DF98C1A1A.title: "Stress \\& Transmission"
	chapter.6E63D2E12D7AADD8.title: "Create"
	chapter.714F689E91085F1A.title: "Beekeeping Guide"
	chapter.763725A3E967AF9C.title: "Animal Husbandry Guide"
	chapter.770B76471F7F0E60.title: "Aeronautics"
	chapter.78A071BB4504038C.title: "Chapter IV: The Bronze Age"
	chapter.7F68F8A72B162FA0.title: "Cosmonautics"
	chapter_group.47652EC60BA7B927.title: "Side Chapters: Things You Should Learn"
	chapter_group.7230BCDFA3557B8C.title: "Main Questline: You and TerraFirma"
	chapter_group.787619235D44E5B6.title: "Create \\& Immersive Engineering"
	quest.00572026F4A12262.quest_desc: [
		"Note: this chapter is still a work in progress!"
		""
		"&4None of this mod's content is available in survival mode yet! Back up your save before trying it in creative!!"
	]
	quest.00572026F4A12262.quest_subtitle: "Our goal is the sea of stars..."
	quest.00572026F4A12262.title: "Create: Cosmonautics"
	quest.0067038823493751.quest_desc: [
		"Deployers on contraptions cannot execute recipes — they can only mimic player actions. On the bright side, they consume no stress."
		""
		"If a deployer's filter is set to items stored in a container on the contraption, it will automatically use those items while the contraption moves."
		""
		"If the contraption has a container, drops from blocks broken by the deployer are transferred into it."
	]
	quest.0079DF1195F93142.quest_subtitle: "Slate, limestone, shale and the like, found near the surface"
	quest.0079DF1195F93142.title: "Borax"
	quest.008E955FDCA4F0CB.quest_desc: [
		"Graphite powder, kaolinite powder and clay can be crafted into fire clay — the material used for a whole series of blast furnace components later on."
	]
	quest.008E955FDCA4F0CB.title: "Tempered a Thousand Times"
	quest.00DDF32FC3452477.quest_desc: [
		"Create adds a whole series of storage and logistics blocks. There is so much of it that a dedicated chapter in the Create section covers them."
	]
	quest.00DDF32FC3452477.title: "Create Storage \\& Logistics"
	quest.00E9E6C8653D0E65.quest_desc: [
		"Opening an anvil shows this UI:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/smith.png width:170 height:90 align:1}"
		"①: A red ruler and a green ruler — your first goal is to align them"
		"②: Clicking moves the green ruler; don't push it out of bounds"
		"③: Your second goal — hover over it to see the required final three steps"
		"④: A weld button"
		""
		"Basic smithing means completing those two goals."
		""
		"If you have the smithing helper resource pack installed, you can see the value of every ruler move and technique — then it is just simple arithmetic."
	]
	quest.00EBCE85242695EF.quest_desc: [
		"To survive what comes next, you should start paying attention to your body temperature."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the 'Cold Sweat' side chapter."
	]
	quest.00EBCE85242695EF.title: "Cold Sweat"
	quest.012786034E6351BF.quest_desc: [
		"Even in vanilla Minecraft, farming and forestry are unavoidable — and in TerraFirmaCraft, where a huge share of resources comes from growing things, they are downright essential."
		""
		"Compared to vanilla, plants grow very slowly and demand much more from their environment; do it wrong and you may harvest nothing for ages. This chapter teaches you farming, forestry and beekeeping so that never happens."
	]
	quest.012786034E6351BF.title: "Farming Guide"
	quest.01439887E8F1802C.quest_desc: [
		"Craft rose quartz with an iron sheet to get electron tubes — one of the raw materials for most smart machines."
		""
		"The other material is the brass casing, obtained the same way as the andesite casing."
	]
	quest.01439887E8F1802C.title: "Smart Machinery"
	quest.014E3312B13E7457.quest_subtitle: "Sedimentary rock, near the surface"
	quest.014E3312B13E7457.title: "Magnetite"
	quest.01528A1A4E1B74CC.quest_desc: [
		"These two filters go into devices with filter slots to expand their filtering options. Both can be filled by dragging items straight from JEI."
		""
		"The list filter handles up to 18 individual items, while the attribute filter matches a whole class of items sharing a property. Stack filters together to copy configurations."
		""
		"Too many filter entries may lower TPS and cause lag!"
	]
	quest.01A897954EAC215B.quest_desc: [
		"Trains run on train tracks. Right-click to place one track piece on the ground, then right-click it again to drag out a whole stretch of track."
	]
	quest.01C4BFE307119D2B.quest_desc: [
		"Place eight kiln bricks in a 2x2x2 cube and right-click with an engineer's hammer to form the alloy kiln. It handles simple alloying, but has no logistics input or output."
	]
	quest.01FFB92709ABF783.quest_desc: [
		"Immersive Engineering is a mod focused on building multiblock machines. Its ultimate goal is the pinnacle of smelting: the arc furnace. Along the way you will unlock machines and items that make life much easier."
	]
	quest.01FFB92709ABF783.title: "Welcome to Immersive Engineering"
	quest.02079461CB4F1A98.quest_desc: [
		"With enough vinegar, you can seal food in it — each piece of food needs 125 mB of vinegar. Sealed this way, food lasts ten times longer; the vinegar is not consumed, but the barrel is occupied."
	]
	quest.02079461CB4F1A98.title: "Vinegar Sealing"
	quest.0209E651F7F5A346.quest_desc: [
		"Hold at least five clay to start clay knapping. It works like knapping stone tools, and you can also check JEI for the patterns."
		""
		"Fire a large vessel first — the pit kiln can only fire one of those at a time, while most other pottery can be fired four at once."
	]
	quest.0209E651F7F5A346.quest_subtitle: "No one wets clay and walks away, as if bricks would make themselves. — Plutarch"
	quest.0209E651F7F5A346.title: "Pottery"
	quest.020B7513E972F64E.quest_desc: [
		"Seal gypsum and concrete together in a barrel to get alabaster, which can be chiseled into its smooth variant just like natural rock."
	]
	quest.024C7F4406D16A26.quest_desc: [
		"The repackager must be connected to a container to work. When activated by a redstone signal, it merges the packages inside the connected container into one — handy for keeping crafting recipes in order when packages arrive from different sources."
	]
	quest.02988D2038D79AD9.quest_desc: [
		"The steam vent is the industrial upgrade of the burner: hooked to a steam boiler, it fills balloons with steam instead of hot air. Like the steam engine, it needs enough heat, water and boiler capacity."
		"Multiple vents can feed one balloon in parallel, as long as the boiler keeps up. More lift, more style — the standard of the airship age."
	]
	quest.02988D2038D79AD9.quest_subtitle: "Boiler-powered ascension"
	quest.02988D2038D79AD9.title: "Steam Vent"
	quest.02ED753941A99D46.quest_desc: [
		"Barley, wheat, rye, oats, maize and rice — these six crops are the grains. What they share: the raw crop itself has no nutritional value and must be processed into dough-based food first."
	]
	quest.02ED753941A99D46.title: "Grain Processing"
	quest.02FEAFC709453F5E.quest_desc: [
		"In case you didn't know: once you have wrought iron, vanilla chests can be crafted."
		""
		"Vanilla chests are the best fit for contraptions — they are recognized as storage blocks, and can even be opened directly while riding a contraption."
	]
	quest.0319BFEDA67C819B.quest_desc: [
		"This is an optional quest. If you haven't finished the previous chapter, completing it will unlock what follows."
	]
	quest.0319BFEDA67C819B.title: "Stone Javelin"
	quest.03376277C54B5225.quest_desc: [
		"The electric motor turns electricity back into rotational stress. Generator to wire to motor may sound like a pointless loop, but it matters enormously: rotation can now cross mountains through a wire, with no floors full of shafts and gears."
		"Power from a single water wheel can drive a machine hundreds of blocks away — that is the value of a grid."
	]
	quest.03376277C54B5225.quest_subtitle: "The road back for electricity"
	quest.03376277C54B5225.title: "Electric Motor"
	quest.03436E35E643FAC3.quest_desc: [
		"The windmill bearing automatically assembles the sail structure in front of it. Every 8 sail blocks give 1 RPM, capping at 128 sails (16 RPM). Wool, sails and sail frames all count."
		""
		"Windmills in this pack are very picky about location. Final efficiency is the product of four factors:"
		""
		"[Biome] Plains, plateaus, mountains, hills, badlands, windswept areas and all oceans are prime biomes (x1.0 efficiency); other biomes still spin, but at x0.75."
		"[Openness] A windmill needs a huge open area around it to catch the wind. Blocked by mountains or buildings, it stops entirely."
		"[Height] The bearing must sit 12 blocks above the surrounding terrain for full efficiency — at ground level you only get half. Build tall!"
		"[Live wind] TerraFirma's weather wind adds a real-time bonus: as low as x0.25 in calm weather, up to x1.5 in strong wind; ordinary wind means standard output."
		""
		"Stare at the bearing with engineer's goggles to read each current multiplier. A full-sail windmill, high up, in a prime biome, on a windy day outputs over ten thousand su of free stress."
	]
	quest.03840B3A92A037A3.quest_desc: [
		"Once Create is unlocked, the millstone can replace the quern for grinding, and hooked to power it works fully automatically. Simple materials: one cogwheel, one andesite casing, one stone — all craftable once you have andesite alloy. No zinc, no quartz needed."
	]
	quest.03B7D89DD6AC9237.quest_desc: [
		"The fluid pump actively moves fluids. Set its input and output with an engineer's hammer first; once powered by a redstone signal it pumps fluid from the input side to the output side. Feed it electricity and it runs even faster."
	]
	quest.0405DAAE5B61A651.quest_desc: [
		"Of course, you don't have to follow this questline — you can look up other guides online. Veterans have prepared guides in various communities; go find them."
		""
		"Two guides recommended by this pack:"
		""
		"1. 'The Evolution of a TFC Player — a complete 1.20.1 TerraFirmaCraft: Next Generation tutorial' by mcmod user '推窗子' (based on 1.20.1, but most mechanics still apply in 1.21.1)."
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Open page\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://www.mcmod.cn/post/3123.html\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
		""
		"2. '[Zero-to-hero TerraFirmaCraft guide] 2024 full babysitter tutorial' by Bilibili creator '猪人喜欢朋友'."
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Open page\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://space.bilibili.com/13243373/channel/collectiondetail?sid=3399778\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
	]
	quest.0405DAAE5B61A651.quest_subtitle: "Please support the guides other veterans worked hard on — the TFC community thrives because of them"
	quest.0405DAAE5B61A651.title: "Other Guides"
	quest.0436DD294285DBC9.quest_desc: [
		"Use shears to harvest wool."
	]
	quest.0436DD294285DBC9.quest_subtitle: "The sheep has no objection"
	quest.0436DD294285DBC9.title: "Shearing Sheep"
	quest.045DD6FE26295735.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a honey-looking hive with an empty glass jar to fill it with honey. Bees may attack you in the process, depending on how calm they are."
		""
		"Craft a full honey jar once to get raw honey — a sweetener that can replace sugar."
	]
	quest.048A9394DA1A65F2.quest_desc: [
		"The compost tumbler is the upgraded composter, powered by TerraFirma-style rotation. It has twice the capacity and can even take a little meat and bone."
		""
		"Items can only be put in while it is unpowered, and it only processes compost while powered — consider hooking it up through a clutch."
		""
		"A total of 32 units of input yields 3 compost, 24+ units yields 2, and 16+ yields just 1. Below that you get nothing."
	]
	quest.048A9394DA1A65F2.quest_subtitle: "More compost"
	quest.0490196856A3B732.quest_desc: [
		"Don't throw bones away — grind them in a quern into bone meal."
		"Bone meal is a natural phosphate fertilizer for crops, and also the base for white dye."
	]
	quest.0490196856A3B732.quest_subtitle: "Crunchy"
	quest.0490196856A3B732.title: "Bone Meal"
	quest.04CBBF61E5ACDAD5.quest_desc: [
		"Flour can be made into noodles — rice flour makes rice noodles instead. Both can be stir-fried directly in a pan, and noodles can be crafted with tomato sauce and other ingredients into lasagna. "
	]
	quest.051EA6F7628BA048.quest_desc: [
		"Create integrates nicely with vanilla redstone: some blocks respond to redstone control, and there are convenient redstone components such as simple pulse generators and wireless redstone. Check the Ponder scenes for details."
	]
	quest.051EA6F7628BA048.title: "Advanced Redstone Control"
	quest.0521B9E491C0D01C.quest_desc: [
		"Mailboxes work with trains to transport packages, but must first be bound to a train station."
		""
		"Right-click to open the mailbox and configure its address at the top. When an arriving train carries a package with a matching address, it is unloaded; conversely, packages in the mailbox are loaded onto the train."
		""
		"Like trains, mailboxes keep loading and unloading even when the chunk is unloaded."
	]
	quest.055FFAB83C1BE571.quest_desc: [
		"The contraption controls block operates machines mounted on a contraption. Install it, right-click it, and toggle whether the contraption's machines run. Set a filter to control specific machines only."
			"The Linked Controller works handheld on any bound contraption. If you want it lectern-mounted, bind it to the lectern on the ground BEFORE assembly — lecterns inside a physics structure cannot be converted. Note: repeated assembly and disassembly of physics structures makes the lectern lose the controller's binding data; on aircraft, prefer the ship helm and controls."
]
	quest.055FFAB83C1BE571.title: "Advanced Contraptions"
	quest.057BFABF2D5AED4C.quest_desc: [
		"The diesel generator is the highest-output generator in Immersive Engineering, burning biodiesel for 4096 FE/t."
		""
		"The output is so high that it has three connection points, preventing a single wire from being unable to carry it all. Power splits evenly across the three lines."
	]
	quest.057BFABF2D5AED4C.quest_subtitle: "Not just exhaust pollution — noise pollution too"
	quest.057BFABF2D5AED4C.title: "Environmental Pollution"
	quest.058D3C28DA2940FD.quest_desc: [
		"The grain mill grinds grain into flour — see JEI for the setup. It yields twice the flour of a hand quern and has automatable input and output."
	]
	quest.058D3C28DA2940FD.quest_subtitle: "Crush them!"
	quest.058D3C28DA2940FD.title: "Grain Mill"
	quest.0593955C5444B2DB.quest_desc: [
		"The rotation inverter reverses the direction of incoming power while activated by redstone."
	]
	quest.059C1DB7E27EF2BE.quest_desc: [
		"Seal sand in a barrel of limewater to get mortar. Mortar is mainly a building material ingredient, most often used for stone bricks."
	]
	quest.059C1DB7E27EF2BE.quest_subtitle: "Meet at the village entrance, bring your own cement"
	quest.0658304215058402.quest_desc: [
		"The mixing bowl has five item slots and one fluid slot for processing certain ingredients. You need to put a spoon in it before it works."
	]
	quest.073A1A75F3452258.quest_desc: [
		"Mix steel, nickel and black bronze in the right proportions to get weak steel."
	]
	quest.075AE6BBAE11F698.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to Electrical Engineering. This mod brings Create a true-to-life power system: generators turn rotation into electricity, wires carry it far away, and appliances turn it back into light, heat and motion."
		""
		"It coexists with Immersive Engineering's generators, and there are ways to convert its power into the FE that IE machines need. Its efficiency beats IE's power generation handily, but the learning curve is real."
		""
		"This system simulates real circuits — voltage, current, resistance: overloaded wires burn out, overloaded devices break, and touching a live connector barehanded will shock you. Don't worry — this chapter walks you from your very first wire all the way to an electrified railway."
		""
		"Tip: most devices in this chapter come with Ponder animation tutorials. Hold W on them in your inventory or JEI — far clearer than any text."
		""
		"Note: this chapter is still a work in progress. You can watch the tutorial video by TrueAnnYpsT!"
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Tutorial video (Bilibili)\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1ck3p6AEDY/\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
	]
	quest.075AE6BBAE11F698.quest_subtitle: "From spark to grid"
	quest.075AE6BBAE11F698.title: "Electrical Engineering"
	quest.075F00263E56C723.quest_desc: [
		"Your obsession with mining has surpassed the dwarves — you are the true mining tycoon."
	]
	quest.075F00263E56C723.title: "&eChallenge: Mining Tycoon"
	quest.077923B370F52B53.quest_desc: [
		"One mechanical bearing, one chest, one mechanical saw and two portable storage interfaces make a simple tree farm. Add a deployer if you want automatic sapling planting."
	]
	quest.077923B370F52B53.title: "Automatic Tree Farm"
	quest.077A6316F3122567.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have steel, there isn't much TerraFirma content left — metals above steel have limited uses. Steel mostly goes into building Immersive Engineering machines, though forging black, red and blue steel still eats plenty of it."
	]
	quest.077A6316F3122567.quest_subtitle: "The biggest challenge is done; the rest is easier"
	quest.077A6316F3122567.title: "Chapter VI: Chapter Goal"
	quest.07A894FCB5BD3AFC.quest_desc: [
		"To run a bloomery, drop materials in through the chimney. The bloomery holds up to 192 items (64 per chimney level, up to three levels). The rule: every 100 mB of iron in the input eventually yields one wrought iron ingot, and each batch needs two charcoal to match."
		""
		"For example, using 100 mB cast iron ingots as input means 16 ingots plus 32 charcoal, producing 16 wrought iron ingots."
		""
		"Once fully loaded, seal the bloomery block and light it to start smelting. One cycle takes 15 in-game hours."
	]
	quest.07A894FCB5BD3AFC.quest_subtitle: "Fe2O3+3CO==2Fe+3CO2 (high temp)"
	quest.07A894FCB5BD3AFC.title: "Bloomery Guide"
	quest.081423E323406D0D.quest_desc: [
		"The stainless steel pot only works on an oven base and can batch-process certain pot recipes — see JEI."
		""
		"Mind the ingredient ratios when using the pot, and sneak-right-click to put the lid on, or it won't run."
	]
	quest.086DCB92F2D515AC.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a brass casing with a sturdy sheet to get a train casing — the base block of trains."
		""
		"A train station creates a stop: hold the station block and click a spot on the track to set the stopping point, then place the station."
		""
		"The station offers a 'create train' option. Building a train is much like building a contraption: hold a train casing and right-click the track to place a bogey — two bogeys per carriage is best. Then build the carriage, glue it together with super glue, and finally place a controls block."
		""
		"You can use a wrench to move a train onto nearby tracks."
	]
	quest.086DCB92F2D515AC.quest_subtitle: "An ugly train clips through every corner"
	quest.086DCB92F2D515AC.title: "Building Trains"
	quest.0881C669347BC338.quest_desc: [
		"If — and I mean if — you spawn in tropical mountains and happen to see the blocks in the image below: dig them. Don't ask why. Dig them."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/kaolin.png width:119 height:57 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0881C669347BC338.title: "Kaolin!"
	quest.08C79C6017BF4193.quest_desc: [
		"The Cold Sweat–TFC compat mod gives most medium and large animals furs with different insulation properties, all craftable into clothing."
	]
	quest.08E78907ED01EFB3.quest_desc: [
		"Grapes must be grown on a special trellis: place two two-block-high grape posts one block apart (the protruding parts facing each other)."
		""
		"Then connect the two with jute fiber. Plant grapes on the ground between the posts; as they grow they spread onto the trellis above."
		""
		"You can also grow grapes in a greenhouse using lattice planters."
	]
	quest.08F44649495B615A.quest_subtitle: "Below y=0 in intrusive igneous rock, mostly gabbro"
	quest.08F44649495B615A.title: "Garnierite"
	quest.093E2CBCB7707870.quest_desc: [
		"The fluid splitter moves inserted or dropped items one block in the input direction, then ejects them (items dropped vertically default to north)."
		""
		"Sounds useless, but this is actually Create's rare one-block logistics: the classic setup is andesite funnel into splitter, splitter rolling items onto a depot."
	]
	quest.093E2CBCB7707870.quest_subtitle: "A textbook case of the side use beating the main use"
	quest.093E2CBCB7707870.title: "Alternative Logistics"
	quest.094D58277DD958E3.quest_desc: [
		"In Create 6.0, Create gained an AE-like logistics system: build a network from a series of logistics devices to store and retrieve items, order crafts, run shops and deliver mail."
	]
	quest.094D58277DD958E3.title: "Advanced Logistics"
	quest.098B2C65DDD98688.quest_desc: [
		"Lumber is used to craft many blocks; some of them also need planks."
	]
	quest.098B2C65DDD98688.title: "Lumber"
	quest.099A619313B81629.quest_desc: [
		"The moment you got this, you probably realized it's the TerraFirmaCraft guide book — it says TerraFirmaCraft right on the cover."
		""
		"Open it by right-clicking with it in hand, or look at the right side of your inventory — five extra buttons appeared there; the bottom one has the same icon as this book."
		""
		"You can search entries from any chapter just by typing."
		""
		"Note: the book may occasionally conflict with the questline — when in doubt, the questline is right. If you spot an error in the book, please report it."
	]
	quest.099A619313B81629.quest_subtitle: "If you lose it, come back here for a new one"
	quest.099A619313B81629.title: "About This Book"
	quest.09CE4D4DF2AE6255.quest_desc: [
		"The crusher crushes various ores and is part of ore processing for extra yield. See the Immersive Engineering Engineer's Manual for assembly."
		""
		"There is a control panel on the front that takes a redstone signal. Falling into the crusher hurts a lot. Likewise, items it can't process are destroyed."
	]
	quest.09CE4D4DF2AE6255.quest_subtitle: "Once your home has a crusher, your home IS the crusher."
	quest.09CE4D4DF2AE6255.title: "Dangerous Machinery"
	quest.09FF39E8779DCF92.quest_desc: [
		"The millstone runs grinding recipes. It works much like the quern, but with more recipes, input/output on all six faces, and no grinding stone to wear out."
	]
	quest.09FF39E8779DCF92.quest_subtitle: "It's a millstone, not graphite"
	quest.09FF39E8779DCF92.title: "Hands-Free Grinding"
	quest.0A4C81319EA728EC.quest_desc: [
		"The portable engine is the heart of any vehicle: one fluid tank, one encased fan, wrapped in six wrought iron sheets — craft and go."
		"It runs on Immersive Engineering biodiesel: normal engines drink biodiesel, the red super engines only drink high-power biodiesel (double burn time). Right-click with a fuel bucket to refill; pipes also work."
		"Feed it a blaze cake for superheating and extra output."
	]
	quest.0A4C81319EA728EC.quest_subtitle: "The heart of the vehicle"
	quest.0A4C81319EA728EC.title: "Portable Engine"
	quest.0A5B42FDCB46B18B.quest_subtitle: "Below y=60 (effectively ~0): schist, marble, quartzite, phyllite"
	quest.0A5B42FDCB46B18B.title: "Graphite"
	quest.0ABF6F581A681D48.quest_desc: [
		"If you desperately need a tree, try tree fertilizer — it grows a sapling instantly."
	]
	quest.0AD32C7C666A7387.quest_desc: [
		"The crucible is vanilla TFC's highest-tier metallurgy block, used on top of a charcoal forge. It has nine smelting slots and stores 4000 mB of molten metal. Its temperature follows the forge below and can likewise be pushed to brilliant white with a bellows."
		""
		"Metal melted in the crucible stays stored inside; place a mold or small vessel in the rightmost slot to fill it with molten metal."
		""
		"If different molten metals are loaded into the same crucible, they alloy automatically. As long as the metal doesn't solidify or get moved to another container, correctly proportioned melts always alloy correctly."
		""
		"A wrong ratio no longer ruins everything — as long as the dominant metal is at least 75%, you get an inferior alloy that still smiths into tools bearing an 'inferior' mark. But inferior metal can't enter industrial alloy lines like the arc furnace, so don't try to sneak it through."
		""
		"Fine-tuning tip: when whole ingots can't hit the ratio, adjust with ore pieces — poor 10 mB, normal 20 mB, rich 30 mB. They melt in the crucible just the same and let you dial the mix in far more precisely than ingots alone."
	]
	quest.0AD32C7C666A7387.title: "Crucible"
	quest.0AFC300FD356CFA5.quest_desc: [
		"Mortar is the base material for most building blocks, made by sealing sand with limewater."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the 'Builder's Guide' side chapter."
	]
	quest.0B3408BA5F50B009.quest_desc: [
		"Seal alcohol for a while to get aged alcohol. Compared to fresh brews, aged drinks give longer-lasting or higher-level effects."
	]
	quest.0B3408BA5F50B009.quest_subtitle: "Older, stronger"
	quest.0B3408BA5F50B009.title: "Aged to Perfection"
	quest.0B60FB437AD62D0B.quest_desc: [
		"Boil olive paste — made by grinding olives — in a pot to get crude olive oil."
	]
	quest.0B92663BAE48B51B.quest_desc: [
		" You may know that Create's stress and TerraFirma's rotational power are two completely separate systems that normally can't interconnect. This item converts stress into TFC rotation, letting you drive TerraFirmaCraft devices."
		""
		"See the Ponder scene (hold W) for usage."
	]
	quest.0B92663BAE48B51B.quest_subtitle: "Power conversion"
	quest.0B92663BAE48B51B.title: "Stress --> TFC Rotation"
	quest.0B94A6058F1333A5.title: "Milk"
	quest.0BC70390C3F82272.quest_subtitle: "Above y=40, sedimentary and extrusive rock under riverbeds"
	quest.0BC70390C3F82272.title: "Opal"
	quest.0BD0439BCE9C2B81.quest_desc: [
		"Pets come in two kinds — dogs and cats, descended from wolves and ocelots. You must feed their wild ancestors to domestication, then keep feeding to 15% familiarity for them to accept you as owner."
		""
		"Dogs eat grains, vegetables and meat (even rotten). Cats eat grains, dairy and cooked meat."
	]
	quest.0BD0439BCE9C2B81.quest_subtitle: "Man's best friend is...?"
	quest.0BD0439BCE9C2B81.title: "Pets"
	quest.0BDCE830FD82089F.quest_desc: [
		"The belching flower is a rare functional plant that spawns in any region and can transform blocks."
		""
		"To make it work, place sulfur (powdered) behind the flower (its wider side); it will slowly charge up. When fully charged it lets out a belch and tries to transform the block in front of it."
		""
		"It can turn charcoal piles into cursed coal piles, nether bricks into netheritic bricks, and raise the 'decay' nutrient of soul farmland."
	]
	quest.0BF37DE9318ADB2A.quest_desc: [
		"Mix steel, nickel and chromium in the right proportions to get stainless steel."
		""
		"Stainless steel has few but real uses: building stainless greenhouses, or making solar dryers that process twelve times faster than drying mats."
	]
	quest.0CF4459CAC90B58C.quest_desc: [
		"Blown glass and glass panes are simple, but other glassware is trickier — specific steps in a specific order. Check JEI for the sequences."
	]
	quest.0CF4459CAC90B58C.title: "Glassworking"
	quest.0CFD282963A88F95.quest_desc: [
		"Wild animals in the TerraFirma world are finite — kill one and it's gone for good. Better to protect the tamable ones for later."
		""
		"Sneak-look at a tamable animal to see its familiarity. Mammals need at least two blocks of headroom to be penned; birds need four."
		""
		"Complete this quest to unlock the 'Animal Husbandry Guide' side chapter."
	]
	quest.0CFD282963A88F95.quest_subtitle: "This is sustainable development"
	quest.0CFD282963A88F95.title: "Strategic Encirclement"
	quest.0D2A81C985754D33.quest_desc: [
		"Vinegar comes from sealing alcohol with fruit in a barrel — each fruit matches 250 mB of alcohol."
		""
		"Brined food sealed further in vinegar gains the 'pickled' buff: +50% shelf life, at 125 mB of vinegar per item."
	]
	quest.0D2A81C985754D33.title: "Pickling"
	quest.0D35BFD32CAB74BD.quest_desc: [
		"Yes, another anvil. You can't work metal without one, so ready 14 more iron ingots."
	]
	quest.0D35BFD32CAB74BD.quest_subtitle: "No enchanted books here"
	quest.0E650687F02D8523.quest_desc: [
		"The soul fire lantern effectively resists high temperatures and helps you roam the Nether freely."
		""
		"It burns fuel: soul sprouts, a crop grown in the Nether. The hotter the environment, the faster it burns."
		""
		"Held in either hand, it projects a 9x9 aura that can lower entities' temperature to one degree below the overheating cap."
	]
	quest.0E65B41C92E17572.quest_desc: [
		"The quern grinds items. Craft the quern base and the handstone, then place the handstone on the base. The handstone has durability and must be remade once broken."
		""
		"Place an item with a quern recipe on the center of the handstone and right-click to grind. Products pile up on the base; take them with an empty-hand right-click. The base stores up to 64 items."
	]
	quest.0E65B41C92E17572.quest_subtitle: "And the big tiring thing"
	quest.0E65B41C92E17572.title: "The Little Tiring Thing"
	quest.0E9454F2656BBB89.quest_desc: [
		"The physics assembler is the heart of Aeronautics: select a group of blocks with super glue or honey glue, then right-click the assembler and pull the lever to assemble them into a vehicle with real physics. Note that diagonally adjacent blocks get glued too."
		"Once assembled, the assembler is no longer needed; any assembler can disassemble a physics structure back into blocks."
		"Blocks on a physics structure each have their own weight and traits (light, very heavy, slippery, fragile...). Check a block's physical properties in its tooltip before building ships or cars."
		""
		"&4Warning: TerraFirma's gravity blocks (dirt, grass, clay, peat, cobblestone, sand, gravel — anything prone to collapse) cannot be assembled into physics structures, nor placed onto an already-physicalized vehicle. &rThe physics engine can't hold up collapsing material; this is an anti-corruption safeguard specific to this pack."
	]
	quest.0E9454F2656BBB89.quest_subtitle: "The holy sword of physics"
	quest.0E9454F2656BBB89.title: "Physics Assembler"
	quest.0E9DCEC6190B6CC9.quest_desc: [
		"Boiling salt water in a pot yields one salt per 125 mB. Note a clay pot yields at most five salt per batch."
	]
	quest.0E9DCEC6190B6CC9.quest_subtitle: "Salt from brine"
	quest.0EBEBC430F74E991.quest_desc: [
		"Seal a prepared hide in a barrel of tannin for a while to get leather: large hides give 3 leather, medium 2, small 1."
	]
	quest.0EBEBC430F74E991.quest_subtitle: "Genuine leather"
	quest.0F17A8D9D2F281E7.quest_desc: [
		"Strictly speaking, rail transport isn't exploration — at best it 'saves you from re-walking the same route'. Still, for places you visit often, it's invaluable."
	]
	quest.0F17A8D9D2F281E7.title: "Rail Transport"
	quest.0F5B2728A7868BC3.quest_desc: [
		"Power machinery consumes stress to work: grinding, pressing, sawing, mixing, even an automatic crafting table."
	]
	quest.0F5B2728A7868BC3.title: "Power Machinery"
	quest.0F66B28732EAA8C5.quest_desc: [
		"Once you obtain any copper-alloy item, this chapter opens automatically."
	]
	quest.0F66B28732EAA8C5.title: "Copper Alloys"
	quest.0F97AEAD57E3CC06.quest_desc: [
		"As a place full of lava, the Nether is understandably scorching. Enter unprepared and the extreme heat will give you heatstroke, dehydration, and finally death."
		""
		"Use every cooling method available: heat-resistant clothing, a cool waterskin, or soul sprouts gathered in the Nether that lower body temperature. Crafting the soul-sprout-fueled soul fire lantern is also well worth it."
	]
	quest.0F97AEAD57E3CC06.quest_subtitle: "One slip and you're a torch"
	quest.0F97AEAD57E3CC06.title: "Preparation: Temperature"
	quest.0F9D093B94BB5654.quest_desc: [
		"Pottery needs clay, which generates abundantly where rainfall exceeds 175 mm. Clay blocks blend into grass and are hard to spot by eye, but the indicator at the top of the screen helps you find them."
		""
		"Certain plants also mark clay: athyrium ferns, canna, goldenrod, pampas grass, russian sage and water canna — clay likely generates beneath them. Small amounts also appear near lakes and rivers."
		""
		"Finding clay isn't hard, but if you've searched for nearly an hour without luck, using a helper mod or starting a fresh world is a fine choice."
	]
	quest.0F9D093B94BB5654.title: "Gathering Clay"
	quest.0FE8624158DB509E.quest_desc: [
		"With or without the smithing helper, you've learned to forge perfect tools. Congratulations — here's your reward."
	]
	quest.0FE8624158DB509E.quest_subtitle: "Perfect!"
	quest.0FE8624158DB509E.title: "&eChallenge: Perfect Smithing"
	quest.0FF8890123C28762.quest_desc: [
		"The prospector's pick surveys a 25x25x25 area around the right-clicked block and reports the type and amount of one ore within."
		""
		"Low-tier prospector's picks can give false negatives — they may miss ore that exists, but will never report ore that doesn't. Higher tiers are more accurate."
		""
		"A surface prospecting trick: find the boundary between 'very large' and 'large' readings, connect the points, and dig down from the center of the enclosed shape."
	]
	quest.1005BE3C28B3739A.quest_desc: [
		"The copper casing sheathes pipes and is used in later machines."
	]
	quest.1005BE3C28B3739A.quest_subtitle: "Never leaks"
	quest.10177654911AEBF1.quest_desc: [
		"One of the strongest fuels: high burn temperature with decent burn time. Made in the coke oven from two kinds of coal after the Iron Age."
	]
	quest.102E427D31CED155.quest_desc: [
		"Time to upgrade the leather waterskin: the iron flask holds 2000 mB — more than a barrel — and has four times the durability."
	]
	quest.102E427D31CED155.quest_subtitle: "A volume that defies reason"
	quest.1059656A3A30BD26.quest_desc: [
		"Kaolin generates on plateaus, highlands and old mountains with average temperature above 18 and rainfall above 300. Press F3 to see the temperature and rainfall at your position. It looks like this:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/kaolin.png width:150 height:70 align:1}"
		"Kaolin grass hides among normal grass blocks, making it hard to spot. Look for a plant called the fireball flower — where it grows, kaolin is below, sometimes at the surface, sometimes 20 blocks down."
	]
	quest.1059656A3A30BD26.title: "Finding Kaolin"
	quest.105AB4CF8D7237F4.quest_desc: [
		"Belts move items as dropped entities, in horizontal, vertical, extracting, unloading and splitting forms. Upside: they work forever without limits. Downside: slow, and item-entity logistics is a headache."
	]
	quest.1061F636FD641E92.quest_desc: [
		"Smithing wrought iron takes huge amounts of charcoal. If you're short, stock up first."
	]
	quest.1061F636FD641E92.quest_subtitle: "Prepare for a rainy day"
	quest.1061F636FD641E92.title: "Mass Charcoal Burning"
	quest.10C0DBCBA961CB05.quest_desc: [
		"Logs count as 'very large' items and can't go in any TerraFirmaCraft container. Early on, sneak-place a log to consume it and place a log pile block — it has 4 slots, each holding 4 logs of the same wood."
	]
	quest.10C0DBCBA961CB05.title: "Storing Logs"
	quest.10E7BA2131CC0264.quest_desc: [
		"The clockwork bearing recognizes two glued zones in front of it as the hour and minute hands."
		""
		"Powered with stress, its hands rotate according to the world time — matching the TerraFirma calendar too."
	]
	quest.119CEDE0A8B2E7F2.quest_desc: [
		"Water freezes in winter. Once you know Create, you can also craft nine snow blocks into ice — but ice melts outside winter, so craft packed ice and blue ice instead."
	]
	quest.119CEDE0A8B2E7F2.title: "Ice"
	quest.11FCBEA058E78F53.quest_desc: [
		"A clay oven adds the 'oven-baked' tag to food cooked in it, giving a better shelf-life bonus than a campfire."
	]
	quest.11FCBEA058E78F53.title: "Oven"
	quest.1226BC6DFC7C7CF5.quest_desc: [
		"Items shaped from clay and then heat-hardened — like the large vessel — are pottery. Most pottery serves as containers; some are tools."
	]
	quest.1226BC6DFC7C7CF5.title: "Pottery Ware"
	quest.129AB7613941AE8B.quest_desc: [
		"A tortilla plus shredded cheese, tomato sauce, one meat and one vegetable makes a burrito — nearly the same recipe as the pancake. Think of it as another kind of sandwich."
	]
	quest.1382F683D7FA62BB.quest_desc: [
		"Costs 18 sticks. Its burn efficiency can't match logs, but it can go into a log pile and char into charcoal."
	]
	quest.13D0A02DCEA6CD13.quest_desc: [
		"From copper alloys onward, the first step with every higher-tier metal is making its anvil, which takes 7 double ingots. Copper-alloy double ingots must be welded on a copper anvil."
	]
	quest.13D0A02DCEA6CD13.quest_subtitle: "Same as when you made the copper anvil"
	quest.13D0A02DCEA6CD13.title: "Copper-Alloy Double Ingots"
	quest.13FE245B80FF492C.quest_desc: [
		"A small vessel holds at most one stack of copper dust — 320 mB of copper. For better efficiency, craft four dusts into a 20 mB ore chunk; four chunks make an 80 mB ore cluster."
	]
	quest.13FE245B80FF492C.title: "Compacting Copper Dust"
	quest.140CA6C75C16C942.quest_desc: [
		"The simplest cookware — roasts food"
	]
	quest.140CA6C75C16C942.title: "Campfire"
	quest.142140E2E271B7D2.quest_desc: [
		"Mount a steering wheel and throttle lever on your vehicle to drive it yourself: hold right-click to grab the wheel, move the mouse to steer, sneak-turn for 45-degree steps. Drag the throttle with right-click for precise analog control of engine output."
		"A redstone comparator behind the wheel reads the steering angle. Set the bearing mode correctly, or your structure may turn back into blocks mid-drive."
	]
	quest.142140E2E271B7D2.quest_subtitle: "Got your driver's license?"
	quest.142140E2E271B7D2.title: "Steering Wheel \\& Throttle"
	quest.144A45B3C280CA58.quest_desc: [
		"Brine is salt water mixed with vinegar at a 9:1 ratio."
		""
		"Most foods can be sealed in a barrel of brine to gain the 'brined' buff. Only brined food can be further pickled for shelf life. Each item brined consumes 125 mB of brine."
	]
	quest.144A45B3C280CA58.title: "Brining"
	quest.1450C76C168E8678.quest_desc: [
		"The deployer processes items with a held item, requiring a depot or belt two blocks below it. Example recipe: holding sandpaper to polish rose quartz. A filter slot on it specifies the held item."
		""
		"Deployers also count as fake players: they can right-click-use an item two blocks ahead, or left-click attack. Switch modes with a wrench."
	]
	quest.1450C76C168E8678.quest_subtitle: "The king's right hand"
	quest.1457B4E84642DF12.quest_desc: [
		"Basic logistics devices are the simple things that move items from one place to another."
	]
	quest.1457B4E84642DF12.title: "Basic Logistics"
	quest.149844B06EC2B2F0.quest_desc: [
		"Vegetables with naturally long shelf lives need no extra processing — garlic in a cellar keeps for a year as-is."
		""
		"For normal processing, just follow brine → pickle → seal. Vegetables have no unique steps."
	]
	quest.149844B06EC2B2F0.title: "Vegetables"
	quest.1499D994BE32EB6D.quest_subtitle: "Sedimentary rock near the surface"
	quest.1499D994BE32EB6D.title: "Rock Salt"
	quest.14A11CD892C4F1F3.quest_desc: [
		"The adze is a tool for paving roads and roofing more efficiently: roofs made with it cost less material, and its roads give a speed boost."
	]
	quest.14A11CD892C4F1F3.title: "Roofs \\& Roads"
	quest.14AB9880993734CD.quest_desc: [
		"The linked typewriter is the core of wireless redstone: two linked typewriters transmit redstone signals across any distance, and when active one takes over movement controls and all assigned keys."
		"Sneak-right-click to open its config; in bind mode, press any key to bind it to a wireless frequency. Remote-pilot an airship from the ground — or the reverse."
		"You can also mount a typewriter on a vanilla lectern to make a fixed control station: right-click the lectern to pilot from where you stand. Only vanilla lecterns work — the old wooden TFC lecterns will just clamp it like a book, so don't bother."
	]
	quest.14AB9880993734CD.quest_subtitle: "The age of remote control"
	quest.14AB9880993734CD.title: "Linked Typewriter"
	quest.14B141E51322E51E.quest_desc: [
		"Before you set out, prepare well."
		""
		"First, you need decent gear or life-saving measures so you don't die and get sent home mid-journey."
		""
		"Second, make a backpack — ideally several copper-tier ones — to haul your loot home in one trip."
		""
		"Third, prepare transport for the journey — boat, horse or aircraft all beat walking."
		""
		"Fourth, prepare heat protection. The tropics and the Nether are both hot; beware heatstroke."
		""
		"Fifth, stock food and water."
	]
	quest.14B141E51322E51E.title: "Preparations"
	quest.14B2CA889CED1685.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click livestock with food to raise their familiarity — at most once per day; skipping a day lowers it."
		""
		"As familiarity rises, the black heart fills with red. A white outline means it won't drop without feeding; a red outline means it's full."
		""
		"Wild-caught animals cap at 35% familiarity; their offspring can reach 100%."
		""
		"You can also craft a feeding trough to feed animals automatically!"
	]
	quest.14B2CA889CED1685.title: "Feeding"
	quest.14B52DDE8430672C.quest_desc: [
		"Lumber replaces planks in recipes — saw a log to get four."
	]
	quest.1597FFAC1D8851E8.quest_desc: [
		"The compost tumbler is the upgraded composter, powered by TerraFirma-style rotation. It has twice the capacity and can even take a little meat and bone."
		""
		"Items can only be put in while it is unpowered, and it only processes compost while powered — consider hooking it up through a clutch."
		""
		"A total of 32 units of input yields 3 compost, 24+ units yields 2, and 16+ yields just 1. Below that you get nothing."
	]
	quest.15D5737B671A7F2A.quest_desc: [
		"Minecarts are primitive but still effective, and Create gives them many more functions."
		""
		"If you really want to build a minecart line, look at the minecart coupling and the cart assembler."
	]
	quest.15D5737B671A7F2A.title: "Minecarts"
	quest.15E83F8A71435163.quest_desc: [
		"Your first appliance starts with a lamp. Wire a bulb into the generator's circuit, add a breaker switch — snap, the electrical age arrives at your base."
		"Even unlit, bulbs stop monsters from spawning nearby — great for spawn-proofing."
		"If a bulb burns out the instant it lights, the voltage is too high: build a transformer to step it down first, and a fuse can save you too."
	]
	quest.15E83F8A71435163.quest_subtitle: "The Edison moment"
	quest.15E83F8A71435163.title: "Lighting the Bulb"
	quest.1654D34A7C0C9198.quest_desc: [
		"A pancake shell plus shredded cheese, tomato sauce, one meat and one vegetable makes a Mexican pancake — nearly the same recipe as the burrito. Think of it as another kind of sandwich."
	]
	quest.1658AD7F89A9C484.quest_desc: [
		"Builders, there's good news and bad news. Good news: TerraFirmaCraft has plenty of building block varieties. Bad news: their aesthetics aren't for everyone."
	]
	quest.1658AD7F89A9C484.title: "Builder's Guide"
	quest.16AC8D3CB8FA3933.quest_subtitle: "Surface sedimentary rock, underground intrusive rock — more the deeper you go"
	quest.16AC8D3CB8FA3933.title: "Bismuthinite"
	quest.16C867DD567F1FBB.quest_desc: [
		"A bellows can be automated with a crank — though you could already do it with a deployer."
	]
	quest.16C867DD567F1FBB.title: "Automatic Bellows"
	quest.1702D2412B7F5094.quest_desc: [
		"Leather is an important material in TerraFirmaCraft, requiring a barrel and a series of fluids. You can start making it now."
	]
	quest.1702D2412B7F5094.title: "Leatherworking"
	quest.1768230458B173BE.quest_desc: [
		"In TerraFirma, every item has a size and a weight, which determine where it can be stored and how it stacks."
		""
		"Size first: it decides which containers can hold the item — details come with the container introductions."
		""
		"Then weight: it decides stack size."
		""
		"Very light items stack to 64, light to 32, medium to 16, heavy to 4, very heavy to 1."
		""
		"Note especially: carrying one item that is both enormous and very heavy drains your hunger and thirst faster."
		"Carrying two such items gives you the Overburdened debuff and you can barely walk. Don't haul them around for long."
	]
	quest.1768230458B173BE.quest_subtitle: "Say goodbye to the Steve who carries nine pigs across a river"
	quest.1768230458B173BE.title: "Size \\& Weight"
	quest.17A717AD41AEB01E.quest_desc: [
		"Weld a weak steel ingot with a pig iron ingot to get a high-carbon black steel ingot; smith that to get black steel."
		""
		"Black steel is tier V. Besides black steel tools and upgrading the gold backpack, its main use is forging red and blue steel."
	]
	quest.17A717AD41AEB01E.quest_subtitle: "The night gave me black eyes, yet I use them to forge black steel"
	quest.17A717AD41AEB01E.title: "&0Deep as the Night"
	quest.17B4BC82A921F900.quest_desc: [
		"Check the quest book now and then — besides the beginner questline, it holds info on plenty of handy gadgets."
		""
		"If you see a quest-required food item rotted, don't worry — that's a quirk of TFC food code interacting with quests, and it doesn't affect completion in most cases."
	]
	quest.17B4BC82A921F900.quest_subtitle: "Come back often"
	quest.17B4BC82A921F900.title: "The Quest Book"
	quest.17DCD1E10495ABA7.quest_desc: [
		"You may have melted iron ore straight away, hoping to cast iron ingots — only to end up with a dark ingot: cast iron."
		""
		"Plain casting leaves too much carbon in the iron, below the hardness standard. Proper iron is wrought iron, smelted in a special furnace called the bloomery."
	]
	quest.17DCD1E10495ABA7.quest_subtitle: "Why isn't your iron ripe?"
	quest.17DCD1E10495ABA7.title: "Cast Iron"
	quest.181DCB33CD39146A.quest_desc: [
		"Batteries charge at 24V — positive to positive, negative to negative — storing power to discharge when generation falls short."
		"Wire batteries in series and voltages add: ten 24V batteries make a 240V bank, and the charging voltage must rise accordingly."
		"Water wheels have dry seasons, windmills have calm days — battery banks are the key to a stable grid."
	]
	quest.181DCB33CD39146A.quest_subtitle: "Store power against outages"
	quest.181DCB33CD39146A.title: "Accumulators"
	quest.182E9BA1C950EDD7.quest_desc: [
		"As said before — it grinds items."
	]
	quest.182E9BA1C950EDD7.title: "Quern"
	quest.183EEF139E3C4BCC.quest_desc: [
		"The stove is Farmer's Delight's core block — all the mod's dishes are cooked on it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
	]
	quest.183EEF139E3C4BCC.quest_subtitle: "Doesn't provide much heat, though"
	quest.18653925561A463A.quest_desc: [
		"The thresher processes grain ears into grain and straw — see JEI for assembly. It yields double what knife-threshing does, with automatable input and output."
	]
	quest.18653925561A463A.quest_subtitle: "Shake shake, wobble shake"
	quest.18653925561A463A.title: "Thresher"
	quest.18F6E5DCEAF82F45.quest_desc: [
		"The clipboard works as a memo, but its real value is copying machine configurations — copy one machine's settings and paste them onto another of the same type, saving you from reconfiguring every time."
	]
	quest.18F6E5DCEAF82F45.quest_subtitle: "Today's task: hop around on machines"
	quest.19007A8B1BC8381F.quest_desc: [
		"You've forged the raw iron bloom — one final round of smithing and you'll have pig iron."
	]
	quest.19007A8B1BC8381F.quest_subtitle: "Hammer with all your might!"
	quest.190BB8C303D9BF0F.quest_desc: [
		"The &m——&rrailgun is a ranged weapon. Hold left-click to charge; release at 99 charge to fire."
		""
		"Standard ammo: iron rods, steel rods, aluminum rods and graphite electrodes, each with different damage. Special ammo with unique effects also exists. Before the railgun's monstrous damage, even the strongest mob becomes small fry."
		""
		"It stores 8000 energy and each shot consumes 800 — with such small storage, pair it with a battery backpack."
		""
		"The railgun accepts upgrades."
	]
	quest.190BB8C303D9BF0F.quest_subtitle: "Small fry~ small fry~"
	quest.190BB8C303D9BF0F.title: "&m——&rRailgun"
	quest.1920E4FABD8DC5AD.quest_desc: [
		"As mentioned, the gearbox extends shaft connections and also splits power to its other three faces. Right-click with a hammer to open ports for connections — up to four ports in two opposite pairs."
	]
	quest.1920E4FABD8DC5AD.title: "Gearbox"
	quest.1963C4D0F2C52430.quest_desc: [
		"Speed mostly affects machine efficiency. Without other devices in the way, the whole stress network shares one speed — sections meant to be slow get forced fast."
		""
		"Maximum speed is 256. Any device driven faster is destroyed instantly."
	]
	quest.1963C4D0F2C52430.title: "Rotation Speed"
	quest.19908A9AD562B70D.quest_desc: [
		"Copper leg thrusters burn compressed air for creative-style flight; press Z to toggle the inertial damper. Double efficiency in water, quadruple in space — it is, at heart, a diving thruster that changed careers."
		"Copper anchor boots give you faint gravity while standing on blocks — walk stairs normally inside a weightless station, and they double as diving boots."
		"Together they're slower than a jetpack but far cheaper — while titanium is still scarce, these are your first ticket to the sky."
		"Tip: damper on for precision docking, off for cruising. Put the anchor boots on before any spacewalk, or one careless push-off sends you drifting to nowhere."
	]
	quest.19908A9AD562B70D.quest_subtitle: "Cheap for a reason"
	quest.19908A9AD562B70D.title: "Copper Mobility Gear"
	quest.19D7E7F1F554DB6E.quest_desc: [
		"The metal above steel is black steel, which needs nickel and black bronze — four metals in all: nickel, copper, silver, gold."
	]
	quest.19D7E7F1F554DB6E.title: "Nickel Ingot"
	quest.1A3E6BE202975FF2.quest_desc: [
		"The mechanical plough only works on contraptions."
		""
		"Passing over blocks without solid collision boxes — like rails — it breaks them outright. If the contraption has a container, the drops go into it."
		""
		"The plough can also till farmland."
	]
	quest.1A3E6BE202975FF2.title: "Tilling the Land"
	quest.1A4ACE662911DA36.quest_subtitle: "Sedimentary rock near the surface"
	quest.1A4ACE662911DA36.title: "Saltpeter"
	quest.1A55D63A9A97B3C0.quest_desc: [
		"Mix lime with fresh water in a barrel to get limewater, at a ratio of 1:500 mB. Seal a hide with limewater in a barrel to get a soaked hide."
	]
	quest.1A55D63A9A97B3C0.quest_subtitle: "Ca(OH)2"
	quest.1A55D63A9A97B3C0.title: "Limewater"
	quest.1A8A48BED6032904.quest_subtitle: "Marble, limestone, phyllite, chalk, dolomite — any height, more the deeper you go"
	quest.1A8A48BED6032904.title: "Malachite"
	quest.1AA27925AD62B190.quest_desc: [
		"Extrusive igneous rock forms from lava cooling on the surface, usually at the top of an area's rock layers or on the seabed. Four types exist: rhyolite, basalt, andesite, dacite."
		""
		"Intrusive igneous rock forms from lava cooling inside the crust, usually deep underground. Three types exist: granite, diorite, gabbro."
		""
		"Sedimentary rock forms from surface matter piling up or settling — usually the topmost layer of an area. Seven types: shale, claystone, limestone, conglomerate, dolomite, chert, chalk."
		""
		"Metamorphic rock forms when the above three undergo metamorphism, usually found beneath their corresponding parent rock. Six types: quartzite, slate, phyllite, schist, gneiss, marble."
		""
		"Different rocks contain different ores — some ores only generate in specific rocks. To quickly find what you want, memorize the ore–rock relationships. Later quests also note which rocks each ore lives in."
	]
	quest.1AA27925AD62B190.title: "Geology"
	quest.1AB737C31EDC08D5.quest_desc: [
		"The crank needs steel to use and drives certain other devices. Hold a steel rod and right-click the crank to work it: power enters the crank's back and exits through the rod on its left — the driven device sits one block to the crank's left."
	]
	quest.1AB737C31EDC08D5.quest_subtitle: "Some simple mechanics"
	quest.1AE74184E202E553.quest_desc: [
		"Quests with rounded-square icons are key quests; octagonal ones are chapter finales. Key quests advance the main line, while side quests unlock side chapters. Some side chapters also need quests from other side chapters."
		""
		"Main chapters mark the stages of progression — after the Stone Age, each stage ties to a metal: copper, copper alloys, wrought iron, steel. Obtain the stage's metal and its chapter unlocks automatically; finishing the previous chapter's finale is not required."
	]
	quest.1AE74184E202E553.title: "Quest Types \\& Stages"
	quest.1AF92C46694147BF.quest_desc: [
		"Grind nixtamalized maize in a quern for masa flour — like other flours, it must be made into dough."
	]
	quest.1B05E693BBFE6443.quest_desc: [
		"The TFC–Immersive Engineering crossover adds multiblock machines. Broken by bugs back in 2.2, they are finally ready for real use."
	]
	quest.1B05E693BBFE6443.title: "TerraFirma Engineering"
	quest.1B29C064B62C5CCE.quest_desc: [
		"TerraFirma's power sources are simple: the water wheel and the windmill."
		""
		"A water wheel only spins with its lower one or two blocks dipped in a river — flowing water doesn't count, it must be a river. The more valid water, the faster it spins."
		""
		"The windmill needs a huge 13x1x13 space. Hold windmill sails and right-click a shaft to place five sails; more sails, more speed."
		""
		"Both sources can only drive 10 devices each — beyond that you need new power sources."
	]
	quest.1B29C064B62C5CCE.title: "Power Sources"
	quest.1B4770643123E26F.quest_desc: [
		"Rideable animals are horses, donkeys and mules. All three eat grains and fruit (never rotten). Mules are horse–donkey hybrids and can't breed."
		""
		"Once familiarity is high enough, add a saddle and ride. Donkeys and mules can also carry a chest."
	]
	quest.1B4770643123E26F.title: "Rideable Animals"
	quest.1B4D5C533AA2E5AF.quest_desc: [
		"Graphite generates in gneiss, marble, quartzite and schist — metamorphic rocks that usually form the second or third layer, so graphite is effectively below y=0, with low spawn rates."
		""
		"To find graphite, watch the rock layers: target areas topped with chalk, limestone, dolomite or chert."
		""
		"A non-metal prospector's pick helps you locate all non-metal minerals, graphite included."
	]
	quest.1B4D5C533AA2E5AF.title: "Prospecting Graphite"
	quest.1BEFEAB3F8B3817A.quest_desc: [
		"Tomatoes make tomato sauce and salsa."
	]
	quest.1BFBC2F00C7974E8.quest_desc: [
		"Break fruit tree leaves to get fruit leaves — only good for making drying mats."
	]
	quest.1C1BC469151DF73C.quest_desc: [
		"Water wheels and large water wheels are the cheapest stress sources, but picky about placement — final efficiency is the product of [Biome] and [Water body]:"
		""
		"[Biome] River biomes are prime: stress x1.25. Other biomes still spin, but at x0.75 speed and x0.5 stress."
		""
		"[Water body] The wheel scans for water source blocks within 64 blocks; 512 sources count as a 'large water body': speed x1.5, stress x1.25. Without one, touching a single flowing water block still works, but speed and stress drop to half (x0.5)."
		""
		"A perfectly placed small wheel (river + large water body) outputs about 1200 su; dumped by a plains puddle it makes a fraction of that. Watch the wheel with engineer's goggles to read current efficiency and the reason it's low."
		""
		"Water wheels spin fast (8 RPM) with low stress; large water wheels halve speed (4 RPM) but double stress. Covering the wheel's side or fully submerging it stops it."
	]
	quest.1C1BC469151DF73C.quest_subtitle: "The power mill"
	quest.1C1BC469151DF73C.title: "Water Wheel"
	quest.1CCF818F5DA33242.quest_desc: [
		"Open the hive, left-click to pick up the knife, hover over a comb that holds a queen and right-click to get beeswax. This removes the queen from the comb."
		""
		"Beeswax is a very useful material in many recipes."
	]
	quest.1CCF818F5DA33242.quest_subtitle: "Killing the goose that lays golden eggs"
	quest.1CFD2728D3CFCDA4.quest_desc: [
		"Kaolin's actual conversion rate is terribly low, so haul home every bit you find — at least a large chest's worth."
	]
	quest.1CFD2728D3CFCDA4.title: "Kaolin"
	quest.1D31CA89AF9F2910.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit trees differ from normal trees: no logs, only fruit. They are the most important and abundant source of fruit."
		""
		"Fruit trees demand specific annual temperatures and rainfall; a sapling in the wrong climate dies after a while."
		""
		"Each species has its own growing and fruiting season. Right-click fruiting leaves empty-handed to harvest."
	]
	quest.1D31CA89AF9F2910.title: "Fruit Trees"
	quest.1D8A3B061E9F7EA8.quest_desc: [
		"Clay molds are knapped from clay too: hold at least five clay and right-click to open the knapping interface, then chip away the extra squares to match the pattern. What you get is only an unfired mold — it must be fired in a pit kiln before it can hold molten metal."
		""
		"Recommended molds for now: pickaxe, axe, ingot, saw, chisel, prospector's pick."
		""
		"Tip: if EMI won't show how a mold is made, don't panic — the knapping recipes are attached to the UNFIRED molds, so search \\\"unfired\\\" instead. You can also check JEI, or the pottery chapter of the TFC field guide."
	]
	quest.1D8A3B061E9F7EA8.title: "More Pottery"
	quest.1D8D0D09087A335F.quest_desc: [
		"The wooden bucket works like the vanilla iron bucket except it can't hold lava — 1000 mB capacity. Unlike iron buckets, it only picks up fluid, not the source block; pouring water out makes it vanish instead of leaving a source."
	]
	quest.1DAD44FCD6E74DC0.quest_desc: [
		"TerraFirmaCraft has three damage types: piercing, slashing and crushing."
		""
		"Piercing comes from sharp things — spears, knives, arrows; spiders also pierce. Zombies resist piercing poorly, while skeletons are fully immune to it."
		""
		"Slashing comes from edged things — swords and axes; large predators also slash. Creepers are weak to slashing."
		""
		"Crushing comes from blunt things — hammers and maces. Zombie attacks crush and they resist crushing, but skeletons take extra crushing damage."
	]
	quest.1DAD44FCD6E74DC0.title: "Damage Types"
	quest.1DD8C59B7FC94A8A.quest_desc: [
		"Greenhouse crops need planters, and different planters grow different crops — the seed tooltip tells you which one it needs."
		""
		"Planters can be fertilized like farmland, but need watering every so often. Unwatered crops won't grow. Build an automatic irrigation system or water by hand with a watering can."
		""
		"Crops have preferred temperature ranges — even in a greenhouse they can be too cold or too hot. Aim at a crop to see whether the temperature suits it."
	]
	quest.1DD8C59B7FC94A8A.quest_subtitle: "Time to water every day"
	quest.1DD8C59B7FC94A8A.title: "Planters"
	quest.1DFE9CB59336AF65.quest_subtitle: "Deeper metamorphic and intrusive rock"
	quest.1DFE9CB59336AF65.title: "Chromite"
	quest.1DFF940337685C7D.quest_desc: [
		"Soaking in water lowers body temperature significantly."
	]
	quest.1DFF940337685C7D.title: "Taking a Dip"
	quest.1E66BAB348387E16.quest_desc: [
		"If meat or bones went into your compost, you get rotten compost, which kills your crops outright."
		""
		"Then again, mature crops that die of decay drop extra seeds — so it's actually useful."
	]
	quest.1E988359FD5A5E6A.quest_desc: [
		"Engineer's goggles show the working state of this mod's blocks, while the wrench easily dismantles Create blocks, rotates them, or edits machine configs."
	]
	quest.1E988359FD5A5E6A.title: "Engineer's Gear"
	quest.1E9D624342B76DEE.quest_subtitle: "Surface extrusive rock, deep intrusive rock — more at depth"
	quest.1E9D624342B76DEE.title: "Sphalerite"
	quest.1F390509695E4AA4.quest_desc: [
		"A good farmer must be a good cook, and a good cook must be a good farmer."
	]
	quest.1F390509695E4AA4.title: "&eChallenge: Master of Agriculture"
	quest.1F55F5EE7E3CA276.quest_desc: [
		"Birds only lay eggs in nest boxes, and fertilized eggs only hatch in nest boxes too."
	]
	quest.1F55F5EE7E3CA276.quest_subtitle: "Our birdie is about to lay eggs!"
	quest.1F58485DED80F718.quest_desc: [
		"A year in the TerraFirma world is 180 days — a month is 15 days, though a week is still 7. Spring runs March to May, and so on."
		"A day lasts 24 minutes, and sunrise/sunset shift with season and latitude: long summer days, long winter nights; the nearer the pole, the wilder the swing — polar summers even have midnight sun, polar winters endless night."
		"Use /time set monthlength x (x = desired days) to change month length."
	]
	quest.1F58485DED80F718.title: "Knowing the World: Calendar"
	quest.1F67CB96F0EF37A2.quest_desc: [
		"Aeronautics brings a real physics engine to TerraFirma: weight, lift, thrust, air pressure, ropes, springs... What you build is no longer a pile of blocks but a vehicle with mass that can roll — and crash."
		""
		"This chapter's route: first learn to assemble blocks into physics structures, then fit engines and controls, and finally let hot air balloons and airships carry you skyward. The rockets of the Cosmonautics chapter also start from this tech."
		""
		"As always: nearly every part in this chapter has a Ponder animation tutorial — hold W to view."
		""
		"Note: this chapter is still a work in progress. You can watch XeKr's video tutorial!"
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Bilibili tutorial\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1y8dZBVEEX/\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
	]
	quest.1F67CB96F0EF37A2.quest_subtitle: "Next up: the time when gravity fails"
	quest.1F67CB96F0EF37A2.title: "Aeronautics"
	quest.1FD35953ED9DE026.quest_desc: [
		"The hose pulley pumps and drains fluids over large areas; the direction of rotation lowers or raises the hose. The hose end's position decides where fluids are pumped or drained."
		""
		"Pumping fluid into it drains fluid out below the hose until the end's layer is filled; drawing fluid out pumps fluid in from above the hose until the end's layer is empty."
	]
	quest.1FD35953ED9DE026.quest_subtitle: "Bulk transfer"
	quest.207021C554EEE032.quest_desc: [
		"The toolbox effectively gives you 8 extra inventory slots — within its range, press Alt (default) to quick-draw items straight into your hand."
	]
	quest.207021C554EEE032.title: "Toolbox"
	quest.208B4424B11148AF.quest_desc: [
		"Mix black steel, steel, brass and rose gold in the right proportions to get weak red steel."
	]
	quest.208B4424B11148AF.quest_subtitle: "Red steel, lite edition"
	quest.20B02062076B307A.quest_desc: [
		"Used for fluid interaction with moving structures: align the moving one with a stationary one and they dock. Pipes can then draw fluid out of the moving structure."
	]
	quest.20CAEFF29E12B9CC.quest_desc: [
		"With cocoa powder and cocoa butter ratios, the mixing bowl makes three chocolate pastes:"
		"2 powder + 1 sweetener = dark chocolate"
		"2 butter + 1 sweetener = white chocolate"
		"1 powder + 1 butter + 1 sweetener = milk chocolate"
	]
	quest.20CAEFF29E12B9CC.title: "Chocolate Paste"
	quest.20E251A41A35E400.quest_desc: [
		"On a contraption, the mechanical drill can only break blocks directly ahead — but consumes no stress."
		""
		"If the contraption has a container, drops go into it."
	]
	quest.2121C8FA109E1C34.quest_desc: [
		"Blue steel requires weak blue steel first — an alloy of black steel, steel, bismuth bronze and sterling silver."
	]
	quest.2121C8FA109E1C34.title: "Sterling Silver Ingot"
	quest.2199434138EE8F2D.quest_desc: [
		"The space helmet, fed by a pressurized air supply, lets you breathe in space and underwater; the jetpack toggles with G, burns fuel for thrust, briefly defies gravity when you hold space, and doubles as an air supply for the helmet."
		"Refuel the jetpack with a bucket of biofuel (hold the bucket and Alt-click), or through a fluid spout. Our engineers assure us: using it as a helmet has received zero complaints so far."
		"The helmet's composite laminate shell also shrugs off extreme cold — neither the Moon's -50°C nor deep space's near-absolute-zero can touch you. Helmet on before you step outside."
		"Jetpack fuel bills by the second — budget before any long flight: keep margin for takeoff, hover and landing alike. A crashed pilot isn't called a pilot. They're called a meteor."
		"The space survival trinity: helmet for breathing, jetpack for moving, anchor boots for not drifting away. Check all three before opening the hatch — miss one, and don't open it."
	]
	quest.2199434138EE8F2D.quest_subtitle: "Space doesn't welcome streaking"
	quest.2199434138EE8F2D.title: "Space Suit"
	quest.1DFA57F00DCEED01.quest_desc: [
		"Low FPS? If your PC uses integrated graphics or is otherwise low-end, the steps below give the biggest improvement:"
		""
		"&e&lStep 1: Disable two mods"
		"Uncheck them in your launcher's mod manager (or rename the .jar files in the mods folder to .jar.disabled):"
		"&7- aeronautics_modernui_compat"
		"&7- ModernUI"
		"These are purely cosmetic UI mods with heavy rendering cost. After disabling, Aeronautics screens fall back to vanilla style - that's normal."
		""
		"&e&lStep 2: Video settings"
		"Set render distance to 6-8 chunks and simulation distance to 6."
		"In Sodium Extra settings: lower particle quality and entity render distance."
		""
		"&e&lStep 3: Dynamic lights"
		"Never use the \"Fancy\" preset! Set LambDynamicLights to fastest, or turn it off entirely."
		""
		"&e&lOther tips"
		"Allocate about 6 GB of RAM - more is actually worse (iGPUs share system memory)."
		"Do not use shaders. Voxy is built in and enabled by default — make sure to disable it in Video Settings."
	]
	quest.1DFA57F00DCEED01.quest_subtitle: "The secret to big FPS gains"
	quest.1DFA57F00DCEED01.title: "Low-End PC Optimization Guide"
	quest.219E58F012A1322A.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to TerraFirma: Rebirth (TFCR)!"
		"You are playing: TerraFirma Rebirth 2 · 1.0.0-release"
		""
		"&l&aThis is the Release build — stable and recommended for long-term survival. If you run into any bugs, please report them to the pack team!"
		""
		"Report bugs on our Discord:"
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Join our Discord\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://discord.gg/Fc7v5EXmkK\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
		""
		"&c&lDo NOT install ScalableLux yourself!"
		""
		"&e&lTip: If recipes appear invalid, the creative inventory search stops working, or other strange issues occur after entering a world, simply re-enter the save to fix it. If that doesn't help, restarting the game solves 99% of all bugs!"
		""
		"&8TFCR difficulty: medium-low"
		""
		"If you're new to modpacks, check the built-in questline whenever you feel lost — it also contains useful info to improve your experience. The Field Guide, the Engineer's Manual and other books walk you through each mod step by step; the MCMOD wiki has even more detailed tutorials — search 'TFCR' there to find this pack's page."
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"MCMOD Wiki\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://www.mcmod.cn\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
		""
		"&6&l☆ Sponsored by Wabbanode ☆"
		"&7Our official North America server is proudly hosted by Wabbanode."
		"Want your own server to play TFCR with friends? Use code &b&lTFCR&r for &a20% OFF&r any hosting plan:"
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"wabbanode.com/affiliate/terrafirmarebirth\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://wabbanode.com/affiliate/terrafirmarebirth\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
	]
	quest.219E58F012A1322A.quest_subtitle: "Author: ZJWEU Minecraft Club"
	quest.219E58F012A1322A.title: "Must Read!"
	quest.21B43782428F07D8.quest_desc: [
		"Soybeans are a food with special recipes — they can be pressed for oil and made into tofu."
	]
	quest.21B6C2F8ECC10BF3.quest_desc: [
		"The depot mainly assists other machines and stores one batch of items — any number of items inserted at once."
		""
		"All six faces are input/output faces, and it accepts dropped items too, but won't take anything new until its current batch leaves."
	]
	quest.21F33563EF259066.quest_desc: [
		"The metal press makes Immersive Engineering's parts, shaping materials into sheets, rods, wires and metal blocks. It pairs with IE conveyor belts, holds 16 kFE, takes power from the top, and has redstone control below — right-click the redstone control block with the engineer's screwdriver to reverse the belt direction."
	]
	quest.21F33563EF259066.title: "Pressing Metal"
	quest.220E00DDC712BD11.quest_desc: [
		"The waterskin works with the boiler and the fridge, and must be filled with water first."
		""
		"Placed in the boiler's or fridge's slot, it gradually consumes their fuel or refrigerant until it reaches a set temperature."
		""
		"Take it out and it holds that temperature until you use it."
		""
		"Two ways to use it: right-click to apply it directly — instantly changing your temperature and emptying the water; or hold it in main/off hand, where it slowly shifts your temperature while returning to normal — without emptying."
	]
	quest.220E00DDC712BD11.quest_subtitle: "Warm in summer, cool in winter — reversed"
	quest.224F7F841626C5E1.quest_desc: [
		"The Iron Age's final goal is steelmaking. To make steel you need lots of wrought iron plus two rare resources: graphite and kaolin. Use the new gear from the Iron Age — trek across the tropics, or dive into the Nether and build Create production lines — and finally build the steel blast furnace and make steel."
	]
	quest.224F7F841626C5E1.quest_subtitle: "A long journey ahead"
	quest.224F7F841626C5E1.title: "Chapter V — Chapter Goal"
	quest.23024DC07BA44C91.quest_desc: [
		"Most smithing recipes in TerraFirmaCraft use metal that must be heated to workable temperature or above."
		""
		"Most metals can be forged on a tier-I anvil — the copper anvil; some need anvils of higher-tier metals."
		""
		"Put the heated metal on the anvil, make sure a hammer is in there, and complete both smithing goals before it cools too far."
		""
		"When forging metal tools, fewer steps mean higher quality: crude, common, fine, perfect. Higher quality means more durability and faster work. Forged tools generally outperform cast ones."
	]
	quest.23024DC07BA44C91.title: "Smithing Guide: Advanced"
	quest.2323C0FFE654EBC9.quest_desc: [
		"The other thing the blast furnace needs is the tuyere — the furnace only works with a tuyere placed inside the blast furnace block."
	]
	quest.237003BA6B1A4983.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a gem with a magnifying glass and sandpaper to get a cut gem."
	]
	quest.237003BA6B1A4983.quest_subtitle: "If only someone in this world would trade you for it..."
	quest.237003BA6B1A4983.title: "Cut Gems"
	quest.2422EF40DDF3F28F.quest_desc: [
		"Compost is an all-round fertilizer. To make it you need a composter, which holds up to 16 units of 'green items' and 16 units of 'brown items'."
		""
		"Once full it starts working — but note that adjacent composters interfere and lower efficiency."
		""
		"Among greens, fruits and vegetables count most; among browns, pumpkins, melons and withered grass count most. Check the guide book for exact kinds."
	]
	quest.2422EF40DDF3F28F.quest_subtitle: "TerraFirma folk don't use toilets"
	quest.2422EF40DDF3F28F.title: "Composter"
	quest.24B6EF9798DD901F.quest_desc: [
		"The mechanical roller only works on contraptions, digging blocks at its own height and one below."
		""
		"It has multiple terrain-filling modes: replace surface blocks to level land, and fill gaps under roads and terrain for bridge foundations."
	]
	quest.24B6EF9798DD901F.quest_subtitle: "It's a Road Roller!"
	quest.24B6EF9798DD901F.title: "Road Roller"
	quest.2523764808A716D2.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit pie and pumpkin pie share nearly the same recipe: besides flour and sugar, the former needs butter and jam, the latter pumpkin and eggs."
		""
		"You also need to smith a baking tray from a cast iron sheet before baking them in an oven."
	]
	quest.2544550FCC093678.quest_desc: [
		"To fit TerraFirmaCraft's weight system, its native storage blocks are very limited: small capacity, and oversized items don't fit. Fine for the early game only."
	]
	quest.2544550FCC093678.title: "TFC's Native Storage Blocks"
	quest.258B0BB6F1CA1F1B.title: "Placeholder Quest (not yet written)"
	quest.25E42DD7011EAE24.quest_desc: [
		"The redstone requester must first be linked to the storage network. When triggered by redstone, it asks the network to send the configured items to a specific address."
	]
	quest.2643DF4CC466346D.quest_desc: [
		"If the fluid body at the hose end exceeds 10,000 blocks (configurable), it counts as an 'infinite fluid', like the Nether's lava sea. Aiming at the hose pulley then shows 'Infinite Supply'."
		""
		"If you fill ten thousand blocks of lava yourself, note that 9,900 blocks sometimes also shows 'Infinite Supply' while pumping still drains it — best to double-check."
	]
	quest.2643DF4CC466346D.quest_subtitle: "One TerraFirma underground lava lake is enough"
	quest.2643DF4CC466346D.title: "Infinite Lava"
	quest.269CABDFE57142E2.quest_desc: [
		"A liquid rocket engine is modular: engine mount, cycle plumbing and nozzle stack three blocks along the axis. Wrench to switch cycles — closed, open, full-flow, expander — each trading thrust against efficiency."
		"Propellant is pumped continuously: 1000mB each in the fuel and oxidizer tanks, and both water and air work as oxidizer. Thrust scales with pump RPM; the thrust gauge shows live readings."
		"Copper nozzles overheat at high thrust; titanium alloy nozzles don't. Reference figures: closed-cycle copper 10000N, open-cycle titanium 20800N, full-flow titanium 26000N. Engineer's goggles read engine parameters directly."
		"The engine stores no fuel itself. Pre-ignition checklist: fuel tank full? Oxidizer tank full? Pump powered?"
		"Hook it to a CC computer and the engine is fully programmable: setThrust, setGimbal, getFluidAmount — your automated orbit program starts right here."
		"Warning: the exhaust plume is extremely hot. Do not stand under the engine at ignition — under any meaning of the word."
	]
	quest.269CABDFE57142E2.quest_subtitle: "Final check before ignition"
	quest.269CABDFE57142E2.title: "Rocket Engine"
	quest.26BC95484D4DDCEF.quest_desc: [
		"An elytra alternative with nearly the same glide performance, but very low durability and no enchanting. Repairable, yet it can't take high speeds — diving fast or using fireworks wears it out much faster."
	]
	quest.26BC95484D4DDCEF.quest_subtitle: "Budget elytra"
	quest.26D1B97DFE73847E.quest_desc: [
		"The mechanical arm takes and places items from almost any Create container — even through walls."
		""
		"Set its input and output before placing. Powered, it telekinetically takes items from the input and puts them in the output, respecting container filters."
		""
		"Use the config panel on its base to change how it picks and places."
	]
	quest.26D1B97DFE73847E.quest_subtitle: "The clever arm"
	quest.26DEEFF8A5942B26.quest_desc: [
		"Grains honestly need little processing — just remember to craft grain ears with a knife into grain. Raw grain stores for a long time as-is."
	]
	quest.26DEEFF8A5942B26.title: "Grains"
	quest.26E91EAA9E4DB9EF.quest_desc: [
		"Craft bone meal, dirt and tree bark into organic fertilizer; place it beside water and after a while it becomes rich soil."
		""
		"Rich soil is special dirt that speeds up plants growing on it. TFC saplings planted on it follow vanilla growth logic, shrinking months of growth into days."
		""
		"It doesn't play well with anything but saplings, though — weird bugs happen — so only use it for trees."
	]
	quest.26E91EAA9E4DB9EF.quest_subtitle: "Nothing to do with manure"
	quest.26F1F343873FDBD3.quest_desc: [
		"Machines that work by consuming stress — used well, they cover most of your recipe needs."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the 'Power Machinery' side chapter."
	]
	quest.26F1F343873FDBD3.title: "Power Machinery"
	quest.2703BCA3E265C338.quest_desc: [
		"Drawers store huge amounts of one item type — up to 32 stacks each, with the front slots deciding how many types it holds."
		""
		"Drawers accept many upgrades granting extra functions."
		""
		"Special variants exist: fluid drawers for fluids, compacting drawers that show both compressed and uncompressed forms, and ender drawers that bind to each other."
	]
	quest.2703BCA3E265C338.title: "Drawers"
	quest.27042E3F6BBBCAD8.quest_desc: [
		"Pure titanium isn't good enough for rockets. Titanium alloy is 3 titanium ingots plus 1 netherite ingot, mixed under superheat — in this pack netherite is arc-furnace smelted from red steel, blue steel and nether wart, with byproduct from the Mining Magnate achievement and ancient debris drills."
		"Mixing requires a superheated blaze burner, which means blaze cakes. RPM and stress are not the bottleneck — cakes are. Set up a cake production line early; future you will be grateful."
		"Titanium alloy's strength and heat resistance make it the mandated material for engine nozzles and load-bearing parts — copper nozzles overheat at high thrust, titanium alloy ones don't. And roll your titanium into plates while you're at it; the hull needs them."
	]
	quest.27042E3F6BBBCAD8.quest_subtitle: "Top-tier metal"
	quest.27042E3F6BBBCAD8.title: "Titanium Alloy"
	quest.273C77FEE01501F3.quest_desc: [
		"When the bloomery finishes, its melt becomes a raw iron bloom — one per 100 mB of iron in the input, fractions discarded. Mine it out with a pickaxe, then take it to your copper-alloy anvil for two more rounds of smithing: first into a refined iron bloom, then into a wrought iron ingot."
	]
	quest.273C77FEE01501F3.quest_subtitle: "Hammer the carbon out"
	quest.276F1852697AE589.quest_desc: [
		"Brass is a copper alloy of 88%-92% copper and 8%-12% zinc. Unlike the three copper alloys before it, it is only used for machines."
		""
		"TerraFirmaCraft recipes mostly use brass rods and brass mechanisms, while Create uses brass ingots directly."
	]
	quest.276F1852697AE589.quest_subtitle: "Another copper alloy"
	quest.277349DD2693B7CA.quest_desc: [
		"Immersive Engineering machines mostly come as multiblock structures: build the structure as shown in the Engineer's Manual, then right-click a specific block with the engineer's hammer to form the machine."
	]
	quest.277349DD2693B7CA.title: "Immersive Engineering: Multiblocks"
	quest.27AD50F2899C636A.quest_desc: [
		"Nearly all of Create's fluid devices need copper."
	]
	quest.27AD50F2899C636A.title: "Fluid Transport"
	quest.27E7D972AE5F15B2.quest_desc: [
		"Heat a blowpipe holding glass to at least faint red, then hold right-click on the bottom of a casting basin before it cools — glass fills the whole basin. Once cooled, harvest it with a gem saw. Craft the blowpipe with certain powders beforehand for stained glass. Glass panes are poured in the center of a casting table."
		""
		"Blowing glass items is more complex than blocks and panes; there are too many kinds to list here — check the book and JEI as needed."
	]
	quest.27E7D972AE5F15B2.quest_subtitle: "Crystal clear"
	quest.2828BD31C3610C8A.quest_desc: [
		"Powered mechanical crafters perform automatic shaped crafting."
		""
		"Build a wall of crafters, and make sure the path formed by their arrows ends at a single crafter on the edge. Insert items by right-click or logistics; when the crafter fills up, or a redstone signal fires, crafting begins."
		""
		"If the layout matches a recipe, the product exits the final crafter. Otherwise crafting fails and everything spills out as drops."
		""
		"Use a wrench on a crafter's back to link adjacent crafters, making them accept the same items together."
		""
		"Some recipes are mechanical-crafting-only and usually need a wall bigger than 3x3."
	]
	quest.288B45ED152DEEB8.quest_desc: [
		"Many TerraFirmaCraft recipes need animal drops, so you'll hunt often."
		""
		"Careful: some herbivores fight back, and most carnivores attack first. Protect yourself while hunting."
	]
	quest.288B45ED152DEEB8.title: "Hunting Animals"
	quest.28E17A2BBCF31633.quest_desc: [
		"The crane borer turns the glued area in front of it into a contraption and moves with it. It must be placed on a crane rod and can only travel along the rod."
		""
		"A crane-driven contraption stops when blocked by a block."
		""
		"Cranes can be chained — see the Ponder scene for usage."
	]
	quest.2949C7D752F14BA5.quest_desc: [
		"Greenhouse irrigation is driven by the pump station. Find water near the greenhouse, mount the pump station above it and hook up power — it is now a true fluid container with 500 mB storage; each irrigation tank stacked above adds 500 mB (up to 3), fill rate scales with speed, and fluid pipes work too."
		""
		"Sprinklers no longer spray forever — each spray consumes 5 mB of stored water. Whether water arrives depends on pump pressure: pressure = pump height + tank count + speed − sprinkler height; zero or above means it works. Even unpowered, height difference plus tank water can barely supply it."
		""
		"Copper pipes run at most 32 blocks. Replacing one greenhouse wall with the connector keeps the seal even with pipes passing through a wall-embedded irrigation tank — it's a natural wall-penetrating port and doubles as greenhouse wall."
		""
		"Finally, place sprinklers above or below any pipe. A downward sprinkler covers a 5x5x6 area centered one block below it; an upward one is the reverse."
	]
	quest.2949C7D752F14BA5.quest_subtitle: "No more daily watering"
	quest.2949C7D752F14BA5.title: "Automatic Irrigation"
	quest.2968899F318BFF88.quest_desc: [
		"In vanilla TerraFirmaCraft, the Nether is unreachable except by commands — but with an addon, entry becomes possible. With wrought iron in hand, you're ready to brave the Nether. Confirm to unlock 'The Beneath' side chapter."
	]
	quest.2968899F318BFF88.quest_subtitle: "Why explore the Nether? Because it's there"
	quest.2968899F318BFF88.title: "The Beneath"
	quest.29868E685B95DCE5.quest_desc: [
		"Lime is a core material for building blocks — besides mortar, concrete also needs it."
	]
	quest.29868E685B95DCE5.quest_subtitle: "CaO"
	quest.29A4B21CB648052D.quest_desc: [
		"A stage separator is a redstone-pulse-triggered explosive bolt: boosters burnt out, lower stage dry — one signal, bang, dead weight drops away and the rocket flies light."
		"The charge-loaded variant separates cleaner; the shaft-driven variant passes rotation across stages, letting the upper engine borrow the power delivered from below."
		"Wiring the signal to a button is the easy mode; wiring it to a CC computer lets you stage by altitude, by velocity, by fuel margin — the latter is how multi-stage rockets are truly meant to fly."
		"The art of staging is to never feel sorry when it's time to let go."
	]
	quest.29A4B21CB648052D.quest_subtitle: "Drop the baggage"
	quest.29A4B21CB648052D.title: "Stage Separation"
	quest.29B14AB2FFDAE7FC.quest_desc: [
		"Once the catenary (or third rail) is powered and the train is fitted with a pantograph (or contact shoe) and electric motors, your steam locomotive officially retires."
		"Lay a stretch of electrified railway and let the train run — this is the graduation ceremony of the Electrical Engineering chapter."
	]
	quest.29B14AB2FFDAE7FC.quest_subtitle: "Woo— clackety-clack"
	quest.29B14AB2FFDAE7FC.title: "Electric Trains"
	quest.29CA2AC0C401C889.quest_desc: [
		"Bushes are the third source of fruit besides fruit trees and farming. Collect wild bushes with a knife and bring them home."
		""
		"Unlike fruit trees, bushes only care about local temperature, drawing moisture from nearby water source blocks."
		""
		"Given space, bushes try to spread; each kind has its own growing and fruiting season. Right-click fruiting bushes empty-handed to harvest."
	]
	quest.29CA2AC0C401C889.quest_subtitle: "Watch for ambushes"
	quest.29CA2AC0C401C889.title: "Bushes"
	quest.2A25AFA7C429656D.quest_desc: [
		"First, roast the cocoa beans in an oven."
	]
	quest.2A6AA37EBBE50925.quest_desc: [
		"The most basic heat source — only low-temperature fuels. It works with a bellows, but the cost-efficiency is poor. Luckily, nothing that needs a campfire asks for high temperatures."
	]
	quest.2A6AA37EBBE50925.title: "Campfire"
	quest.2A840AC056888886.quest_desc: [
		"You can drive a train manually, but trains can also run automatically."
		""
		"Prepare a train schedule listing what the train does per loop. The train follows the shortest route through the schedule; if any stop is unreachable, it won't run at all."
		""
		"Once the schedule is set, give it to the driver — an animal leashed to a seat one block in front of the controls, or a blaze burner. With schedule in hand, the driver drives itself."
		""
		"If you store fuel in the train's storage blocks at departure, the train runs faster."
	]
	quest.2A840AC056888886.quest_subtitle: "The enslaved blaze is still being exploited"
	quest.2A840AC056888886.title: "Running Trains"
	quest.2A8A8C83490EFD87.quest_desc: [
		"The wooden storage crate is Immersive Engineering's storage block, requiring creosote to craft. Like a shulker box, it holds a chest's worth and keeps its contents when broken."
	]
	quest.2AAA5BC1B8F2C8C9.quest_desc: [
		"Hold rope and right-click a winch or rope connector to tie two physics structures together — a balloon carrying its basket, an airship towing a cargo hold, all rely on this."
		"Feed rotation into the winch to reel the rope in or out; right-click the rope with a wrench to slide down it, and shears cut it."
	]
	quest.2AAA5BC1B8F2C8C9.quest_subtitle: "Kite flying starts from childhood"
	quest.2AAA5BC1B8F2C8C9.title: "Ropes \\& Winches"
	quest.2ADA31FF3CDC6B85.quest_desc: [
		"Opposite faces of a cross gearbox spin in opposite directions — naturally useful for reversing rotation."
	]
	quest.2ADA31FF3CDC6B85.title: "Gearbox Reversal"
	quest.2B6C10EBEFAC8A8E.quest_desc: [
		"Powered, the encased fan creates airflow whose direction depends on the rotation. The flow passes through non-full blocks, pushing or pulling entities."
		""
		"Passing over certain blocks transforms the airflow, letting it process dropped items or items on depots and belts by recipe — over water, for instance, it batch-washes ores in place of the sluice. See JEI."
		""
		"Fun fact: items under multiple airflows process proportionally faster. Try an empty blaze burner with fans above and below."
	]
	quest.2B6C10EBEFAC8A8E.title: "A Stronger Wind Blows"
	quest.2B91688E20CE8A18.quest_desc: [
		"The portable storage interface enables contraption logistics."
		""
		"Place one on a contraption; when it sits face to face one block apart from a stationary interface, they dock — letting you push or pull items between them. The contraption needs a storage block, of course."
		""
		"The portable fluid interface works the same way, but fluids need pipes."
	]
	quest.2B91688E20CE8A18.title: "Contraption Logistics"
	quest.2B949E68DF47E3C1.quest_desc: [
		"The mining drill is a handheld digging tool, far more efficient than TFC tools. It needs a drill head installed and biodiesel as fuel."
		""
		"Drill heads have three tiers: iron digs 2x2, steel and black steel dig 3x3, blue and red steel dig 5x5."
		""
		"Three different upgrade modules grant it stronger abilities."
		""
		"Each block mined consumes 1 mB of fuel. Refuel at the refinery or a barrel of biodiesel — refueling from a barrel requires the drill to be empty."
	]
	quest.2B949E68DF47E3C1.quest_subtitle: "Who do you think I am!!"
	quest.2B949E68DF47E3C1.title: "Pierce the Heavens"
	quest.2BB6A4E867BC5097.quest_desc: [
		"The table cloth decorates, or sets up a shop. As decoration it displays up to 4 items."
		""
		"As a shop: hold the cloth and right-click a stockkeeper, choosing an item from storage to sell (remember to set an address). Then place the cloth and set the price on its front (lock the logistics network in the stockkeeper when selling)."
		""
		"To buy, right-click the cloth for a purchase list; further clicks on the cloth add items to the list."
		""
		"Hold the list and right-click the shopkeeper to check out — payment items are taken from your inventory, and the telegraph fires one signal requesting the goods."
		""
		"Customers' payments are stored in the stock telegraph."
	]
	quest.2BB6A4E867BC5097.title: "Table Cloth"
	quest.2BD6562746D0B990.quest_desc: [
		"Poultry are chickens, ducks and quail. They eat fruit, vegetables, grains and seeds — only ducks refuse rotten food."
		""
		"They do one thing: lay eggs. Only mated poultry lay fertilized eggs, but any egg works as an ingredient."
	]
	quest.2BD6562746D0B990.title: "Poultry"
	quest.2BFB2821B55B2EDE.quest_desc: [
		"The andesite casing crafts into most basic machines: hold andesite alloy and right-click a stripped log — any wood species works. A wrench dismantles it quickly."
	]
	quest.2BFB2821B55B2EDE.quest_subtitle: "Simple machines forming Create's production lines"
	quest.2BFB2821B55B2EDE.title: "Machine Basics"
	quest.2C8CA898AC4C8DFE.quest_desc: [
		"There are two starter routes to andesite alloy. The handcraft route: split a wrought iron ingot into nine nuggets, then craft 4 iron nuggets, 4 loose andesite and 1 quartz into 2 andesite alloy — easy but iron-hungry."
		""
		"The metal-free route: grind loose extrusive rock (andesite, basalt, dacite, rhyolite all work) in a quern into igneous powder, heat it molten, then in a small vessel or crucible blend 95%~98% molten igneous rock with 2%~5% molten cast iron to get molten andesite alloy, and cast it into ingots. Stone is free, great for mass production — but note the ingot mold has roughly a one-in-ten chance of cracking per cast, so keep spares."
		""
		"Once you have a mixer, mass production begins: toss in loose andesite and metal nuggets and stir. Nuggets come from splitting wrought iron or zinc ingots nine-to-one. Given how much wrought iron is in demand, zinc is recommended."
	]
	quest.2C8CA898AC4C8DFE.title: "Andesite Alloy"
	quest.2C90232F314ABFDC.quest_desc: [
		"Next, add lime to the filtered cane juice to alkalize it."
	]
	quest.2C90232F314ABFDC.quest_subtitle: "Adding the clarifier"
	quest.2C90232F314ABFDC.title: "Alkalizing"
	quest.2CF285001286EB5B.quest_desc: [
		"Some Create machines can work on contraptions — they lose recipe execution and keep only world interaction. Others ONLY work on contraptions, with similar functionality."
		""
		"Contraption-mounted machines need no stress and work automatically; their speed depends on the contraption's movement. If the contraption has a container, broken blocks go straight into it."
	]
	quest.2CF285001286EB5B.title: "Machines on Contraptions"
	quest.2D12A78196D788A3.quest_desc: [
		"With string you can make a bow — remember to stock up on arrows too."
	]
	quest.2D12A78196D788A3.quest_subtitle: "Piercing damage, so don't use it on skeletons"
	quest.2D12A78196D788A3.title: "Bow \\& Arrows"
	quest.2D159EE393AECF97.quest_desc: [
		"To open a Nether portal, prepare seven offerings: skeleton skulls; anvils; ingot piles holding gold, pig iron or black steel (one ingot in the pile is enough); or black-steel-plated or gold-plated blocks. You don't need every kind — any seven offerings will do."
		""
		"Lay the offerings together (as blocks). Lead a pig, sheep or goat over and kill it with a scythe within five blocks of the offerings. Amid thunder and lightning, the Nether portal appears where the offerings were."
		""
		"Opening the portal causes an explosion that destroys everything in a large area — keep it far from your home."
	]
	quest.2D159EE393AECF97.quest_subtitle: "Offer sacrifices to the demons to open the gate to their realm"
	quest.2D159EE393AECF97.title: "To the Nether"
	quest.2D6453B208327031.quest_desc: [
		"The most basic fuel — feeds campfires and ovens, and can be processed further for better burning."
	]
	quest.2D6453B208327031.title: "Logs"
	quest.2D68D0EECF694474.quest_desc: [
		"Honey glue is the physics-structure-specific adhesive, made by pouring honey onto an iron sheet. Right-click two endpoints to create a glue zone, hold Ctrl and scroll to expand it, hold Alt to place endpoints mid-air."
		""
		"Unlike super glue, honey glue only sticks to physics structures and won't accidentally catch Create contraptions. For complex vehicles, use both glues together."
	]
	quest.2D68D0EECF694474.quest_subtitle: "Glue down your ambition"
	quest.2D68D0EECF694474.title: "Honey Glue"
	quest.2D7441C2B65BA37F.quest_desc: [
		"Seal lumber in a barrel of creosote for 8 minutes to get treated lumber; 4 treated lumber craft into treated planks. Each lumber consumes 50 mB of creosote."
	]
	quest.2D90F91942AE919A.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a clay pot onto a campfire to place it. A campfire turned cooking pot loses its roasting function, so build a second campfire."
		""
		"The pot boils up to five foods into a soup with its own shelf life, and nutrition equal to 75% of all ingredients combined. Soup consumes one jug of water; once the water boils for a while, the soup is done — ladle it out with a bowl."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the 'Chef's Guide' chapter."
	]
	quest.2D90F91942AE919A.quest_subtitle: "Some basic cooking"
	quest.2E714780F701D299.quest_desc: [
		"Note: the 'cilantro' in recipes is actually a kind of herb."
	]
	quest.2ECCA5AE179FFA0C.quest_desc: [
		"Soul soil can now be hoed into soul farmland, on which Nether crops grow. Unlike the overworld, the Nether has five nutrients: death, destruction, flame, decay and sorrow. A crop favoring one nutrient doesn't consume it — it consumes the others to raise that one. Fertilize with sulfur, gunpowder and the like, or find nutrient fertilizers in loot chests."
		""
		"In the current version, only three Nether crops are harvestable: ghost pepper (a vegetable), glimmerflower (a light source) and nether wart (for brewing). Two more — crimson and warped roots — can't be harvested and instead shift soil nutrients."
		""
		"You can also grow mushrooms in the Nether: place a fertilizing block near them and fill it with mushrooms, ghast tears or Nether crops, and mushrooms will sprout nearby."
	]
	quest.2ECCA5AE179FFA0C.title: "Nether Plants"
	quest.2EFC30C54F4F811C.quest_desc: [
		"Certain chunks in the world hold virtual ore veins with enormous reserves. The mineral drill mines these veins, and it eats a massive amount of stress."
		""
		"Use the prospecting rod to locate a deposit, place the drill in that chunk, and feed it stress and water. After a while, ore appears at the output. Place multiple drills for more efficiency."
	]
	quest.2EFC30C54F4F811C.title: "What Is a Collapse?"
	quest.2F2D53888136A19E.quest_desc: [
		"The engineer's workbench makes press molds, bullets and electronic components. It needs blueprints, which you craft yourself; different blueprints show different craftables on the right."
		""
		"The engineer's workbench differs from a crafting table only in having some storage."
	]
	quest.2F4813E06F69E1A2.quest_desc: [
		"Food stored in vessels gains a storage buff doubling its shelf life — note the large vessel must be sealed."
		""
		"Don't put food in regular storage blocks like chests."
	]
	quest.2F4813E06F69E1A2.title: "Vessels Big \\& Small"
	quest.2F5F3B7D868CD534.quest_desc: [
		"Nether ore generation is reworked to match the overworld: concentrated veins. Six minerals generate in the Nether: gold, pyrite, sylvite, slime, nether quartz and cursed coal."
		""
		"Two new minerals: slime, used in the sacrifice ritual, and cursed coal, used to build the key structure — the Nether forge."
		""
		"Sulfur also generates directly on the Nether floor and can be shoveled up — but iron and steel shovels cause a huge explosion the instant they touch sulfur."
		""
		"Sadly, netherite can't be mined or looted — but there is one way: find an ancient debris vein with the prospecting rod in the Nether, then set up a Create mineral drill to pump it dry."
	]
	quest.2F5F3B7D868CD534.title: "Nether Minerals"
	quest.2FD8C89C38B920CE.quest_desc: [
		"The chisel works rock-type items: craft it with loose stone or gypsum to make bricks, or carve natural stone blocks into smooth ones."
	]
	quest.2FD8C89C38B920CE.quest_subtitle: "When each of us carves stone, raises columns, cuts stained glass, we know we are building something far bigger than ourselves. — Adrienne Clarkson"
	quest.2FD8C89C38B920CE.title: "Copper Chisel"
	quest.3008DEA61A7B9C65.quest_desc: [
		"The programmable gearbox is used to precisely control contraptions. Right-click it to program its transmission logic; a redstone pulse then runs the preset program once."
	]
	quest.3008DEA61A7B9C65.title: "Programmed Transmission"
	quest.3010455F84F0E7AA.quest_desc: [
		"The energy meter counts total power flowing through: positive to the input terminal, load terminal to the appliance, return to the neutral terminal — don't mix up the three."
		"The frequency meter watches grid frequency stability. When generator speed wobbles, it's the first to tell you."
	]
	quest.3010455F84F0E7AA.quest_subtitle: "The grid's dashboard"
	quest.3010455F84F0E7AA.title: "Energy \\& Frequency Meters"
	quest.308C74C2017D7D52.quest_desc: [
		"Sadly, TerraFirmaCraft offers no way to reach the End, but the Nether portal can still be opened through a special ritual, detailed in later quests."
		""
		"Create: Cosmonautics lets players enter outer space by sitting in a seat on a physicalized vehicle and ascending past y=20000. In the current version, only the Moon is reachable. &8PS: this content is best experienced in creative mode; survival support is incomplete."
	]
	quest.308C74C2017D7D52.title: "Other Dimensions"
	quest.3134942B4B939CA6.quest_desc: [
		"The stock telegraph lets players remotely retrieve items from the storage network."
		""
		"Hold it and right-click a stock link to connect to its network. Once placed, it needs a seat with a sitting creature or a blaze burner nearby as the stockkeeper."
		""
		"Browse the network's contents at the stockkeeper and order items delivered to a chosen address."
		""
		"Filters can be placed on the stock telegraph to categorize the stockkeeper's listing for easier browsing."
	]
	quest.3148DC2DBA3849AE.quest_subtitle: "Only in 'veins', only in gabbro"
	quest.3148DC2DBA3849AE.title: "Kimberlite"
	quest.314A4FFC942A2557.quest_desc: [
		"Right when the pit kiln finishes burning, its contents are at &ebrilliant white****&f and the copper in your vessel is molten. Let it cool to &6orange****&f and the copper solidifies — you'd have to reheat it."
		""
		"So the right move: the moment the pit kiln finishes, grab the vessel, open it, and put in molds until full."
	]
	quest.314A4FFC942A2557.title: "Casting"
	quest.31854FA6B7ED3C26.quest_desc: [
		"Given tool durability, the stone knife is the recommended first stone tool. Craft a stick or branch with a knife blade to make one."
	]
	quest.31854FA6B7ED3C26.title: "Stone Knife Blade"
	quest.31C6A79A45DC491E.quest_desc: [
		"Packages come from the packager and hold up to nine stacks inside."
		""
		"Packages behave like normal items in transport. The packager and the mechanical saw can unpack them."
		""
		"A package sealed by a packager with an address carries that address, readable by package filters and other devices."
	]
	quest.31C6A79A45DC491E.title: "Packages"
	quest.31DC9CC3F6C92B9A.quest_desc: [
		"The campfire is a vital early-game block: lighting, warmth, cooking, and making torches."
		""
		"Drop one log and three sticks with Q into the same spot, then hold right-click with a firestarter on the top of the block beneath the drops. Sometimes you must keep holding right-click until the campfire finally lights."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the 'Heating \\& Fuel' side chapter."
		""
		"Warning: never place a campfire near hay or wooden blocks — its heat may set them alight!"
	]
	quest.31DC9CC3F6C92B9A.quest_subtitle: "Fire... warm fire"
	quest.31DC9CC3F6C92B9A.title: "&eBONEFIRE LIT"
	quest.3216401F1B6C669A.quest_desc: [
		"Steel is the material foundation of Immersive Engineering's advanced industry — without steel, no IE multiblock machines."
	]
	quest.322DA724CB100A09.quest_desc: [
		"With no aids and only your feet, traveling is hard, because grass slows you down."
		""
		"Running through grass or snow forcibly slows you — slower than walking. So you need help from something else."
	]
	quest.322DA724CB100A09.title: "By Land"
	quest.3234CA6489B308BF.quest_desc: [
		"It all starts with wire. Copper wire is the grid's blood vessel and must be laid with a spool: hold the spool, right-click one connector, then another — a wire is strung. To remove it, right-click with an empty spool."
		""
		"Insulated wire is safer and can be dyed to mark circuits; bare wire is cheaper, but touch it and you'll learn what 'tingly' means."
		""
		"Every wire has a max current — overload it and it burns out. For high-power grids, use thicker wire, or do as in real life: raise the voltage, lower the current."
	]
	quest.3234CA6489B308BF.quest_subtitle: "Highways for electricity"
	quest.3234CA6489B308BF.title: "Wires \\& Spools"
	quest.3270EADED45FCD0F.quest_desc: [
		"Step three: put ore chunks into the quern and grind them into dirty dust. The quern takes input from its sides and outputs below. Try wooden funnels for automation."
		""
		"At the copper stage you can already use Create-in-TFC power — that is, automating the quern. Completing this quest unlocks that side chapter."
	]
	quest.3270EADED45FCD0F.title: "Grind Once"
	quest.32778D39E6113B91.quest_desc: [
		"The factory gauge must first be linked to the storage network. It watches the count of a chosen item in the network and sends a signal to ship more to an address when it runs low."
		""
		"Stuck on a packager, it watches the chosen item in the packager's connected container and fires when below the set count."
		""
		"Not on a packager, it watches the whole network. Multiple factory gauges can then compose a recipe: when the set item runs low, materials are sent to an address. The recipe can even be a mechanical crafter's shaped recipe."
	]
	quest.32972ACE7076CD4F.quest_desc: [
		"The windmill bearing treats the glued area in front of it as a windmill and spins it, provided the area meets windmill requirements. Once spinning, the bearing becomes a stress source."
		""
		"See the 'Stress \\& Transmission' chapter for application."
	]
	quest.32CCA4DFDD85BD46.quest_subtitle: "Metamorphic or intrusive rock near lava"
	quest.32CCA4DFDD85BD46.title: "Sulfur"
	quest.32DDD057F12B1AC5.quest_desc: [
		"After a while of normal operation, molten pig iron appears in the blast furnace block; with a crucible below, it flows into the crucible. The iron solidifies when too cool, so you still need a charcoal forge heating the crucible."
		""
		"A pig iron ingot is like the bloomery's raw iron bloom — it needs two rounds of smithing to become steel."
	]
	quest.33318AF7E086B8E3.quest_desc: [
		"The packager must be connected to a container. It records the container's contents and reports them to the stock link."
		""
		"Once connected, a redstone signal or a signal from the stock link makes it package items — up to nine stacks at a time."
		""
		"A sign placed near the packager gives it an address: whatever is written becomes the address carried by its packages for other devices to read."
	]
	quest.3334A1823AF502AF.quest_desc: [
		"Xaero's minimap etc.: if JourneyMap (bundled, with TFC integration) doesn't suit you, swap in whichever map mod you prefer."
		"&8Please also delete/disable:"
		"&8jmi-neoforge-1.21.1-1.9.jar"
		"&8journeymaptfcintegration-neoforge-1.0.3.jar"
		"&8journeymap-neoforge-1.21.1-6.0.3.jar"
		""
		"Carry On: built in since this version — Shift+right-click to carry chests, livestock and more. Carrying hostile or aggressive creatures, Create/Aeronautics/Immersive Engineering blocks, and any multiblock structure is disabled."
		""
		"OptiFine: strongly discouraged — for any modern-version pack, really. This pack already ships shader support."
		""
		"X-ray: fine in singleplayer, but please don't add it when playing on others' servers."
		""
		"You are responsible for any dependency or compatibility issues caused by mods you add yourself."
	]
	quest.3334A1823AF502AF.title: "Mods You May Add at Your Discretion"
	quest.334C1658B421E704.quest_subtitle: "Metamorphic rock at any height — more the deeper you go"
	quest.334C1658B421E704.title: "Tetrahedrite"
	quest.3384B5B44F4B831F.quest_desc: [
		"To make wine, grapes must first be crushed in the stomping basin. Put grapes in and jump on them 16 times to get crushed grapes, then seal them in a barrel for 5 days to ferment."
	]
	quest.3384CC87F75CE3D8.quest_desc: [
		"The blast furnace block — made from a crucible and wrought iron sheets — is the core of the blast furnace multiblock. See the Field Guide for assembly."
		"The chimney is built from reinforced fire bricks: craft fire brick blocks one-to-one with wrought iron sheets. Each chimney layer needs 8 reinforced fire bricks, i.e. 8 fire brick blocks and 8 sheets; all five layers total 40 of each."
		"Each extra chimney layer lets the furnace smelt 4 more items at once, up to five layers. Once you have steel, steel sheets work identically in the recipe — purely for prestige."
	]
	quest.3384CC87F75CE3D8.quest_subtitle: "The Great Leap Forward"
	quest.33A7DF6877E1156F.quest_desc: [
		"Concrete roads are the fastest roads — +55% walking speed — but a pain to lay."
		""
		"First, make dry concrete from road gravel and lime, then mix with water for wet concrete. Wet concrete can be poured onto roadbed, spreading to nearby roadbed within a certain distance. Poured wet concrete hardens after one day."
		""
		"During that time, prevent footprints and cracks: smooth footprints with an adze, and pre-empt cracks by texturing with an adze, bricks, slabs or smooth stone."
	]
	quest.33A7DF6877E1156F.quest_subtitle: "Swift as flight"
	quest.33A7DF6877E1156F.title: "Concrete Roads"
	quest.33AA8BC85792D78B.quest_desc: [
		"The steam whistle works like the steam engine: attach it to a fluid tank, heat with a blaze burner below, and feed water into the tank."
		""
		"Then trigger it with a redstone signal to sound. Taller whistles mean higher pitch."
	]
	quest.33AA8BC85792D78B.quest_subtitle: "Alternative redstone music"
	quest.33D468009A3EC3C0.quest_desc: [
		"The small vessel has only four slots and holds items of small size or less — but carrying any number never overburdens you. It preserves food like the large vessel, and doesn't attract rats."
		""
		"It also holds molten metal, which makes it essential for early-game smelting."
	]
	quest.33E80491FC2DC2C8.quest_desc: [
		"A hoe. It tills, and only tills."
	]
	quest.33E80491FC2DC2C8.quest_subtitle: "Humble devotion"
	quest.33E80491FC2DC2C8.title: "Stone Hoe"
	quest.33F3478160739D5C.quest_desc: [
		"Most crops provide grain and vegetable nutrition — the wheats, rice, potatoes, tomatoes and so on."
		"Some are purely functional, like jute and papyrus. Some provide fruit nutrition, like melons and pumpkins."
		"The TerraFirma world now has six new faces: peanuts, lentils, cassava, alfalfa, radishes and rapeseed. Peanuts and lentils are legumes that enrich soil; alfalfa is prime livestock feed; discover the rest in JEI at your leisure."
		"Some crops have extra recipes processing them into other foods — check JEI yourself."
		""
		"The wilds hide two kitchen treasures as well: &aMugwort&r grows in sparse-to-moderate forests (temperature -8~35°C, groundwater 110~320mm — it won't grow in the densest old-growth woods). Harvest it like any wild crop: it's a signature herb in Kaleidoscope Cookery dishes, and you can replant it at home (best at 0~30°C). The same forests may also hide &awild tea trees&r (Oolong, Biluochun) — be sure to pick them when you spot them."
	]
	quest.33F3478160739D5C.title: "Crop Varieties"
	quest.3426F71FFE26FC02.quest_desc: [
		"A mod of epoch-making significance — it truly brings physics to TerraFirma."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the 'Aeronautics' side chapter."
	]
	quest.3426F71FFE26FC02.title: "Aeronautics"
	quest.343FF73154FB81F9.quest_desc: [
		"The stock link creates storage networks and must sit on a packager to work."
		""
		"A freshly placed link creates a new network; other network devices — including more links — right-click a placed link to join the same network."
		""
		"The network records the contents of every container under every link's packager, for other devices to draw on."
	]
	quest.344C0DE52BB39203.quest_desc: [
		"In case you haven't: pineapple fiber, wool and cotton balls must all be processed with a spindle."
	]
	quest.346251D17EE4D23C.quest_desc: [
		"You can craft four ore dusts into an ore chunk."
	]
	quest.346251D17EE4D23C.title: "Ore Chunks"
	quest.34968B0E98E0361B.quest_desc: [
		"To make dye, boil flowers with fresh water in a clay pot — one flower yields 100 mB of dye. An item-form dye can also be boiled with water into 1000 mB."
		""
		"Seal liquid dye in a barrel with the item to be dyed for one minute to dye it."
	]
	quest.34968B0E98E0361B.title: "Dyeing"
	quest.34C46B1F330D644B.quest_desc: [
		"Basic generators come in two kinds: kinetic and thermoelectric. The kinetic's water wheel and the thermoelectric generator both need steel. The windmill needs no steel, but lots of fiber for its sails."
		""
		"The thermoelectric generator makes power from temperature difference between blocks on its opposite sides — uranium blocks are hottest, blue ice coldest. See the IE manual for temperatures and math. A fully loaded one gives about 60 FE/t."
		""
		"Kinetic generators come as windmills and water wheels. Three parallel full-speed water wheels reach 75 FE/t; windmills are unstable, generating more the higher and more open the site."
	]
	quest.34C46B1F330D644B.title: "Power Generation"
	quest.34CF2CC505369BDE.quest_desc: [
		"Once you obtain a wrought iron ingot, this chapter opens automatically."
	]
	quest.34CF2CC505369BDE.quest_subtitle: "Here comes the most grueling part"
	quest.34FFDE76B445328D.quest_desc: [
		"Titanium is the rocket's skeleton. Titanium veins are rare, generating in diabase, basalt, diorite and granite (y=-60 to 30), and surface indicators are scarce too — locate veins with the prospecting rod, or set up a mineral drill and pump directly."
		"The fastest smelting route is the IE arc furnace: crush titanium ore and electro-smelt straight into ingots. The official crush–wash–calcine chain also works, but it's much slower. Not recommended."
		"Titanium ingots have two destinies: rolled into plates for the rocket hull, or stockpiled for titanium alloy. Do the math before mass production — you will need a lot. More than you think."
		"Titanium tools are real, but don't waste the metal. In this pack, every ingot of titanium belongs at the launch site."
	]
	quest.34FFDE76B445328D.quest_subtitle: "The aerospace metal"
	quest.34FFDE76B445328D.title: "Titanium"
	quest.3501024A6D495590.quest_desc: [
		"Smelting copper alloys means mixing copper with other metals in these ratios:"
		""
		"Bronze: copper 88%-92%, tin 8%-12%"
		""
		"Lead bronze: copper 88%-92%, tin 2%-12%, lead 0%-10%"
		""
		"Bismuth bronze: copper 50%-65%, zinc 20%-30%, bismuth 10%-20%"
		""
		"Black bronze: copper 50%-70%, silver 10%-25%, gold 10%-25%"
		""
		"Lead bronze performs exactly like bronze, but lead won't dissolve into copper on its own — it only alloys alongside tin, so pure lead won't cut it. Once you reach the industrial age, the arc furnace can smelt 10 bronze ingots straight from 9 copper ingots and 1 lead ingot."
	]
	quest.3501024A6D495590.title: "Metals for Alloying"
	quest.353810193654E546.quest_desc: [
		"Speed scales with machine speed: faster is more efficient, and some machines won't even run below a minimum speed. But faster also means more stress consumed — once consumption exceeds production, the whole system overloads and stops."
	]
	quest.353810193654E546.title: "Speed \\& Machine Efficiency"
	quest.354C40286C33986F.quest_desc: [
		"Craft mortar with bricks to get brick blocks. 'Bricks' can be clay bricks, stone bricks from loose stone plus chisel, or alabaster bricks from gypsum plus chisel."
	]
	quest.354C40286C33986F.quest_subtitle: "I am a brick"
	quest.354C40286C33986F.title: "Brick Blocks"
	quest.35761A414FD15CF7.quest_desc: [
		"With wrought iron you can forge a wrought iron grill — same performance as the cast iron one, but it roasts five items at once."
	]
	quest.35761A414FD15CF7.quest_subtitle: "Secret-recipe BBQ"
	quest.35B744A70CF5346E.quest_desc: [
		"The redstone accumulator stores an analog signal that grows or shrinks over time: input at the back adds, at the sides subtracts, with rates configurable up to one hour."
		"The inductor lets the output smoothly follow the input. They are the logic blocks of vehicle automation — cruise control, auto-hover."
	]
	quest.35B744A70CF5346E.quest_subtitle: "The art of analog signals"
	quest.35B744A70CF5346E.title: "Accumulator \\& Inductor"
	quest.35EB4D21853E71CD.quest_desc: [
		"The levitating stone (floating crystal) lets physics structures ignore gravity: with enough of them a structure hovers; at low speed it dampens movement, at high speed the drag fades. It only holds altitude — it can't gain it — so pair it with propellers or balloons."
		"Key point: in this pack it comes from the Moon. After landing, crush lunar soil into moondust, heat-mix with zinc nuggets and water into a levitating mixture, then heat-crystallize it. This is an endgame material past the Cosmonautics chapter — just get acquainted for now."
	]
	quest.35EB4D21853E71CD.quest_subtitle: "The stone from the stars"
	quest.35EB4D21853E71CD.title: "Levitating Stone"
	quest.35EDA0570B25B5B7.quest_desc: [
		"Greenhouse blocks come in four materials — treated wood, copper, iron, stainless steel — all valid for greenhouse walls. They no longer have tiers or crop restrictions; a greenhouse is judged on three things only: whether the space is enclosed, the ratio of glass in the roof, and the walls' insulation."
		""
		"Building is simple: enclose a space (floor is your choice), and let more than half the roof be sky-visible glass. The system scans automatically every 5 seconds — no extra devices needed."
		""
		"&4Key point: an enclosed space alone is NOT a greenhouse — you must place planters inside before it starts working. Only planters judged 'in a valid greenhouse' let crops grow year-round; aim at a planter to see its current status."
		""
		"Once built: place planters → sow seeds (each seed says which planter it needs) → ensure water supply (pump station + irrigation tanks, see later quests) → aim at crops to check temperature. With all that, crops grow year-round regardless of season or latitude."
		""
		"Except for stainless steel, greenhouse blocks slowly weather and look aged — purely cosmetic. For a warmer interior, choose wall materials with higher thermal resistance; see the 'Cellar' section."
	]
	quest.35EDA0570B25B5B7.title: "Building a Greenhouse"
	quest.35F4AC7FB65C9134.quest_desc: [
		"Mix oil one-to-one with the lye from boiling wood ash to get liquid soap."
	]
	quest.35F4AC7FB65C9134.quest_subtitle: "Mainly fatty-acid metal salts"
	quest.35F4AC7FB65C9134.title: "Adding Lye "
	quest.3606AB504297B1DA.quest_desc: [
		"The fluid valve controls whether fluid passes; the direction of input rotation toggles it open or shut."
	]
	quest.362650C4D6EE8386.quest_desc: [
		"Wooden and andesite propellers mount on propeller bearings: spin for thrust, reverse the spin (or use a wrench) to reverse the thrust."
		"Mind air pressure: the higher the altitude, the thinner the air and the weaker the thrust. Engineer's goggles show propeller thrust and airflow directly."
	]
	quest.362650C4D6EE8386.quest_subtitle: "The shape of wind"
	quest.362650C4D6EE8386.title: "Propellers"
	quest.363CEADA6EDB2674.quest_desc: [
		"Olives are edible as fruit, but their main use is oil pressing — some recipes need olive oil."
	]
	quest.36541C2252B8E3CF.quest_desc: [
		"The mechanical saw runs sawing recipes — stripping logs, or turning stripped logs into planks. Items always move opposite the saw's spin. A recipe filter slot on the saw accepts a target product to prevent recipe mix-ups."
		""
		"Besides recipes, the saw breaks wooden blocks placed in front of its blade — usable for tree cutting, with tree-felling chain behavior."
		""
		"The saw can be mounted on moving contraptions."
	]
	quest.36541C2252B8E3CF.quest_subtitle: "This thing one-shots you through armor"
	quest.36541C2252B8E3CF.title: "Lumberjack"
	quest.36635352EDEFED02.quest_desc: [
		"Shafts are crafted from two andesite alloy in a column (yields 8) — the medium of power transmission, linking power sources to machines."
		"Early on, you can also smith them on a copper anvil: 1 andesite alloy ingot yields 4 shafts."
		"When you need to change direction, merge or split rotation, bring in a gearbox."
		""
		"Tip: super glue for contraptions is made from TFC glue — 600 mB of limewater plus 1 bone meal, sealed in a barrel for about 6 minutes (or just mix it once you have a mechanical mixer). Slime balls are crafted from dough and lime dye (dough = wheat flour + water)."
	]
	quest.36635352EDEFED02.quest_subtitle: "Primitive power"
	quest.36635352EDEFED02.title: "Shafts"
	quest.36A613F0590DA6C6.quest_desc: [
		"Craft roasted cocoa beans with a knife to get one cocoa butter and one cocoa powder."
	]
	quest.36A613F0590DA6C6.title: "Cocoa Powder \\& Cocoa Butter"
	quest.36E9E8D7BFAA90D5.quest_desc: [
		"Leather makes a powerful backpack with a chest's 27 slots, upgradeable even bigger later, plus functional addons. But you need wrought iron to craft it."
	]
	quest.37121B8A35C25813.quest_desc: [
		"The Nether's two structures — the fortress and the piglin bastion — are much like vanilla; only their chest loot changed: more TFC-style, no netherite items, plus one new item: the Lost Page."
		""
		"Everything else is unchanged — barter with piglins, farm blaze rods for brewing stands, even collect wither skeleton skulls to challenge the Wither."
	]
	quest.37121B8A35C25813.title: "Nether Fortress \\& Bastion"
	quest.3719F7703554F320.quest_desc: [
		"Grafting lets you plant multiple saplings in one spot — just hold saplings in your off-hand while planting. The more saplings grafted together, the taller the fruit tree."
		""
		"Branch-grafting lets you keep planting on an existing fruit tree: chop the leaves one block above a side branch, and a sapling can be planted on that branch — and these can be multi-grafted too."
		""
		"Note: both techniques only work within the same species."
	]
	quest.3719F7703554F320.title: "Grafting \\& Branch-grafting"
	quest.380699080752117C.quest_desc: [
		"TerraFirma's geography and geology — in this version even the continents' outlines, climate and elevation — resemble the real Earth, and the world wraps east to west: walk west far enough and you return from the east."
		""
		"Land and seabed are built from combinations of rock layers, distributed randomly but following rules set by rock type. By formation, rocks fall into four categories: intrusive igneous, extrusive igneous, sedimentary, metamorphic."
		""
		"You can preview the world on the 'More' page when creating it, as shown below."
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quest/earthpic.png width:199 height:199 align:center fit:true}"
	]
	quest.380699080752117C.quest_subtitle: "Also documented in high-school geography textbooks"
	quest.380699080752117C.title: "Geography"
	quest.3868F993DA506EFB.quest_desc: [
		"&8*Full tutorial at"
		" {\\\"text\\\":\\\"Blueprint System\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"change_page\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"5A304CBBF873084F/1\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
		""
		"To keep your home from becoming a crater, this cannon has been strictly educated. Please be informed:"
		""
		"1. It never destroys terrain."
		"In the TerraFirma world, raw rock, ores, cobblestone, gravel, sand, dirt — anything 'collapse-prone' — is skipped entirely during printing. It won't tear down your mountain or fill in your river. For a flush fit, level the site yourself first."
		""
		"2. It refuses to print three categories:"
		"· Collapse-prone natural blocks (raw rock, ores, sand and soil, etc.);"
		"· Crops and food plants (crops, berry bushes, grape trellises, etc.);"
		"· Functional devices (firepits, crucibles, bloomeries, barrels, looms, ovens — blocks with a 'soul')."
		""
		"If you include such things when selecting a blueprint area, they are automatically stripped on upload — gone from the blueprint. Not a bug."
	]
	quest.3868F993DA506EFB.quest_subtitle: "Absolutely divine"
	quest.3868F993DA506EFB.title: "Schematic Cannon"
	quest.39107DBA8BD69DCC.quest_desc: [
		"An electric heat source, used with a crucible — with power, it heats the crucible it faces continuously up to brilliant white."
	]
	quest.3932DC5968DF0C33.quest_desc: [
		"The storage crate needs 8 treated planks; same capacity as a vanilla chest, but keeps its contents when broken — a shulker box equivalent. You can also smith a blast-resistant reinforced version from wrought iron."
	]
	quest.3932DC5968DF0C33.quest_subtitle: "Budget shulker box"
	quest.398B6DAC78DC2CFE.quest_desc: [
		"Besides soup, the clay pot processes certain items — recipes usually using fluid and items together."
	]
	quest.398B6DAC78DC2CFE.quest_subtitle: "You TerraFirma folk distill with THIS?"
	quest.398B6DAC78DC2CFE.title: "Clay Pot"
	quest.39DE2E8BC467A29A.quest_desc: [
		"Then sun-dry the soybean mixture to make tofu."
	]
	quest.3A01FA1E3321994A.quest_desc: [
		"Hold a roofing material to turn frames into roofs: clay shingles, thatch, or wooden roofs."
	]
	quest.3A01FA1E3321994A.title: "Laying Roofs"
	quest.3A42F619D5B43142.quest_desc: [
		"Most metal-bearing items have a melting point; heat one above it and it becomes molten metal. Items that can melt say so in their tooltip."
		""
		"The pit kiln burns at &ebrilliant white****&f, above copper's melting point of &6orange****&f, so it can smelt copper. The vessel for that is the small vessel, since it holds molten metal."
		""
		"Early on, copper tools can only be cast, so you'll need clay molds. Copper itself is gathered with an item called the gold pan."
	]
	quest.3A42F619D5B43142.title: "Metal Smelting"
	quest.3A55B82F4CB9279F.quest_desc: [
		"As everyone knows, raw food can be cooked over fire, and cooked food lasts longer."
		""
		"You can also process ingredients into dishes — soup, cooking and the like. Some of these steps reset the food's shelf life."
	]
	quest.3A55B82F4CB9279F.quest_subtitle: "Always eat your food cooked"
	quest.3A55B82F4CB9279F.title: "Cooking"
	quest.3A6ECF3BC2695612.quest_desc: [
		"Crude olive oil must be filtered through a jute net — the net gets dirty afterward."
	]
	quest.3A78004CF696FED3.quest_desc: [
		"Try completing TerraFirmaCraft's challenging advancements"
	]
	quest.3A78004CF696FED3.title: "Missing Some Advancements?"
	quest.3AC8BBC5D8A18D03.quest_desc: [
		"Contraptions are Create's signature mechanic: they move in various ways and operate machines that interact with the world's blocks. The ultimate test of your imagination and creativity."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the 'Contraptions' side chapter."
	]
	quest.3AC8BBC5D8A18D03.title: "Contraptions"
	quest.3AE900D7D541CE10.quest_desc: [
		"A contraption is, simply put, a group of blocks connected in some way that specific devices can move."
		""
		"At rest, contraptions stay in 'block form'; once moving, the blocks become 'entities' and can sometimes even pass through walls."
		""
		"When entity blocks turn back into blocks, they destroy whatever overlaps them — the principle behind certain tunnel borers."
	]
	quest.3AE900D7D541CE10.title: "Contraptions"
	quest.3B2B3B973F81A152.quest_desc: [
		"Four lumber craft into planks — a solid anti-gravity block, extremely useful against collapses."
	]
	quest.3B59AE17DFC0A2FD.quest_desc: [
		"Red steel requires weak red steel first — an alloy of black steel, steel, brass and rose gold."
	]
	quest.3B59AE17DFC0A2FD.title: "Rose Gold Ingot"
	quest.3B8708B845F3F428.quest_desc: [
		"When an adjustable chain gearshift in a chain drive group is redstone-activated, every chain drive's speed doubles."
	]
	quest.3BD5B18C86A48A8F.quest_desc: [
		"The sledgehammer mines stone-type blocks in a 3x3 area, losing durability proportionally."
	]
	quest.3BD5B18C86A48A8F.title: "Sledgehammer"
	quest.3BE6B2F8C725A33B.quest_desc: [
		"The chainsaw is a handheld tree-felling tool. Compared to TFC axes, its chain-felling also destroys leaves. It runs on biodiesel."
		""
		"A saw blade must be installed to work; blades have durability and must be replaced when broken."
		""
		"Three different upgrade modules grant it stronger abilities."
		""
		"Each block cut consumes 1 mB of fuel. Refuel at the refinery or a barrel of biodiesel — refueling from a barrel requires the saw to be empty."
	]
	quest.3BE6B2F8C725A33B.quest_subtitle: "A storm of sap and sawdust"
	quest.3BE8BA6DBF8C0672.quest_desc: [
		"The pack team has prepared shaders perfectly adapted to the TerraFirma world!"
		""
		"We strongly recommend:"
		"ComplementaryReimagined_r5.8.1 + EuphoriaPatches_1.9.3"
		"ComplementaryUnbound_r5.8.1 + EuphoriaPatches_1.9.3"
		""
		"We not only fully adapted these two beloved shaderpacks to TerraFirma, but also optimized them for Create and Voxy."
		""
		"The pack already bundles the EuphoriaPatches mod — grab the shaderpacks from the links below!"
		""
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Complementary Shaders - Reimagined\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://modrinth.com/shader/complementary-reimagined/version/r5.8.1\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
		""
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Complementary Shaders - Unbound\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://modrinth.com/shader/complementary-unbound/version/r5.8.1\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
		""
		"Low FPS with shaders on? Go to Video Settings → Shader Packs → Shader Pack Settings and drop the quality profile (top-left) to Medium or Low — shadow quality, water reflections and volumetric clouds are the heavy hitters."
		"If the counter shows high FPS but the game still hitches, make sure you're on the latest version: 1.0.0-release fixed two render-thread spikes that caused periodic stutter."
	]
	quest.3BE8BA6DBF8C0672.quest_subtitle: "The fragrance of a graphics card"
	quest.3BE8BA6DBF8C0672.title: "Shader Compatibility"
	quest.3C11714A5B52041C.quest_desc: [
		"Once livestock familiarity reaches 30%, feeding two animals of different sexes makes the female pregnant — or makes egg-layers' eggs fertilized."
		""
		"Animals age each time they're milked, sheared, bred or lay eggs. A fully aged animal produces nothing."
	]
	quest.3C11714A5B52041C.title: "Animal Production"
	quest.3C199CD2E93E3A39.quest_desc: [
		"The sewing table adds cloth to armor for insulation. By default: helmets +4 warmth, chestplates +6, leggings +5, boots +4."
		""
		"Usable cloths are the five mentioned before; you can also sew a full leather set onto armor."
	]
	quest.3C2EB8929EB21826.quest_desc: [
		"The greatest geologist of the TerraFirma world."
	]
	quest.3C2EB8929EB21826.quest_subtitle: "The meaning of travel"
	quest.3C2EB8929EB21826.title: "&eChallenge: Adventuring Time"
	quest.3C5338C73A49C6E7.quest_desc: [
		"If you have grain left after breadmaking, brew it into alcohol. Grain alcohol quenches more thirst than fresh water and grants potion effects."
	]
	quest.3C5338C73A49C6E7.quest_subtitle: "Only Du Kang"
	quest.3C5338C73A49C6E7.title: "What Cures Sorrow"
	quest.3C5CA88FF94EE6F0.quest_desc: [
		"Want something different? Try trains. This great Create addition has a complete transport system — seriously fun."
		""
		"The tutorial is in Create's side chapter, or hold W on a train station to ponder it."
	]
	quest.3C5CA88FF94EE6F0.title: "Trains"
	quest.3C5CE18D51751BCE.quest_desc: [
		"After fermentation, winemaking finishes in the pressing basin. You'll need bottles and corks to bottle it, and can craft labels to name your wine."
		""
		"Three wines are possible depending on ingredients: pure grape = red or white; red-white mix = rosé; white plus sweetener = dessert wine. In any case, one batch of wine consumes four servings of crushed grapes as the base."
	]
	quest.3C820C87C5A199E7.quest_desc: [
		"The grounding rod makes the earth itself part of the circuit. In electrified railways and similar setups, the ground can serve as the return path: negative terminal to the rod, current comes home through the earth — saving half your wire."
		"Remember what it looks like; you'll need it again at the railway electrification step."
	]
	quest.3C820C87C5A199E7.quest_subtitle: "The earth is the best conductor"
	quest.3C820C87C5A199E7.title: "Grounding"
	quest.3C85EA3C2F146C7D.quest_desc: [
		"Copper pipes are the medium of fluid transport; open a viewing window with a wrench. Pipes themselves neither store nor move fluid — they need a pump's help."
		""
		"In a properly connected pipe run, fluid first spends some time traveling through the pipes, then gets drawn from the input and discharged at the output."
		""
		"Pipes can be encased in copper casing to stop them connecting to newly placed pipes nearby."
	]
	quest.3CE7C06DCC97A989.quest_desc: [
		"Sequenced assembly works like a production line: an item passes through every processing step shown in the recipe to complete one sequence, and completing the required number of sequences finishes the recipe."
	]
	quest.3CE7C06DCC97A989.quest_subtitle: "Assembly line basics"
	quest.3CE7C06DCC97A989.title: "Precision Mechanisms \\& Sequenced Assembly"
	quest.3D212DF3C92D3A48.quest_desc: [
		"The frogport works with chain drives to transport packages, but must first be bound to a point on the chain."
		""
		"Right-click to open it and configure its address at the top. When a package with a matching address reaches the bound point, it unloads it; otherwise it hangs packages from its own stock onto the bound point."
		""
		"The frogport reads the inventory of the container below it for automatic loading and unloading."
	]
	quest.3D4A2683955E9A3E.quest_desc: [
		"Preserving dairy is simple, since liquid milk itself never spoils."
		""
		"To use it as an ingredient, make cheese — but block-form cheese also never spoils, so there's really no need to preserve dairy at all."
	]
	quest.3D4A2683955E9A3E.title: "Dairy"
	quest.3D512BAC43861997.quest_desc: [
		"Javelins deal piercing damage and are common hunting tools. Hold right-click to throw; all but stone javelins deal extra damage when thrown, and thrown javelins can be recovered."
	]
	quest.3D512BAC43861997.title: "Stone Javelin"
	quest.3DA307C6BE5C30E9.quest_desc: [
		"Weld a weak red steel ingot with a black steel ingot for a high-carbon red steel ingot; smith that into a red steel ingot."
		""
		"Red steel is the top tier-VI metal, making the finest gear and weapons with some new recipes. Performance is close to blue steel, but with slightly fewer recipes."
	]
	quest.3DA307C6BE5C30E9.quest_subtitle: "&cRed is destruction"
	quest.3DA307C6BE5C30E9.title: "&4Seeing Red"
	quest.3DBEC5FDBDA6531C.quest_desc: [
		"The clutch controls transmission: while a redstone signal is applied, its output stops transmitting."
	]
	quest.3DD999F93EBE72F0.quest_desc: [
		"Biodiesel is the pack's strongest liquid fuel, blended from plant oil and ethanol. A biodiesel generator can power an arc furnace; a biodiesel blaze burner super-burns; a biodiesel lamp never even goes out!"
	]
	quest.3DD999F93EBE72F0.quest_subtitle: "The strongest fuel"
	quest.3DD999F93EBE72F0.title: "Biodiesel"
	quest.3DFC64CF4AB70D66.quest_desc: [
		"Electric pumps move water, resistance heaters supply heat — the grid ends at these appliances that do real work."
		""
		"Powered, the resistance heater continuously heats Create's basin: about 150V gives normal heating, about 260V burns straight to brilliant white — even superheated recipes like titanium-alloy mixing run on pure electricity. No more hauling fuel."
		"The classic route still works: a blaze burner fed blaze cakes also reaches brilliant white. Electricity or blaze — your pick."
	]
	quest.3DFC64CF4AB70D66.quest_subtitle: "Electricity ends in productivity"
	quest.3DFC64CF4AB70D66.title: "Electric Appliances"
	quest.3E20E2E7B5C1A827.quest_desc: [
		"Finally, toss the dirty dust into the sluice for another wash to get clean ore dust."
	]
	quest.3E20E2E7B5C1A827.title: "Second Washing"
	quest.3EC674D6F7C27E47.quest_desc: [
		"Don't want catenary overhead? Lay powered rails beside the track as a third rail, and let the train draw power through contact shoes — that's how subways do it."
		"Both approaches reach the same goal; pick whichever you like. Or both."
	]
	quest.3EC674D6F7C27E47.quest_subtitle: "The subway solution"
	quest.3EC674D6F7C27E47.title: "Third-Rail Power"
	quest.3EDEBC9A4690B413.quest_desc: [
		"Aggregate is made from sand, lime and gravel — the raw material of every kind of concrete."
	]
	quest.3EE9FAE53AF76B68.quest_desc: [
		"The andesite tunnel only sits on belts — it covers them, and splits or merges items."
		""
		"When another belt appears beside the tunnel, spinning outward, the tunnel diverts one item sideways as they pass."
	]
	quest.3F0784CD76D70976.quest_desc: [
		"Wattle is a usable building material that starts as a non-solid block. Reinforce it with four sticks and apply daub to make it solid; it can be dyed afterward."
	]
	quest.3F1BA95908C2732B.quest_desc: [
		"Crops are anything planted on farmland. They continuously track local temperature, soil moisture and more, and stop growing the moment conditions fail — so some crops may only grow in certain seasons at your base."
		""
		"Most seeds are only found in the wild; alternatively, let your own mature crops wither and harvest them for extra seeds."
	]
	quest.3F1BA95908C2732B.title: "Crops"
	quest.3F3AF995356D9D26.quest_desc: [
		"The large cogwheel is the cogwheel's big sibling and works the same; connecting large and small cogwheels requires diagonal placement."
		""
		"Large cogwheels must be placed diagonally above or below each other to connect — which also changes rotation direction."
	]
	quest.3F56FC7D615285CF.quest_desc: [
		"Of IE's three new metals, lead and aluminum go into batteries and wires, while uranium serves as the thermoelectric generator's temperature indicator block."
	]
	quest.3F56FC7D615285CF.title: "IE-Exclusive Metals"
	quest.3F9D2B44C6E87A15.quest_desc: [
		"A carriage on flat ground just sits there — to make it run, first give it a 'mountain'."
		""
		"Hold a chain, right-click the track anchor at the lift hill's start, then the one at the end — that stretch becomes a chain lift. Feed Create rotation into the start end and the chain hauls the carriage up the hill — after that, gravity takes over."
		""
		"Put a carriage on the track, then right-click an existing carriage with another to link a train; chains extend couplings, shears disconnect them, a wrench adjusts their length."
		""
		"Sit tight. Hold the handrail."
	]
	quest.3F9D2B44C6E87A15.quest_subtitle: "Going up to come down"
	quest.3F9D2B44C6E87A15.title: "Roller Coaster: Chain Lift"
	quest.3FAFD4C71152501D.quest_desc: [
		"Used for steelmaking; burns charcoal, and you can keep feeding charcoal to keep it lit."
	]
	quest.4073B1CE55962375.quest_desc: [
		"Glass blowpipe in main hand and paddle in off-hand flattens; wool cloth flips."
	]
	quest.4073B1CE55962375.title: "Paddle \\& Wool Cloth"
	quest.408992F05F89C9EC.quest_desc: [
		"The smart fluid pipe filters what fluid may pass: its filter slot accepts fluid-filled buckets or filters to control intake."
	]
	quest.4097F05E5EEADD26.quest_desc: [
		"Voxy distant-terrain rendering is now built in (running on NeoForge through the Roxy translation layer) and enabled by default — it just works out of the box."
		"On weaker hardware, disable Voxy in Settings > Video Settings for better FPS. With Voxy on, allocate 8 GB or more RAM; with it off, 6 GB is enough."
		""
		"Below: a live demo of Voxy enabled in this version:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quest/voxypic.png width:199 height:105 align:center fit:true}"
	]
	quest.4097F05E5EEADD26.quest_subtitle: "VOXY Distant Terrain"
	quest.4097F05E5EEADD26.title: "Important Info!"
	quest.40DF0E9B77C38D92.quest_desc: [
		"TerraFirmaCraft has a built-in rotational power system — incompatible with Create's, and only able to drive certain TFC blocks. In this pack, you'll use it for early-game ore processing."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the 'Create in TerraFirma' side chapter."
	]
	quest.412838D43D7696DE.quest_desc: [
		"Accumulators are IE's storage blocks — LV stores least, HV stores most. Flip input/output with the engineer's hammer; output rate matches the same tier of wire."
	]
	quest.412838D43D7696DE.title: "Accumulators"
	quest.4138359FFA31C5AA.quest_desc: [
		"Trains are compatible with anything that works on moving contraptions — vaults, rollers, etc. Seats on trains can be seat cushions, and train doors open and close automatically."
	]
	quest.4138359FFA31C5AA.title: "Machines Aboard Trains"
	quest.41DAAB831CADD8D6.quest_desc: [
		"The chute transports items vertically and holds up to one stack of one type. Right-click with a wrench to open a viewing window."
		""
		"It automatically pulls items from a container above, or picks up drops that land on it. Depending on the block below, it will insert items into the container below, eject them, or hold them inside."
		""
		"Drops or other logistics methods can feed up to a full stack into a chute at once, but its own pull from containers is capped at 16 items."
		""
		"Chutes can connect diagonally. A correctly placed encased fan lets a chute output items upward."
		""
		"A chute only accepts drops touching its top face — not drops floating one block above it."
	]
	quest.425D15D6FDA4B24F.quest_desc: [
		"Once a dairy animal's familiarity is high enough, you can milk it. Drink milk from a jug to raise your dairy nutrition."
	]
	quest.425D15D6FDA4B24F.quest_subtitle: "The cow didn't say no"
	quest.425D15D6FDA4B24F.title: "Snatching Milk"
	quest.426E11D4D6257FD2.quest_desc: [
		"Stone roads come in three types, each speeding up walking by 35%. Their surfaces are gravel, stone bricks, and stone slabs respectively — apart from looks, all three are identical."
	]
	quest.426E11D4D6257FD2.quest_subtitle: "Feels great underfoot"
	quest.426E11D4D6257FD2.title: "Stone Roads"
	quest.4302389524B381E8.quest_desc: [
		"The sluice is used for ore processing. Place it as shown below — if water flows through the sluice, the setup is correct."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/sluice.png width:145 height:60 align:1}"
		"Toss items onto the top end of the sluice to start washing; the products appear at the bottom end."
	]
	quest.4302389524B381E8.quest_subtitle: "Where the grind begins"
	quest.4302389524B381E8.title: "Sluice"
	quest.434F32943A1F60DD.quest_desc: [
		"The powder keg is TNT's replacement: put gunpowder inside to make it explosive — the more gunpowder, the stronger the blast. Only a sealed powder keg can be ignited."
	]
	quest.436CFC57235037BF.quest_desc: [
		"The mechanical harvester only works on moving contraptions."
		""
		"It harvests mature crops it passes over, resetting their growth and dropping the yield. If the contraption has storage, the drops are transferred into it."
	]
	quest.436CFC57235037BF.title: "Mechanical Harvesting"
	quest.43C440FC3D7E1296.quest_desc: [
		"Craft flour together with a bucket of yeast and a sweetener (sugar or honey) to get dough — this dough can only be baked in an oven. The resulting bread has more nutrition and a longer shelf life than flatbread."
	]
	quest.43C440FC3D7E1296.quest_subtitle: "Who doesn't love bread?"
	quest.43C8F5AB4360EB12.quest_desc: [
		"A campfire fitted with a grill goes from one heating slot to five. Everything else stays the same."
	]
	quest.43C8F5AB4360EB12.title: "Grill"
	quest.43DF7C319557F1D5.quest_desc: [
		"While exploring Nether structures you may find an item called a Lost Page in loot chests. To use it, you must perform a rite known as the Sacrifice Ritual."
		""
		"Build an ancient altar from blackstone and gold. Place a Lost Page on the altar and right-click it with a cut gem to break its seal. A Lost Page generally contains three things: a cost, a reward, and a penalty. An unsealed page, together with its required cost, can be used for more advanced rituals."
		""
		"Costs and rewards come in fixed pairs: raw slime for rich garnierite, cobblestone for blackstone, cursed leather for a large hide. Penalties, however, are completely random — from nothing at all, to dizziness, to even a Wither! Of course, you can also exploit the penalty mechanic to farm mobs; at least they drop experience."
	]
	quest.43ED67D161B4D11E.quest_desc: [
		"Super glue is the easiest way to build a contraption."
		""
		"Right-click two opposite corners of a rectangular area to glue all connected blocks within it together; left-click to remove a glued area."
		""
		"Glued areas covering the same blocks count as one whole. When a machine moves one block, every block in the area moves with it — that is how a contraption is formed."
	]
	quest.43ED67D161B4D11E.quest_subtitle: "How sticky does glue have to be to move blocks?"
	quest.43ED67D161B4D11E.title: "Contraption Basics"
	quest.4459F03597D66E94.quest_desc: [
		"Compress several foods into one dish to gain more nutrition per meal."
	]
	quest.4459F03597D66E94.title: "Salad"
	quest.4477187C54E7FC6A.quest_desc: [
		"Stress is generated by stress sources and has magnitude. In a stress network of sources and machines, more sources mean more total stress capacity, more machines mean more stress consumed, and raising rotation speed raises consumption proportionally."
		""
		"When consumption exceeds capacity, the whole network overloads and stops."
	]
	quest.4477187C54E7FC6A.title: "Stress"
	quest.44B6DA3984A355EC.quest_desc: [
		"A maxed-out boiler sets your stress free."
	]
	quest.44B6DA3984A355EC.title: "Rolling Steam"
	quest.450A080198B48675.quest_desc: [
		"You've gathered seven copper-alloy double ingots and made a copper-alloy anvil. Time to learn advanced smithing techniques."
	]
	quest.450A080198B48675.quest_subtitle: "Don't forget to melt down the copper anvil"
	quest.450A080198B48675.title: "Level Up"
	quest.4525DB7844975EC1.quest_desc: [
		"That's all there is to say. Your TerraFirma journey begins now."
		""
		"One more thing:"
		"Most of TFCR's BGM is composed by the pack's author; at players' request, the classic 3.1.2 tracks are mixed into the rotation."
		"Press \\\"Page Up\\\" (default) to skip the current track!"
		""
		"Albums:"
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"TerraFirma: Rebirth Original Soundtrack\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://music.163.com/album?id=357966421&uct2=U2FsdGVkX1/rFe7nS3Z6XJkbTLczZTH5d7xl3yu519U=\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"TFCR 3.1.2 Legacy BGM\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://music.163.com/playlist?id=13680143559&uct2=U2FsdGVkX1+0Dhqwse6DBuO2cpnMGK6m6l73HlZL/l4=\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
	]
	quest.4525DB7844975EC1.quest_subtitle: "Thanks to every player for supporting this modpack!"
	quest.4525DB7844975EC1.title: "Have Fun!"
	quest.4569D647280858BE.quest_desc: [
		"TerraFirmaCraft demands a lot of travel — many resources, like ores, crops, and kaolinite, can only be found by exploring. Trips of hundreds or thousands of blocks eat up huge amounts of time, so you need to learn how to travel faster and more conveniently."
	]
	quest.4569D647280858BE.title: "Exploration Guide"
	quest.457F36F33E087936.quest_desc: [
		"The voltage regulator dynamically adjusts its output: connect the power source to the top input terminal, ground to the bottom terminal, and the load to the output terminal. It does its best to hold the output at the set voltage (up to 300V)."
		"Generator speed fluctuates, and so does voltage. Anything voltage-sensitive deserves a regulator in front of it."
	]
	quest.457F36F33E087936.quest_subtitle: "Rock-steady output"
	quest.457F36F33E087936.title: "Voltage Regulator"
	quest.45A01E8B81172528.quest_desc: [
		"The mechanical drill runs no recipes — once powered, it mines whatever block is in front of it, unless that block is unbreakable."
		""
		"The drill can be, and mostly is, mounted on moving contraptions."
	]
	quest.45A01E8B81172528.title: "Pierce the Heavens"
	quest.45BA1D7C95494A6A.quest_desc: [
		"Wild fruit trees are your only source of fruit-tree saplings. Breaking leaves won't drop saplings — the correct way is to break the side branches (the elbow-shaped limbs connected to the trunk), which have a chance to drop one."
	]
	quest.45BA1D7C95494A6A.title: "Fruit Trees"
	quest.45C227A1327D347F.quest_desc: [
		"The sticker merges two glued areas and is often used to flexibly combine multiple contraptions. Power it with a redstone signal to attach it to the glued area in front of it, carrying that area along when it moves."
		""
		"The sticker cannot move a contraption by itself; it needs help from other devices."
	]
	quest.45C78FC9FC33C382.quest_desc: [
		"Charcoal pits, pit kilns and the like devour logs. Before the trees around your base are all gone, you'd better start planting."
		""
		"Breaking leaves has a chance to drop saplings — higher in autumn and winter, lower in spring and summer. Chopping down the tree itself never yields saplings."
		""
		"Plant a sapling on dirt and wait one or two months for it to grow into a tree. Saplings grow in any environment, so don't worry about them freezing to death."
	]
	quest.45C78FC9FC33C382.title: "Planting Trees"
	quest.4621165AE02945E7.quest_desc: [
		"First, look at the status bars below:"
		""
		"Red bar: health. The 850 HP you spawn with in TerraFirma equals only eight and a half vanilla hearts, and the damage you take is scaled up accordingly. Empty bar, instant death."
		"Blue bar: thirst. It drains constantly; when empty you can barely run. Right-click a water source block or drink from a jug to refill."
		"Green bar: hunger. It drains constantly; when empty you lose health. Eat food to refill."
		""
		"Press E to open your inventory and you'll find several new tabs on the right. From top to bottom: inventory, calendar, nutrition, climate."
		""
		"Inventory: the vanilla inventory you know."
		"Calendar: shows the current season, date, and time."
		"Nutrition: shows your nutrition — how balanced it is directly affects your max health. Five categories: fruit, vegetables, protein, grain, dairy."
		"Climate: shows local geographic info in five lines — climate zone, geology, average yearly temperature, rainfall, and current temperature. Invaluable for farming."
		""
		"Monsters don't spawn on the surface of the TerraFirma world, but aggressive predators do. Protect yourself."
	]
	quest.4621165AE02945E7.quest_subtitle: "Know yourself to survive better"
	quest.4621165AE02945E7.title: "Know the World: Know Yourself"
	quest.4644474B31278A94.quest_subtitle: "Sedimentary rock, near the surface"
	quest.4644474B31278A94.title: "Limonite"
	quest.469CA7D075645A48.quest_desc: [
		"Pottery only hardens at &eYellow-White****&f heat, so a charcoal forge can't fire it. A pit kiln burns for 8 hours; the products can be removed once it finishes."
	]
	quest.469CA7D075645A48.title: "Pit Kiln Firing"
	quest.46C06C69F3E01563.quest_desc: [
		"Step two: toss the rocky ore chunks into the sluice to wash them into clean ore chunks."
	]
	quest.46C06C69F3E01563.title: "First Wash"
	quest.46DF54D6E0F92F32.quest_desc: [
		"Congratulations on your steel ingot! Before you knew it, you've reached the tail end of TerraFirma's main progression — only the final sprint remains."
	]
	quest.46DF54D6E0F92F32.quest_subtitle: "God made us out of iron. Then he turned up the heat and forged some of us into steel. — Marie Osmond"
	quest.47855701499FB613.quest_desc: [
		"The mechanical piston pushes a glued area into a moving contraption; the sticky version can also pull. Piston poles behind it provide its extension length."
		""
		"A contraption pushed by a mechanical piston shoves blocking blocks along with it, but won't pull them back."
		""
		"Use the config panel on its side to choose when the contraption re-solidifies into blocks."
	]
	quest.47893AFAA75E6084.quest_desc: [
		"Surround a wrought iron backpack with steel ingots to upgrade it into a steel backpack."
	]
	quest.47893AFAA75E6084.title: "Backpack Upgrade"
	quest.478AAC782ABD463B.quest_subtitle: "Extrusive \\& metamorphic rock below y=75"
	quest.478AAC782ABD463B.title: "Pitchblende"
	quest.47AF6FB29788705A.quest_desc: [
		"Only usable in campfires. Low burn temperature, decent duration — but food cooked with it spoils faster. Handy when you need to bulk-process items over a campfire."
	]
	quest.47B95BC50C5BF469.quest_desc: [
		"If copper opened up most of TerraFirmaCraft to the player, copper alloys are what let you truly experience it. If you haven't tried the side chapters yet, I strongly suggest you pause here — those contents are far more fun than the main line."
		""
		"If you're ready, let's begin. This chapter revolves around forging and a new multiblock: the bloomery. With them you will forge the next tier of metal: wrought iron."
	]
	quest.47D557DEACB82596.quest_desc: [
		"Some items and blocks affect your body temperature — just being near them is enough."
	]
	quest.47D557DEACB82596.quest_subtitle: "If you won't change yourself, change the environment"
	quest.47D557DEACB82596.title: "Change the Environment"
	quest.4826595E2F983E4D.quest_subtitle: "Intrusive rock, long thin veins"
	quest.4826595E2F983E4D.title: "Emerald"
	quest.483C8248CC9656DB.quest_desc: [
		"Each of these liquid fats has its own uses — for example, sealing one with a large prepared hide yields a large waterproof hide — but they all share one: making soap. If you have olive oil, that works for soap too."
	]
	quest.483C8248CC9656DB.quest_subtitle: "As everyone knows, rendering lard takes water"
	quest.483C8248CC9656DB.title: "Rendering Animal Fat"
	quest.4841F51E141440D5.quest_desc: [
		"Some gear increases your temperature tolerance, marked by a colored bar on the item. The colors mean:"
		""
		"Blue: cold resistance. Red: heat resistance. Purple: both, at the same strength but half the length. Green (rare): slowly converts to heat or cold resistance based on the environment, at slightly lower strength."
	]
	quest.4841F51E141440D5.quest_subtitle: "If you won't change the environment, change yourself"
	quest.4841F51E141440D5.title: "Change Yourself"
	quest.484748376883382B.quest_desc: [
		"You can use Create's two grinding recipes to mill graphite powder directly; otherwise you'll have to go through ore processing."
	]
	quest.484748376883382B.title: "Graphite Powder"
	quest.486E1B9CF4D2EFB9.quest_desc: [
		"Compared to vanilla MC, the TerraFirma world doesn't spawn monsters every night — but faster-draining hunger, hard-to-get food, predators roaming the wilds, and tougher travel make survival harder instead. Securing the supplies you need to stay alive as early as possible is crucial."
		""
		"In this chapter you'll learn basic stone-tool crafting, gather essential resources, and find a base site that can support you late-game."
	]
	quest.486E1B9CF4D2EFB9.quest_subtitle: "Survival comes first"
	quest.486E1B9CF4D2EFB9.title: "Chapter 1 — Chapter Goals"
	quest.489B226BA26DF7F0.quest_desc: [
		"The modpack uses Journeymap as its minimap, with some TerraFirmaCraft integration. Press J to open the full-screen map."
		""
		"FTB Chunks is also bundled: on servers, press J to open the map and claim your territory — all its features are integrated into Journeymap."
	]
	quest.489B226BA26DF7F0.title: "Minimap"
	quest.48E61577434BAE55.quest_desc: [
		"The pickaxe works like vanilla — it mines stone-type blocks. Worth noting: in TerraFirmaCraft, a wrought iron pick can already mine obsidian."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the \\\"Miner's Guide\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.48E61577434BAE55.quest_subtitle: "And who is more trustworthy than a miner's wife? — Merle Travis"
	quest.48E61577434BAE55.title: "Copper Pickaxe"
	quest.48F4F67F7CE0B7A9.quest_desc: [
		"For now, riding a horse is the fastest way to travel overland. It ignores snow and grass — the most reliable companion for long journeys."
		""
		"If you don't know how to ride yet, check the \\\"Animal Husbandry Guide\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.48F4F67F7CE0B7A9.title: "Horseback Riding"
	quest.49192023FED0246F.quest_desc: [
		"Sugarcane juice must be sealed in a barrel with a jute net to filter it. A used jute net gets dirty — wash it the same way you wash sugarcane."
	]
	quest.49192023FED0246F.quest_subtitle: "Removing impurities"
	quest.49192023FED0246F.title: "Filtering"
	quest.49545DEE6C45E26B.quest_desc: [
		"Logistics — the one system no tech mod can live without, and Create does it with variety and beauty."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the \\\"Logistics \\& Trains\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.49545DEE6C45E26B.title: "Logistics \\& Trains"
	quest.497C472062AAA77F.quest_desc: [
		"Once everything is ready, sneak-right-click the pressing basin to bottle the wine. Wine starts aging as soon as it's bottled — though that's good for little besides showing off."
		""
		"Likewise, the soil, climate, and your naming are all recorded on the bottle — again, mostly for showing off."
		""
		"To drink it, open your inventory, left-click to pick up a knife, then right-click the bottle with it to pop the cork. Afterwards you can pour the wine into a container. Each bottle holds 2000 mB."
	]
	quest.497C472062AAA77F.title: "Bottling"
	quest.498C0678E848015F.quest_desc: [
		"Item vaults and fluid tanks share many traits: both are multiblock-capable, and neither allows direct manual access. Vaults only extend horizontally, though, while tanks extend vertically."
		""
		"Both are recognized by contraptions as storage blocks — vaults store items, tanks store fluids."
	]
	quest.49E9A981425AB2FC.quest_desc: [
		"When you fell a tree with a TerraFirma axe, the whole tree chain-harvests — but the leaves \\\"vanish\\\" rather than get \\\"broken\\\". Only broken leaves can drop saplings, so break the leaves before chopping."
		""
		"The recommended tool is the scythe, which breaks all leaves in a 3x3x3 area. Also, sapling drop rates are higher in autumn and winter than in spring and summer."
	]
	quest.49E9A981425AB2FC.title: "Getting Saplings"
	quest.4A2459F2548324B8.quest_desc: [
		"Seal soybean paste with water for another day to get soybean oil. It's interchangeable with olive oil."
	]
	quest.4A3E47C3873C7F23.quest_desc: [
		"The most convenient rock-type building block — just don't cause a cave-in while chiseling."
	]
	quest.4A3E47C3873C7F23.title: "Smooth Rock"
	quest.4A494F83E795394C.quest_desc: [
		"Wool-bearing animals are alpacas, sheep, and musk oxen. All three eat grain, alpacas also eat fruit, and none of them will touch rotten food."
		""
		"All three produce wool."
	]
	quest.4A494F83E795394C.title: "Wool Animals"
	quest.4A7ADAB0AB733D4B.quest_desc: [
		"Two mineral fuels — bituminous coal burns hotter than lignite. See the \\\"Miner's Guide\\\" side chapter for the rock layers where they generate."
	]
	quest.4A7ADAB0AB733D4B.title: "Coal"
	quest.4A99F71C49461D9E.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a wheel seat with a tire to mount it. In this pack, tires are made from AFC rubber — find a rubber tree in the rainforest and refine some rubber before dreaming of off-roading."
		"From small tires to monster tires, bigger wheels crush more — and eat more rubber. Know your budget."
	]
	quest.4A99F71C49461D9E.quest_subtitle: "Long live rubber"
	quest.4A99F71C49461D9E.title: "Tires"
	quest.4AC4D0ABB02B7448.quest_desc: [
		"Create's core material is andesite alloy — and in this pack it's a true alloy, made the alloying way: grind loose extrusive igneous rocks (andesite, basalt, dacite, or rhyolite — all common on the surface) into magma rock powder with the TFC quern, melt it, then in a small vessel or crucible mix 95%~98% molten magma rock with 2%~5% molten cast iron to get molten andesite alloy, and finally cast it into ingots with an ingot mold."
		""
		"Note that the ingot mold has about a 10% chance to crack per cast — keep spares. Also watch for spherical quartz geodes with a basalt shell: the quartz clusters inside yield quartz shards, and quartz blocks cut on a chopping board give quartz — useful later for rose quartz and electron tubes. No rush now; just mine geodes when you see them."
	]
	quest.4AC4D0ABB02B7448.title: "Material Preparation"
	quest.4AF0C372CFFE8D7C.quest_desc: [
		"JEI is a handy recipe-lookup mod. In your inventory, press R on an item to see recipes that make it; press U to see recipes that use it."
	]
	quest.4AF0C372CFFE8D7C.quest_subtitle: "Surely everyone knows how to use this, right?"
	quest.4AF0C372CFFE8D7C.title: "JEI"
	quest.4B563160ACEE9B03.quest_desc: [
		"In the TerraFirma world you can't smelt sand into glass — you have to blow it."
		""
		"First, prepare a blowpipe. Ceramic or brass, your choice."
		""
		"Second, mix four blocks of the same sand with either saltpeter powder (ground saltpeter) or soda ash (heated dried kelp), plus lime (heated flux), to make glass batch."
		""
		"Crafting glass batch with a blowpipe gives a glass-filled blowpipe. Heat it until pale red to start blowing — but never heat it to white-hot, or the glass inside will vanish."
	]
	quest.4B563160ACEE9B03.quest_subtitle: "A true test of lung capacity"
	quest.4B563160ACEE9B03.title: "Glassblowing"
	quest.4B56E71B921DDA48.quest_desc: [
		"The leather waterskin holds 500 mB of liquid. It's made from two waterskin halves knapped from leather plus a bladder dropped by animals. Drinking wears it down; once broken, it can be repaired with leather and a bladder."
	]
	quest.4B56E71B921DDA48.quest_subtitle: "Based on real craftsmanship"
	quest.4B76274FC4069E8D.quest_desc: [
		"Engineering plastic is made by filling phenolic resin from the refinery in a bottling machine. Mainly used for the railgun."
	]
	quest.4B92A8A1B66D3449.quest_desc: [
		"The quern makes flux at the same yield as the stone hammer — but it can also grind borax into flux."
	]
	quest.4B92A8A1B66D3449.quest_subtitle: "CaCO3"
	quest.4B9C11A6C3097BD9.quest_desc: [
		"Before you set up systematic food preservation, food doesn't keep long. Even campfire-roasted meat sealed in a large vessel lasts only about two and a half months; fruit keeps less than a month even in a vessel. Eating rotten food anyway gives you debuffs."
		""
		"To keep food longer, there are three approaches: choose longer-lasting ingredients, improve your processing, and improve your storage."
	]
	quest.4B9C11A6C3097BD9.quest_subtitle: "You don't want to eat rotten food all day, do you?"
	quest.4B9C11A6C3097BD9.title: "Food Preservation"
	quest.4BADFA04EF810F23.quest_desc: [
		"A modular engine is a three-block axial stack: thruster mount, cycle piping, nozzle. Hang one tank on each side of the mount with 1,000 mB of fuel and 1,000 mB of oxidizer — water and air work as oxidizer too."
		"Right-click the cycle piping with a wrench to switch thermodynamic cycles: closed, open, full-flow, expander — trading thrust against efficiency."
		"Reference thrust: closed cycle + copper nozzle ~10,000 N; open cycle + titanium nozzle ~20,800 N; full-flow + titanium nozzle up to 26,000 N."
		"Copper nozzles overheat and break at high thrust; titanium nozzles do not — one more reason titanium comes first."
		"Parallel engines balance fluids automatically. Wear engineer goggles to read thrust, efficiency and specific impulse live."
	]
	quest.4BADFA04EF810F23.quest_subtitle: "Rocket engineering, advanced course"
	quest.4BADFA04EF810F23.title: "Engine Cycles"
	quest.4BFBFADA2F05761D.quest_desc: [
		"Once a copper ingot is heated enough, its temperature reads \\\"Weldable\\\" — meaning it can be welded at this heat. Welding fuses two ingots into a double ingot for more advanced work."
		""
		"Take copper double ingots: place two weldable copper ingots in a stone anvil with a hammer and one flux, then click the weld button on the right. Flux is crafted from a hammer plus calcium-carbonate items — limestone, dolomite, or chalk rocks."
	]
	quest.4BFBFADA2F05761D.quest_subtitle: "A quest of the same name exists in the \\\"Smithing Guide\\\" side chapter"
	quest.4BFBFADA2F05761D.title: "Welding"
	quest.4C0F061FE6239576.quest_desc: [
		"The drying mat sun-dries items. Dried fruit keeps twice as long; dried thatch blocks can be composted."
		""
		"Drying mats need sunlight to work. In rain or snow they stop and all progress resets."
	]
	quest.4C0F061FE6239576.quest_subtitle: "Humanity's first use of solar power"
	quest.4C395797A48CBFFF.quest_desc: [
		"As a tech mod, Create naturally has a fluid transport system for moving fluids automatically."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the \\\"Fluid Transport\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.4C395797A48CBFFF.title: "Fluid Transport"
	quest.4C42A21E7B59CC9F.quest_desc: [
		"Since you've opened this quest, you're ready to experience this modpack. The quest line will help you as much as it can. Good luck."
		""
		"&l&4Note: this version's quest line is not fully finished — a few spots may diverge from actual gameplay. When in doubt, trust the TerraFirma field guide and the game itself!"
	]
	quest.4C42A21E7B59CC9F.quest_subtitle: "Where am I? Why can't I punch trees? Why is my health bar so long?? What are those blue and green bars on the right?? Why is the ground covered in rocks and sticks??"
	quest.4C42A21E7B59CC9F.title: "Arrival on TerraFirma"
	quest.4C79708B45817652.quest_subtitle: "Limestone \\& marble at y=20~80"
	quest.4C79708B45817652.title: "Lapis Lazuli"
	quest.4C915E1A95A2EB1A.quest_desc: [
		"Steel pipes and the steel pump can move fluid source blocks. Connect a crank shaft to the narrow end of the pump with steel rods — if you see wooden blocks inside the pump moving with the rods, it's working. Run steel pipes from the pump's bottom to a water source; the pipe's end must sit in water, no more than 16 blocks from the pump."
		""
		"If built correctly, a water source appears at the pump's wide end. One pump tries to fill an enclosed area of up to 32 blocks; anything larger won't be filled."
	]
	quest.4C915E1A95A2EB1A.quest_subtitle: "The only way to move fluid sources in base TFC"
	quest.4D00107C01892548.quest_desc: [
		"For every modpack, the Nether seems unavoidable. The original TerraFirmaCraft: Next Generation offered no way there — but through addon mods, this pack makes the trip possible."
		""
		"The addons add new content to the Nether: you can enjoy most vanilla Nether features alongside TFC-flavored additions — mining TFC ores in the Nether, growing new Nether crops the TFC way, even building a gigantic forge from new Nether blocks."
	]
	quest.4D00107C01892548.quest_subtitle: "What lies beneath your feet?"
	quest.4D00107C01892548.title: "Below TerraFirma"
	quest.4D4464605DAA18DC.quest_subtitle: "Sedimentary rock near the surface"
	quest.4D4464605DAA18DC.title: "Bituminous Coal"
	quest.4D519734EF3819FC.quest_desc: [
		"In MC, most mods measure fluid in B (Buckets) — a unit based on the iron bucket, so both the iron bucket and the TFC wooden bucket hold 1B."
		""
		"Then, like liters and milliliters in real life, the milli-bucket (mB, lowercase) appeared: 1B = 1000mB. It's the most common unit today, and it'll be invaluable once you start working with fluid recipes."
	]
	quest.4D519734EF3819FC.title: "Fluid Units"
	quest.4D54513E21ADC4B6.quest_desc: [
		"You can melt ore directly, but that loses 5mB of metal. Or you can process the ore a bit first — more steps, but some byproducts too. Later, advanced ore processing will raise yields further."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the \\\"Ore Processing\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.4D54513E21ADC4B6.title: "Ore Processing"
	quest.4DC9620F74CF73F0.quest_desc: [
		"The andesite funnel outputs items from a container as drops, or inserts drops into a container. A redstone signal controls whether it works."
		""
		"The arrow on it shows its input/output mode; change the mode with a wrench."
		""
		"A funnel can accept unlimited items at once, but only outputs one item at a time."
	]
	quest.4DC9620F74CF73F0.title: "Basic Logistics"
	quest.4DECDC947436829D.quest_desc: [
		"Chromium is a steel-tier metal. It can be obtained through normal ore processing, but must be forged on a steel anvil. Chromium sheets can replace wrought iron sheets for cladding the blast furnace."
	]
	quest.4DECDC947436829D.title: "Chromium Ingot"
	quest.4E1DA53A0BC4CEF5.quest_desc: [
		"Water can't exist as a block in the Nether, yet you still need to drink. Luckily, water sealed in a barrel won't vanish there — so carry a full barrel of water, even though it speeds up hunger and thirst drain."
		""
		"Another option is the water bag: insert the mushrooms found everywhere in the Nether to convert them into water at a 1:50mB ratio. Note the mushrooms must not be rotten."
	]
	quest.4E1DA53A0BC4CEF5.quest_subtitle: "See those mushrooms? Beat them up."
	quest.4E1DA53A0BC4CEF5.title: "Preparation: Water"
	quest.4E73C5BC16FA0E74.quest_subtitle: "High altitude, above y=80, intrusive rock"
	quest.4E73C5BC16FA0E74.title: "Cassiterite"
	quest.4EC0DE11FE000001.quest_desc: [
		"This chapter measures electricity in watts (W), while Immersive Engineering uses FE. The power converter exchanges between the two grids in both directions: roughly 24W equals 1FE/t, with a per-unit cap of 100kW."
		"Want to feed this chapter's abundant generation into IE's arc furnace? Or rescue the grid with a diesel generator instead? Place a converter and wire up both sides."
	]
	quest.4EC0DE11FE000001.quest_subtitle: "The bridge between two grids"
	quest.4EC0DE11FE000001.title: "Power Converter"
	quest.4EF8B05F318CA79E.quest_subtitle: "Sedimentary rock near the surface"
	quest.4EF8B05F318CA79E.title: "Lignite"
	quest.4F69388DB45DEB39.quest_desc: [
		"Mud brick blocks are built from mud bricks — craft mud with straw into wet mud bricks and leave them on the ground to dry for a day. Note that rain stops the drying."
		""
		"Once your industry is going, batch it instead: wet mud bricks dry right in a smoker; better yet, run a Create encased fan across fire — it recognizes smoking recipes and blow-dries a whole stack at once, rain or shine."
	]
	quest.4F69388DB45DEB39.title: "Mud Bricks"
	quest.5034E5C35DD76F0F.quest_desc: [
		"Whether or not you've actually found a base, you're ready for what's next."
		""
		"In this chapter you'll master most stone tools, learn to make and use pottery, and use pottery for basic metal smelting — yielding the material that opens the next chapter: copper."
	]
	quest.5034E5C35DD76F0F.quest_subtitle: "Learn copper smelting and enter the Copper Age"
	quest.5034E5C35DD76F0F.title: "Chapter 2 — Chapter Goals"
	quest.5088AD0665847EE1.quest_desc: [
		"Native copper powder and copper nuggets contain 5mB of copper each, while casting one copper tool takes 100mB. That's twenty portions of powder."
	]
	quest.5088AD0665847EE1.title: "A Little Powder"
	quest.50B4DD5D3C3AE184.quest_desc: [
		"Yes, waterwheels are cheap and easy to build, and easy to spam. But beware — huge numbers of waterwheels hammer the renderer. Don't blow up your PC."
	]
	quest.50B4DD5D3C3AE184.quest_subtitle: "The sweet smell of GPU"
	quest.50B4DD5D3C3AE184.title: "Stacking Waterwheels"
	quest.50C66853953ED13E.quest_desc: [
		"Your nutrition is determined by five categories: grain, fruit, vegetables, protein, and dairy. Each contributes proportionally to your max health — at full nutrition, your max HP is 3000."
		""
		"Each category grows by eating matching foods, but only your last 20 meals are remembered. To maximize health, eat nutritious and varied food."
	]
	quest.50C66853953ED13E.title: "Nutrition"
	quest.50CACCF2DA505DBE.quest_desc: [
		"Charcoal is an efficient fuel, burning up to &eYellow-White**&f."
		""
		"To make charcoal, build a charcoal pit: place log piles, seal them up leaving one cell exposed, light that cell and seal it too. Smoke drifting out means success."
		""
		"Beware: if the pit's cap blocks are gravity-affected, they collapse the moment burning finishes and destroy the charcoal. Early on, cap the pit with clay blocks or mud bricks."
	]
	quest.5105F3A8FA8B8991.quest_desc: [
		"The Create: Electrical Engineering addon converts Create's rotational stress into electricity usable by other tech mods — efficiently — letting it interface with Immersive Engineering."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the \\\"Create: Electrical Engineering\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.5105F3A8FA8B8991.title: "Create: Electrical Engineering"
	quest.51119806AB5BC1FB.quest_desc: [
		"This is an optional quest — if you haven't finished the previous chapter, completing this unlocks what comes after."
	]
	quest.51463A1030EFCD0D.quest_desc: [
		"With a stone axe you can get logs — but for now, logs are all you get. Planks require a later stage."
	]
	quest.51463A1030EFCD0D.title: "Chopping Trees"
	quest.51B901F8B8D878AC.quest_desc: [
		"The knife deals piercing damage and is an extremely versatile tool. Early on it's mainly used to break plants — some plants only drop items when broken with a knife."
	]
	quest.51B901F8B8D878AC.title: "Stone Knife"
	quest.51D48CEFF7CABA0D.quest_desc: [
		"This is the real iron ingot — nearly identical to vanilla in use, with similar tool performance. But before you start using it, you'd better make an anvil first."
	]
	quest.51D48CEFF7CABA0D.quest_subtitle: "Everything has its limit — iron ore cannot be beaten into gold. — Mark Twain"
	quest.5262E6B3F0A4C72F.quest_desc: [
		"The super shovel digs dirt and sand blocks in a 3x3 area, but its durability drains proportionally."
	]
	quest.5262E6B3F0A4C72F.title: "Super Shovel"
	quest.528D8FB5A7903F41.quest_desc: [
		"The directional receiver attenuates the signal by angle to the source: full strength dead ahead, nothing from behind — handy for automatic homing."
		"The modulated receiver attenuates by distance instead: set a minimum and maximum range and the signal varies linearly with distance — great material for a simple ranging radar."
	]
	quest.528D8FB5A7903F41.quest_subtitle: "Direction and distance of signals"
	quest.528D8FB5A7903F41.title: "Link Receivers"
	quest.52A78A36C47026C0.quest_desc: [
		"The shovel works like vanilla — it digs dirt and sand blocks."
	]
	quest.52A78A36C47026C0.title: "Stone Shovel"
	quest.52AAAE7D38BCC11B.quest_desc: [
		"With seven copper double ingots you can make a copper anvil. It requires a crafting table, and can forge copper ingots or weld copper alloys."
		""
		"You can start experimenting with forging copper now — or save the anvil for when you weld copper alloys."
	]
	quest.52AAAE7D38BCC11B.quest_subtitle: "You'll make one of these at every tier"
	quest.52B6A3277A603A50.quest_desc: [
		"Jam is a fruit product, made by boiling fruit with sugar water in a pot, then ladling it into lidded glass jars. It keeps longer than fruit but has almost no nutrition, and the lids are expensive. Not recommended efficiency-wise."
	]
	quest.52B6A3277A603A50.quest_subtitle: "The most useless episode"
	quest.52B6A3277A603A50.title: "Jam"
	quest.52DA99CB3706297B.quest_desc: [
		"Made by churning salt with cream. It shares some recipes with liquid oils, and mostly serves as an ingredient for other foods."
	]
	quest.52E9C7D0D7DD3379.quest_desc: [
		"In the TerraFirma world, mining rock with a pick drops rocks, not blocks. To get a whole raw stone block, find a natural rock (not hardened) and isolate it — it will then &mdie of loneliness&r and drop as an item."
		""
		"In short: dig out all six blocks surrounding a natural rock and you'll get the rock. Watch out for cave-ins along the way."
	]
	quest.52E9C7D0D7DD3379.quest_subtitle: "Do stones die of loneliness too?"
	quest.52E9C7D0D7DD3379.title: "One Hundred Years of Solitude"
	quest.52E9D69037FA9CC6.quest_desc: [
		"To knap rocks into stone tools, hold at least two rocks and right-click to open the knapping interface. There you shape a 5x5 layer of stone into specific patterns to get tools. Check the field guide for knapping recipes, or use JEI."
	]
	quest.52E9D69037FA9CC6.title: "Stone Knapping"
	quest.53072FE9D8040846.quest_desc: [
		"Polished rose quartz is the foundation of smart machines: craft rose quartz from quartz and redstone, then hold sandpaper in your off-hand and hold right-click."
		""
		"Note: TFC sandpaper and Create sandpaper do not share recipes."
	]
	quest.53072FE9D8040846.quest_subtitle: "Crystal clear"
	quest.534302DF25F41154.quest_desc: [
		"Direct smelting loses 5mB of metal — over 15% waste for a 30mB rich ore."
		""
		"If you don't mind the loss, direct smelting works fine. Or you can learn the ore-processing steps — more trouble, but with byproducts."
		""
		"In the Copper Age you can make wooden gears to drive querns with TFC's transmission devices, and use wooden funnels to collect sluice drops — semi-automatic processing."
		""
		"Once Create is unlocked, advanced ore processing raises yields to 250%."
	]
	quest.534302DF25F41154.title: "Ore Processing"
	quest.536B325277444A5F.quest_desc: [
		"The barrel is a fluid container holding 10000mB of a single fluid, and can run the barrel recipes in JEI. Note: if a recipe would leave two fluids in the barrel, it won't run."
		""
		"Metal barrels exist too — they hold two fluids wooden barrels can't: sulfuric acid and lemon juice. The blue steel barrel can even hold lava, serving as a trash can."
	]
	quest.536B325277444A5F.title: "Barrel"
	quest.5375F4D5C6207816.quest_subtitle: "Extrusive \\& intrusive rock, -64~60, more at depth"
	quest.5375F4D5C6207816.title: "Native Gold"
	quest.53EBC57A2404CC13.quest_desc: [
		"Seal aggregate with dye to get concrete powder of that color, then let it touch water to become concrete."
	]
	quest.540385BF2750046C.quest_desc: [
		"Bees with maxed crop affinity supply all three nutrients to every farmland block in at least an 11x3x11 area. With enough bees, the supply rate can even match crop consumption — late-game beekeeping means no more fertilizing."
	]
	quest.540385BF2750046C.quest_subtitle: "Who needs fertilizer?"
	quest.540385BF2750046C.title: "Crop Affinity"
	quest.54149DFBE04F9DCE.quest_desc: [
		"The modpack has an international community on Discord — share your experience, ask for help, report bugs, give feedback, and get resources and news. Read the announcements when you join!"
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Join our Discord\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://discord.gg/Fc7v5EXmkK\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
	]
	quest.54149DFBE04F9DCE.quest_subtitle: "Discussion is welcome"
	quest.54149DFBE04F9DCE.title: "Community"
	quest.5417DFB03897C1A0.quest_desc: [
		"The smart propeller auto-pitches along a single axis, striving to keep the prop facing upward; the gyroscopic propeller bearing keeps the prop vertical at all times — the key to building helicopters. A helicopter on a plain propeller bearing will flip itself over for you."
		"Placed facing downward, the gyroscopic bearing also stabilizes top-heavy structures; a redstone signal resets the tilt to zero."
	]
	quest.5417DFB03897C1A0.quest_subtitle: "Self-righting"
	quest.5417DFB03897C1A0.title: "Smart Propeller"
	quest.5422D3DA32695947.quest_desc: [
		"Craft gem powder with a brass rod to get the gem saw. It has Silk Touch on glass — before you get the enchantment, it's the only tool that breaks glass and keeps the drop."
	]
	quest.5422D3DA32695947.quest_subtitle: "Silk Touch I"
	quest.543F2A726CFEC300.quest_desc: [
		"To blow, face forward with the blowpipe in hand and right-click; to stretch, face straight down. Careful not to blow over a casting basin or table."
	]
	quest.543F2A726CFEC300.title: "Blowing \\& Stretching"
	quest.54427CE3F2BA4109.quest_desc: [
		"Some blocks mounted on contraptions are recognized as storage."
		""
		"Contraptions can access their contents: machines on the contraption can use items stored inside, blocks broken by the contraption go straight into them, and some devices can pull items out of them directly."
	]
	quest.54427CE3F2BA4109.title: "Storage on Contraptions"
	quest.5497D68A7D7C8F81.quest_desc: [
		"Most copper tools and copper ingots contain 100mB of copper, so molds hold 100mB too. Casting one copper tool takes at least 100mB of copper."
	]
	quest.5497D68A7D7C8F81.title: "Firing Molds"
	quest.549EF07E17716D0C.quest_desc: [
		"Circuits always have accidents: shorts, overloads, a slip of the wiring. A fuse blows when current exceeds its rating, sacrificing itself to save the whole network."
		"Hold the fuse and Ctrl-scroll to set its trip current; slot it into a fuse holder in series with the circuit and it's live."
		"Make it a habit: put a properly rated fuse on every branch. A burnt fuse beats a burnt generator."
	]
	quest.549EF07E17716D0C.quest_subtitle: "The seatbelt of circuits"
	quest.549EF07E17716D0C.title: "Fuse"
	quest.54A3AD0FC2415D1E.quest_desc: [
		"The main protein foods are meat and fish. Before actual processing, they can be crafted with salt or a salt lick to be salted. After salting comes normal brining."
		""
		"Before pickling there's also a smoking step: place up to four blocks of wool yarn above a campfire (no pot or grill), light it, and hang the salted meat on the yarn."
		""
		"Eight hours later the meat comes down, ready for pickling and storage."
	]
	quest.54A3AD0FC2415D1E.title: "Protein — Meat"
	quest.54A6F21FD436B7A2.quest_desc: [
		"The large vessel is a nine-slot container that stores items of normal size or smaller."
		""
		"Sneak-right-click to seal it so it keeps its contents when broken. \\\"Extremely large, very heavy\\\" — carrying one inflicts debuffs."
		""
		"Food in a sealed vessel gains the \\\"Preserved\\\" buff, doubling its shelf life. In an unsealed vessel, rats will come eat your food."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the \\\"Food Preservation\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.54DE12BD51525A1F.quest_desc: [
		"Proper bread needs yeast to ferment. To get yeast, seal dried fruit with fresh water in a barrel — each fruit yields 100mB of yeast. Afterwards, sealing flour with yeast multiplies it."
	]
	quest.54DE12BD51525A1F.quest_subtitle: "Fermentation"
	quest.54DE12BD51525A1F.title: "Yeast"
	quest.551595D5332986B2.quest_desc: [
		"Mix black steel, steel, bismuth bronze, and sterling silver in the right proportions to get weak blue steel."
	]
	quest.551595D5332986B2.quest_subtitle: "Blue steel, lite edition"
	quest.553B6BDFE376C572.quest_desc: [
		"Cookie dough must be made in a mixing bowl — three kinds of cookies in total. Cookie dough can only be baked in an oven."
	]
	quest.553B6BDFE376C572.title: "Cookies"
	quest.5541E2C6DB0A43E7.quest_desc: [
		"The rotation speed controller adjusts speed precisely. Requires a large cogwheel to work."
	]
	quest.559339871A4A7287.quest_desc: [
		"Early-game flint no longer comes from breaking gravel. It generates like rocks on freshwater lakebeds and shallow riverbeds. Flint cannot be knapped into tools — it is a key fire-starting material: combine it with pyrite for a flint-and-pyrite, or with an iron ingot for flint and steel."
	]
	quest.55949E9ACBE9E133.quest_desc: [
		"Combine four ore pieces to get a cluster of ore."
	]
	quest.55949E9ACBE9E133.title: "Ore Cluster"
	quest.55A61A306BAB68A8.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click dirt-type blocks with a mattock to compact them into half-height blocks — roads can only be laid on compacted ground. You'll also need road base gravel and filler."
		""
		"Lay the road base gravel on compacted ground, then spread filler on top to form a road."
		""
		"Basic fillers are sandy and gravel filler, each giving a 15% speed boost. You can also lay two layers of gravel filler and compact them for a 35% gravel road."
	]
	quest.55A61A306BAB68A8.quest_subtitle: "Still a bit rough on the feet"
	quest.55A61A306BAB68A8.title: "Basic Roads"
	quest.55AC70FCD93F2F64.quest_desc: [
		"Glass blowpipe in main hand with a saw in the off-hand performs sawing; the jack performs pressing."
	]
	quest.55AC70FCD93F2F64.title: "Saw \\& Jack"
	quest.55B61AF8ADD0794C.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have wrought iron you can use vanilla chests — free of TFC's size and weight limits, purely vanilla flavor."
	]
	quest.55CD54B87E4D036C.quest_desc: [
		"Boil soybeans with brine to get soybean mixture."
	]
	quest.55F5B1391DA681D5.quest_desc: [
		"On contraptions, the mechanical saw runs no recipes — it only breaks wooden blocks. But it consumes no stress."
		""
		"If the contraption has storage, drops are transferred into it."
	]
	quest.5635F6BCFB5B4838.quest_subtitle: "Above y=40, sedimentary \\& metamorphic rock beneath riverbeds"
	quest.5635F6BCFB5B4838.title: "Amethyst"
	quest.566687685C6612A2.quest_desc: [
		"The charcoal forge is a mid-to-late-game facility for heating high-demand items like pottery and metals — not food. The middle ten slots take fuel and materials; the right side takes containers."
		""
		"It demands coal-type fuel — charcoal or coal. Don't use it until you have plenty."
		""
		"Dig a one-block pit, line its four sides (not the top) with cobblestone, place seven charcoal inside and light it. One block of open sky is required within the 5x5 area above it."
		""
		"Once the forge is built, light it once more to complete the quest."
	]
	quest.566687685C6612A2.title: "Charcoal Forge"
	quest.56688B070F76C2CF.quest_desc: [
		"Every device that can take stress has visible cogs or shafts — those are its connection points."
		""
		"Transmission means linking those points between stress sources and machines with transmission devices. You only need to connect them correctly — and avoid overloading the network."
	]
	quest.56688B070F76C2CF.title: "Transmission"
	quest.568E34E1A29A4085.quest_desc: [
		"A sandwich is crafted from two slices of bread, three fillings in between, and a knife. It keeps 50% of the bread's nutrition and 80% of the fillings', with its own shelf life."
	]
	quest.568E34E1A29A4085.title: "Sandwich"
	quest.56E3622EF6FA195E.quest_desc: [
		"The earlier devices simply move contraptions; these next ones put contraptions to clearly defined work."
	]
	quest.56E3622EF6FA195E.title: "Functional Devices"
	quest.56EF78C5DC998A39.quest_desc: [
		"Alright, time to truly begin"
		"— or would you rather stay and read some fairly useful info first?"
		""
		"As a large hardcore survival mod, TerraFirmaCraft changes many things — including Minecraft's underlying mechanics. For instance, you may have noticed: most blocks in the TerraFirma world, unlike vanilla's anti-gravity blocks, fall."
		""
		"There are many more mechanics like this. For details, consult the book, or read the lengthy texts in the following quests. You can also come back later — these quests will wait for you here."
	]
	quest.56EF78C5DC998A39.quest_subtitle: "Knowing the world is the basis of changing it"
	quest.56EF78C5DC998A39.title: "Know the World"
	quest.56F3357472C284D4.quest_desc: [
		"The most versatile high-heat fuel — the charcoal forge, bloomery, and blast furnace all need it. Burn anything that fits in a log pile inside a charcoal pit, or, from the Iron Age on, use a coke oven."
	]
	quest.574AFF66679FF027.quest_desc: [
		"The elevator pulley works like the rope pulley, but its main job is building elevators. It needs constant stress input, in no particular direction."
		""
		"Build an elevator structure below the pulley, with contact redstone signal generators and a contraption controller."
		""
		"Once built, right-click the elevator pulley to create the elevator. Every matching block that can dock with the signal generators becomes an elevator anchor, recording a floor."
		""
		"Activate an anchor with a redstone signal, or pick a floor on the controller, to send the elevator there."
	]
	quest.57768FB38825611D.quest_desc: [
		"In the Copper Age you can build boilers and refrigerators to raise or lower the temperature in an area."
		""
		"The boiler burns combustibles — planks, charcoal — as fuel."
		""
		"The refrigerator takes cold items, or clay blocks, as refrigerant."
		""
		"Put a chimney on top of either and activate it with redstone to heat or cool the surroundings."
	]
	quest.57848BD26ABF0A51.quest_desc: [
		"Place a soaked hide on a log with right-click, then right-click with a knife until its surface fully changes color to get a scraped hide. Soak the scraped hide in fresh water again for a prepared hide. After that, you'll need tannin."
		""
		"Tannin takes at least 1000mB of fresh water plus any amount of softwood — birch, Douglas fir, oak, sequoia, hickory, chestnut, or maple. Every 1000mB of water consumes one log and yields 1000mB of tannin."
	]
	quest.57848BD26ABF0A51.quest_subtitle: "Soak and soak, scrape and scrape"
	quest.57848BD26ABF0A51.title: "Tanning Leather"
	quest.5784D52F2EECFFBF.quest_desc: [
		"Chain drives connected in parallel transmit stress. Hold a wrench and right-click any number of gearboxes to rotate them without breaking the connection."
	]
	quest.57C85AE49C68DE22.quest_desc: [
		"Pair the boring head bearing with rock-milling wheels and you get a walking mobile tunnel-borer: the wheels auto-stick to each other, breaking every block in range at once, drops flowing into containers on the structure; when they're full it stops."
		"Its output speed is a quarter of the input, in reverse; the more blocks to dig, the slower it goes — add more bearing sets to share the load."
	]
	quest.57C85AE49C68DE22.quest_subtitle: "The Foolish Old Man simulator"
	quest.57C85AE49C68DE22.title: "Tunnel-Boring Drill"
	quest.57E5109A0CB2FC03.quest_desc: [
		"A blaze cake makes the blaze burner work in superheated mode for a good long while."
	]
	quest.57E5109A0CB2FC03.quest_subtitle: "Whoa, it's burning up!"
	quest.57E5109A0CB2FC03.title: "Superheated Burning"
	quest.5825DCEF4C80B843.quest_desc: [
		"The longest-lived heat source. Compared to the pit kiln, its edge is melting high-melting-point metals. The container slot on the right lets molten metal flow straight into molds, and allows fine-tuning alloy ratios inside small vessels."
		""
		"Pair it with bellows to hold the charcoal forge at its peak: white-hot."
	]
	quest.5825DCEF4C80B843.title: "Charcoal Forge"
	quest.5897ED90F5479263.quest_desc: [
		"Unhardened oven blocks need heating. Place some logs in the oven base and light them; after a while the oven blocks harden, their texture turning from clay brick to red brick."
		""
		"Besides bread, the oven can bake other things — though not as well as a grill. Items inside must be taken out with a peel."
	]
	quest.5897ED90F5479263.quest_subtitle: "Pottery has been carrying all along"
	quest.5897ED90F5479263.title: "Hardening Up"
	quest.58B6D43ABBD7C9FD.quest_desc: [
		"A vector thruster gimbals its nozzle under side redstone control, steering the rocket without extra RCS blocks."
		"RCS thrusters run on compressed gas and fine-tune attitude in vacuum. Vector inside the atmosphere, RCS above it — you need both."
		"Three iron rules of rocket building: keep the center of mass centered, keep thrusters symmetrical, and keep thrust-to-weight between 1 and 1.5 — below 1 you never leave the pad, above 1.8 you tumble and break apart."
		"Warning: do NOT mount an Aeronautics gyroscope on your rocket. It locks the attitude and makes every vector thruster useless."
		"Want finer control? A computer can take over the gimbal — see the Flight Computer quest nearby."
	]
	quest.58B6D43ABBD7C9FD.quest_subtitle: "The rocket's steering wheel"
	quest.58B6D43ABBD7C9FD.title: "Vectoring \\& Attitude Control"
	quest.58CA9F3CFFBF9F48.quest_desc: [
		"You've got 14 steel ingots waiting already, haven't you?"
	]
	quest.58CA9F3CFFBF9F48.quest_subtitle: "Time you learned to plan ahead"
	quest.58FC62BF4D2DF3B1.quest_subtitle: "Quartzite, granite, schist, gneiss deep underground"
	quest.58FC62BF4D2DF3B1.title: "Cinnabar"
	quest.5979F68E21EE3E30.quest_desc: [
		"For Create, plain text tutorials sometimes fall short — you need illustrated, animated ones. Create ships a built-in tutorial system: hover any item that says \\\"Hold W to Ponder\\\" and hold W to enter the official interactive guide."
	]
	quest.5979F68E21EE3E30.quest_subtitle: "I reckon this'll work"
	quest.5979F68E21EE3E30.title: "Ponder"
	quest.597A3BAD284A1B8F.quest_desc: [
		"Food is heaven to mortals: skip meals and you starve, starving lowers your max HP, and unbalanced nutrition lowers it too. So eat not only enough, but well!"
	]
	quest.597A3BAD284A1B8F.quest_subtitle: "A caveman who can't cook is no good TerraFirma player"
	quest.597A3BAD284A1B8F.title: "Chef's Guide"
	quest.598D35828347926B.quest_desc: [
		"Some fruits and vegetables can be juiced — place an open barrel beneath a quern to catch the liquid."
	]
	quest.598D35828347926B.title: "Juicing"
	quest.59B8A8468EEC484D.quest_desc: [
		"Magma blocks by volcanoes, hot springs, and lava are natural heat sources."
		""
		"Magma blocks are the most portable, but seem to lose effect over time. Hot spring water works best and even heals you, but is hard to transport. Lava heats the most dramatically — with equally dramatic drawbacks."
	]
	quest.59B8A8468EEC484D.title: "Natural Heat Sources"
	quest.59D598D486914B1D.quest_desc: [
		"The smart chute upgrades the chute: pulls a full stack at once, with freely adjustable input/output amounts and item filtering. But smart chutes can't connect diagonally."
	]
	quest.5A304CBBF873084F.quest_desc: [
		"Create's schematic system lets you copy-paste an area of blocks."
		""
		"First, make a schematic with the Schematic and Quill: right-click two blocks to mark a cuboid selection. Saving creates an nbt file in the \\\"version folder/schematics\\\" directory. To share a schematic, just send the file."
		""
		"Deploying one needs the schematic table and the schematicannon. Select your schematic at the table, insert it, and wait for the import. Then pick a spot to deploy, and finally load the schematic into the schematicannon."
		""
		"Put a book or clipboard into the cannon to get the material list; it automatically pulls items from containers within four blocks. Once materials are ready, add gunpowder to power the cannon — one gunpowder prints 399 blocks. Hit start and the cannon begins printing, at roughly one to two blocks per second."
	]
	quest.5A304CBBF873084F.quest_subtitle: "A builder's blessing"
	quest.5A304CBBF873084F.title: "Schematic System"
	quest.5A71C0B2E9D34F01.quest_desc: [
		"Where tires bog down — mud, rough slopes — tracks keep going. The track mount is the backbone: right-click it with a suspension track or track drive wheel to attach, and once the drive wheel gets rotational power, it drives every connected track segment."
		"Then tune the whole assembly with the suspension key: right-click air to cycle modes (strength, spring, damping, grip and more), right-click a mount to apply. Position mode nudges track offsets; reset mode restores defaults."
		"Only the small track and drive wheel can be mass-produced for now — the bigger tracks aren't finished by the mod author yet, so don't hold your breath."
	]
	quest.5A71C0B2E9D34F01.quest_subtitle: "Where wheels fail, tracks prevail"
	quest.5A71C0B2E9D34F01.title: "Traveling on Tracks"
	quest.5A5CAC4313674D3D.quest_desc: [
		"The industrial squeezer presses plant seeds into plant oil, and converts coke powder or graphite powder into highly oriented pyrolytic graphite powder at 8:1."
		""
		"All seeds yield the same — a fixed 80mB of plant oil per portion. No need to pick varieties; just stockpile and press. Plant oil is the key ingredient of biofuel."
	]
	quest.5A5CAC4313674D3D.quest_subtitle: "No street lamps in the TerraFirma world"
	quest.5A5CAC4313674D3D.title: "Endless Pressing"
	quest.5A60D485AF132B1A.quest_desc: [
		"The crafting blueprint enables quick crafting. It can be placed on any face of a block, following the same placement rules as vanilla paintings. One blueprint provides 1, 4, or 9 recipes at a time."
		""
		"Right-click the blueprint to configure recipes; the recipe then displays on it, and right-clicking consumes items from your inventory to craft automatically."
	]
	quest.5AA66C0488CCD153.quest_desc: [
		"The most powerful stress source. See the \\\"Stress \\& Transmission Devices\\\" side chapter for usage."
	]
	quest.5AACBBDDE7A39F4C.quest_desc: [
		"The oven has several accessories. The ash collector block automatically gathers the ash it produces, while the oven hopper automates log input."
		""
		"Oven insulation lets the oven base work independently, so you can put a grill and a pot on the oven — saving fuel."
		""
		"If you like, three finishes change the oven's texture for decoration."
	]
	quest.5AACBBDDE7A39F4C.title: "Multiblock Kitchen"
	quest.5ABB6D4AA0F9C3E4.quest_desc: [
		"Being rotational, stress comes in two directions: clockwise and counterclockwise. Direction affects some devices — conveyor belts, for one."
		""
		"Devices spinning in different directions cannot connect; forcing it will violently break part of the connection."
	]
	quest.5ABB6D4AA0F9C3E4.title: "Direction of Stress"
	quest.5AC7E0544016909D.quest_desc: [
		"In TerraFirma you can't punch trees barehanded — making crafting tables and wooden tools impossible."
		""
		"Luckily you still know some ancestral crafts. See the rocks and sticks scattered everywhere? Gather some, and let's knap stone tools."
	]
	quest.5AC7E0544016909D.title: "Scavenger"
	quest.5B02A779263E1245.quest_desc: [
		"The bucket-wheel excavator is Immersive Engineering's apex technology — one of the late-game methods for mass ore mining. It's extremely power-hungry at 4096FE/t, so it has three power input points, a redstone control panel, and an output port where you can place storage blocks directly."
		""
		"First use the mineral detector to locate veins, then power the core sample drill to survey the vein's exact composition and richness. Only then build the excavator multiblock to start mining."
		""
		"Rich veins hold more ore and less stone and dirt than poor ones. Judging whether a vein is worth mining is a key call for the operator."
	]
	quest.5B02A779263E1245.quest_subtitle: "Kind of outclassed by Create's drills, honestly"
	quest.5B02A779263E1245.title: "Digging to the Core"
	quest.5B08E6A714006B4D.quest_desc: [
		"The fluid separator extracts fluids from items without any power — generally used to drain containers."
		""
		"It has a curious alternate use: since it works by moving items one block across itself, it can serve as a logistics block in some setups."
	]
	quest.5B08E6A714006B4D.quest_subtitle: "The side use beats the main use"
	quest.5B19B19323DCF81D.quest_desc: [
		"The physics bearing sticks to the block in front; feed it rotation and the whole structure assembles into a physics structure and starts spinning. A redstone signal unlocks it to spin freely. Rotation passes straight through it without interruption."
		"The propeller bearing is its aviation cousin: stick at least two sail-type blocks on its face and you have a working propeller — more sails, more thrust efficiency."
	]
	quest.5B19B19323DCF81D.quest_subtitle: "Get the structure spinning"
	quest.5B19B19323DCF81D.title: "Physics Bearing"
	quest.5B1F744DC1832782.quest_desc: [
		"Who can kill me? Who dares kill me?"
	]
	quest.5B1F744DC1832782.quest_subtitle: "Well fed, well nourished"
	quest.5B1F744DC1832782.title: "&eChallenge: Steve Stands on the Earth"
	quest.5B2FCE4917369975.quest_desc: [
		"You have a body-temperature system, shown by the temperature bar on the right of your inventory. Body heat is affected by time of day, biome, nearby blocks, and season. Abnormal temperature — too cold or too hot — harms you, so staying thermally stable is a major survival concern."
		""
		"The full temperature system is covered in the \\\"Cold Sweat\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.5B2FCE4917369975.quest_subtitle: "You are the legendary king of cold and heat endurance"
	quest.5B2FCE4917369975.title: "Body Temperature"
	quest.5B6105124524CE66.quest_desc: [
		"The blast furnace also burns charcoal, and with enough fuel it burns forever without going out. Toss equal parts iron-bearing items and flux into the chimney to start steelmaking."
		""
		"While it burns, keep feeding fuel so the flame never dies, work the bellows to hold white-hot heat, and watch the tuyere's durability so it never hits zero. A mechanical arm can drive the bellows for you."
	]
	quest.5B6105124524CE66.title: "Steelmaking Essentials"
	quest.5B63FF0A83E0373D.quest_desc: [
		"Dig a two-level pit: 5x5 on top, 3x3 below. Place blackstone water bridges at the four upper corners and flow lava in from outside, line the whole lower level and the four upper edges with nether bricks, fill the middle with 8x9=72 cursed coal, and light it — that's the Nether forge."
		""
		"The Nether forge has 18 slots sharing fuel and materials. The four right slots take containers like the charcoal forge, for molten metal. It supports crucibles and bellows like the charcoal forge — but only in the center slot."
	]
	quest.5B63FF0A83E0373D.quest_subtitle: "Until you make external heaters, this is the best furnace"
	quest.5B63FF0A83E0373D.title: "Nether Forge"
	quest.5B932369EEB60656.quest_desc: [
		"Break the grass found everywhere with a knife to get straw. Extremely versatile — gather plenty."
	]
	quest.5B932369EEB60656.quest_subtitle: "Can I have some grass?"
	quest.5B932369EEB60656.title: "Cutting Straw"
	quest.5BB4AB2A25BFA739.quest_desc: [
		"A traditional Mexican staple — corn can be made into tortillas for Mexican dishes."
	]
	quest.5BB99D08032A6CD3.quest_desc: [
		"Connect a vertical shaft to the top of a quern to make it grind automatically — you just drop items in."
	]
	quest.5BB99D08032A6CD3.quest_subtitle: "The first stirrings of automation"
	quest.5BB99D08032A6CD3.title: "Ghost-Powered Quern"
	quest.5C7222F9A6C49487.quest_desc: [
		"The Engineer's Manual contains everything you need to know to play Immersive Engineering."
	]
	quest.5CA2336EA00F02B0.quest_desc: [
		"Dogs and cats can join you on hunts; cats also hunt fish, but can't take large predators. Resting cats will even hunt rats for you automatically."
		""
		"Sneak-right-click opens the pet command panel — most commands are self-explanatory. \\\"We're home\\\" makes the pet treat the surrounding area as home; idle pets will then wander within it."
	]
	quest.5CA2336EA00F02B0.quest_subtitle: "Buddy, let's go!"
	quest.5CA2336EA00F02B0.title: "Good Companions"
	quest.5CE11F6803ECFC83.quest_desc: [
		"The jug holds all kinds of liquids — except lava — with a capacity of 100mB, a tenth of a bucket."
		""
		"You can drink from a full jug of water; each sip consumes 100mB."
	]
	quest.5CF8A7A930D963EB.quest_desc: [
		"Can't burn fuel to heat itself, but inherits the temperature of the charcoal forge beneath it."
	]
	quest.5D23F7FDFBBEEA0F.quest_desc: [
		"The following devices help you control contraptions precisely and build more complex machines."
	]
	quest.5D23F7FDFBBEEA0F.title: "Contraption Control"
	quest.5D2476EFA33AE63A.quest_desc: [
		"The cellar preserves food in bulk — the colder, the longer it keeps. The new cellar no longer needs a weather station: enclose a space with well-insulated blocks and the system recognizes it automatically, granting preservation to containers inside. The sealed blocks and sealed doors that make up a cellar need beeswax to craft."
		""
		"Walls come in three thermal-resistance tiers: high (mud bricks, sealed bricks, supported dirt), medium (stone, cobblestone, dirt, planks, logs, support beams, etc.), low (glass, metal blocks). Build with high-resistance blocks where you can. Doors count as medium, and double doors give a 4x bonus — remember to install double doors. Max size: 15 blocks horizontally, 5 vertically."
		""
		"Preservation starts at 16°C or below, improves at 8°C or below, and is best below 0°C. Digging a cellar in a cold biome gets twice the result with half the effort. Hold a support beam in your main hand and a hammer in your off-hand and right-click dirt or grass to reinforce it into supported dirt — collapse-proof and a top-tier cellar wall."
		""
		"After building, you must place matching containers inside to finish: food shelves preserve most foods, hanging racks preserve meat, and large vessels and cheese wheels benefit too. &4Note: only containers inside a valid space get preservation — outside, they're ordinary furniture.&r A thermometer's redstone signal strength helps you gauge the indoor temperature."
	]
	quest.5D2476EFA33AE63A.quest_subtitle: "Subjective time dilation"
	quest.5D2476EFA33AE63A.title: "Cellar"
	quest.5D6BE2A315BFBD2A.quest_desc: [
		"Cave-in hazards include but are not limited to: destroying ores, burying tunnels, and squashing you flat. Preventing collapses matters. In the current version, you can tell whether the rock you're pointing at will collapse."
		""
		"The simplest method is paving the top layer of the tunnel with anti-gravity blocks — expensive, but reliable."
		""
		"Another is support beams. Note that only horizontal beams support anything, over a 9x5x9 area centered on the beam."
		""
		"Combining both is safest: just place anti-gravity blocks above the support beams."
	]
	quest.5D6BE2A315BFBD2A.quest_subtitle: "When you find yourself in a hole, stop digging. — Will Rogers"
	quest.5D6BE2A315BFBD2A.title: "&cMining Essentials"
	quest.5D95BC05FB558E94.quest_desc: [
		"Mount Sputnik on top of your rocket. Here is the standard launch profile — memorize it:"
		"Phase 1, powered ascent: ignite and climb, then start a gravity turn at safe altitude — pitch toward about 45 degrees to build horizontal velocity."
		"Phase 2, coast: shut down the main engine and keep climbing on inertia. Watch the hologram console — the apex of the parabola is your insertion point."
		"Phase 3, circularization: near the apex, fire again to round the orbit. The periapsis must clear the atmosphere! Firing early only stretches the parabola, it does not circularize."
		"In deep space you can adjust time flow with /rn timescale — speed up the coast phase instead of waiting."
		"This quest only completes when the satellite is truly in orbit — good luck, launch director."
	]
	quest.5D95BC05FB558E94.quest_subtitle: "Space assets +1"
	quest.5D95BC05FB558E94.title: "Launch a Satellite"
	quest.5DB20464EE18F00B.quest_desc: [
		"Mainly used to cook soup, compressing several foods into one meal for more nutrition. Needs water to make soup."
	]
	quest.5DB20464EE18F00B.title: "Pot"
	quest.5DFBD6CE29081618.quest_desc: [
		"The three copper alloys differ in performance: black bronze has the highest durability and damage, bismuth bronze is easiest to source, and bronze tools work the fastest. For armor, black bronze best resists piercing, bismuth bronze best resists blunt force, and bronze balances both."
	]
	quest.5DFBD6CE29081618.quest_subtitle: "Bronze is the mirror of form; wine, of the heart. — Aeschylus"
	quest.5DFBD6CE29081618.title: "Copper Alloys"
	quest.5E1C8A072D4F6B93.quest_desc: [
		"Two toys, complimentary for ambitious orbital engineers."
		""
		"Rivets let you place blocks at any angle, even off-grid — shape your orbital trusses however you like. While placing, follow the item tooltip's keys: rotate in 15° steps, rotate freely, or disable placement snapping."
		""
		"Stick a red balloon to a physics structure and it lifts slightly off the ground, staying upright — handy for moving boats, carts, or houses. Projectiles pop a whole patch of balloons at once; to reclaim them safely, sneak with a wrench."
	]
	quest.5E1C8A072D4F6B93.quest_subtitle: "Acrobatics time"
	quest.5E1C8A072D4F6B93.title: "Rivets \\& Red Balloons"
	quest.5E2ABBBF1C21DBB3.quest_subtitle: "Intrusive, extrusive, or metamorphic rock below y=75"
	quest.5E2ABBBF1C21DBB3.title: "Galena"
	quest.5E2EF32B142A1F00.quest_desc: [
		"The mechanical press runs different recipes in different situations."
		""
		"With a depot, belt, or any solid block two blocks below, it runs pressing recipes — e.g. pressing a copper ingot into a copper sheet. With a basin directly below, it runs compacting recipes, including 2x2 or 3x3 same-item recipes."
	]
	quest.5E2EF32B142A1F00.quest_subtitle: "Smithing? What's smithing?"
	quest.5E2EF32B142A1F00.title: "One Hammer, One Deal"
	quest.5E38466ECBAE7D75.quest_desc: [
		"The walking stick frees you from the drag of snow and grass; the upgraded iron cane has more durability."
	]
	quest.5E48820D1D48EF38.quest_desc: [
		"Most machines and some tools in Immersive Engineering consume electricity. IE's power grid consists of generators, wires, and accumulators."
		""
		"Wires come in low, medium, and high voltage: higher voltage transmits faster with less loss. Each tier has its own connectors and relays — connectors feed machines and take one wire; relays take several. Transformers convert between voltages."
		""
		"Unless insulated, wires damage entities passing through them — the higher the voltage, the deadlier. HV wires are basically one-touch lethal. Only HV wires can't be insulated."
		""
		"Craft the Faraday suit to become immune to wire damage."
	]
	quest.5E48820D1D48EF38.quest_subtitle: "The deadliest content around"
	quest.5E48820D1D48EF38.title: "Power Transmission"
	quest.5E673992EF7CBA4C.quest_desc: [
		"The liming room and the fleshing machine automate leather processing, with automated input and output. The steps mirror TFC's manual ones — put hides of each state plus the matching fluid into the liming room, while the fleshing machine handles the log-scraping step."
		""
		"Machine-processed hides get tagged \\\"Machine-Made\\\"; when a tagged hide finally becomes leather, the yield doubles. But any single step done by hand strips the tag."
	]
	quest.5E673992EF7CBA4C.quest_subtitle: "You'll generally want three liming rooms"
	quest.5E673992EF7CBA4C.title: "Liming Room"
	quest.5EC0DE11FE000002.quest_desc: [
		"Liquid engines too pricey? Solid boosters are the poor astronaut's gospel: believe it or not, they burn coal blocks."
		"Once lit, thrust is maxed — no throttle, no shutdown, discard when spent. Always mount them in symmetric pairs — an off-center booster's torque will spin your rocket like a top."
		"Standard doctrine: strap boosters beside the main engine for the big lift-off kick, blow them away with stage separators once empty, and let the main engine take over the climb."
		"Engine mounts channel that enormous thrust smoothly into the airframe. Don't skip them."
	]
	quest.5EC0DE11FE000002.quest_subtitle: "Brute force works miracles"
	quest.5EC0DE11FE000002.title: "Solid Boosters"
	quest.5ED9F15870E8BD9F.quest_desc: [
		"Create starts from one tiny alloy. With your imagination, this mod lets you build rich and varied automated production lines."
		""
		"Complete this quest to unlock the \\\"Create\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.5ED9F15870E8BD9F.title: "Create"
	quest.5EDC59121C7C0BE5.quest_desc: [
		"The most complete fertilizer, and the richest in nitrogen among easy-to-get ones. Make up the missing phosphorus with bone meal."
	]
	quest.5EDC9490C9358F90.quest_desc: [
		"A wrought iron double sheet can be forged into a wrought iron grill, which sits on a campfire."
		""
		"The grill runs every campfire cooking recipe, heats two items at once, and gives cooked meat the \\\"Log-Grilled\\\" buff — shelf life up 66% versus raw!"
	]
	quest.5EDC9490C9358F90.quest_subtitle: "One craft, a hundred uses"
	quest.5EE8F779D4D53AC8.quest_desc: [
		"To chisel rock, hold a chisel in your main hand and a hammer in your off-hand, then right-click natural rock. This can cause cave-ins — use support beams. Press M with the chisel in hand (rebinding recommended) to switch chisel mode. Don't chisel the wrong thing."
		""
		"The resulting smooth stone works for building and crafting. It's an anti-gravity block — never falls naturally — but cave-ins still affect it."
	]
	quest.5EE8F779D4D53AC8.quest_subtitle: "Can't be used against cave-ins"
	quest.5EE8F779D4D53AC8.title: "Smooth \\& Level"
	quest.5F0253B6892FD526.quest_desc: [
		"Gem powder is ground from gems in a quern — material for the gem saw and one of glassmaking's raw ingredients. Most gems need a steel-or-better pick to mine, with one exception: pyrite. If you have pyrite, put it to work."
		""
		"No pyrite and can't find any? Use the cut gems the quest line gave you earlier — those grind into powder too."
	]
	quest.5F0253B6892FD526.quest_subtitle: "Ground gems have more uses"
	quest.5F0253B6892FD526.title: "Gemworking"
	quest.5F07780C19DAB647.quest_desc: [
		"The bloomery block is the core of the bloomery multiblock. It's essentially a trapdoor, and must be closed while the bloomery runs."
		""
		"For construction, consult the field guide."
	]
	quest.5F30596BED8AEA3E.quest_subtitle: "Shale, slate, and chert near the surface"
	quest.5F30596BED8AEA3E.title: "Sylvite"
	quest.5F3C3C090807C218.quest_desc: [
		"One soap turns 1000mB of fresh water into soapy water — the only thing that can wash containers."
	]
	quest.6050BE2843485525.quest_desc: [
		"Glassblowing needs brass-plated blocks: surround one block of air (except the top) with 5 plated blocks for a casting basin; build a 3x3 platform of 9 for a casting table. The basin casts glass blocks; the table casts glass panes."
	]
	quest.6050BE2843485525.quest_subtitle: "Don't craft brass blocks by mistake"
	quest.6072E13DC350724C.quest_desc: [
		"TerraFirmaCraft's ores fall into four broad classes: metal ores, non-metal minerals, coal, and gems."
		""
		"Metal ores can be processed and melted into ingots; the item shows which metal it becomes."
		""
		"Non-metal minerals are usually ground to powder for processing — gypsum is the exception, worked directly into bricks."
		""
		"Coal comes in only two kinds: bituminous and lignite. Lignite burns like charcoal; bituminous slightly better."
		""
		"Gems are usually cut for decoration, or ground into powder for gem saws, enchanting, and glassmaking. Pyrite is a gem, not an iron ore."
	]
	quest.6072E13DC350724C.quest_subtitle: "In case you didn't read the book"
	quest.6072E13DC350724C.title: "Ores of TerraFirmaCraft"
	quest.6095779F2D508420.quest_desc: [
		"Completing this quest unlocks Chapter 2 directly — or finish the quests below first."
	]
	quest.6095779F2D508420.title: "Chapter 2"
	quest.60DC564F1749B35A.quest_desc: [
		"Water bridges carry water over any distance — fresh, salt, or hot spring water — as long as the bridges connect. A huge help for managing farmland moisture."
		""
		"Note that bridges don't move fluid sources: break the bridge line and the water disappears."
	]
	quest.60DC564F1749B35A.quest_subtitle: "At least no more daily watering"
	quest.60DC564F1749B35A.title: "Water Bridge"
	quest.61145C1D390AB6BB.quest_desc: [
		"Besides eating as fruit, grapes can be brewed into wine. Unlike grain alcohol, wine grants no buffs — you brew it for the joy of brewing."
	]
	quest.61145C1D390AB6BB.title: "Grapes"
	quest.613CD0BFED33D8F2.quest_desc: [
		"A larger charcoal forge requiring Nether materials to build. Same function, bigger capacity."
	]
	quest.613CD0BFED33D8F2.title: "Nether Forge"
	quest.6151CB58369CF50C.quest_desc: [
		"The hammer deals blunt damage and appears in recipes that need \\\"smashing\\\", but its main job is forging and welding on anvils."
		""
		"You need a natural rock as your first anvil — it must be extrusive or intrusive rock. If none near home, completing this quest grants you a few."
		""
		"Completing this quest also unlocks the \\\"Smithing Guide\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.6151CB58369CF50C.quest_subtitle: "Hammered in stone"
	quest.6151CB58369CF50C.title: "Stone Hammer"
	quest.617276B60F099919.quest_desc: [
		"TerraFirma farmland tracks three nutrients: nitrogen, phosphorus, potassium. But crops don't just pick one to eat — they come in four schools:"
		"Legumes (soybeans, peanuts, lentils...): consume P and K, and actually return nitrogen to the soil — the land's benefactor;"
		"Grains (wheat, rice, corn...): devour nitrogen and leave P and K behind — the land's debtor;"
		"Vegetables (tomatoes, radishes...): want all three, but yield the most nutritious food;"
		"Cover crops (alfalfa...): produce all three nutrients — a shame the harvest is barely edible, though it makes fine animal feed."
		"Thrifty farmers know crop rotation: the nitrogen grains eat this year, legumes pay back next year, and the land grows richer with every season."
		"Fertilizer adds nutrients directly — common ones include compost, bone meal, slag, plus some found in specific environments. Check the field guide and JEI for details."
		"Soil itself also comes in grades: good soil boosts fertilizer effect by 20%, poor soil discounts it. Find good land before you start."
	]
	quest.617276B60F099919.title: "Nutrients \\& Fertilizer"
	quest.61730A756764E281.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a thermometer to read ambient temperature, shown on the right of your inventory. You can wear it in the charm curio slot."
	]
	quest.61730A756764E281.quest_subtitle: "Take your temperature"
	quest.61730A756764E281.title: "Thermometer"
	quest.61888AE6092F15D8.quest_desc: [
		"The brass tunnel upgrades the andesite tunnel — freely adjustable splitting ratios and item filtering."
		""
		"Brass tunnels in the same row join into one unit with multiple distribution logics, like splitting input evenly. The config panel above changes the logic — see Ponder for details."
	]
	quest.61A70898D44DA38E.quest_desc: [
		"The TerraFirma world has over a hundred biomes. Some need no mention; others matter a great deal. The important ones:"
		"Plains: mostly in temperate zones, with scattered fruit trees."
		"Tropical plateaus, mountains, and highlands: these three tropical biomes yield kaolinite (crucial!). Shield volcanoes are also great kaolinite spots — look for swathes of blooming blood lilies."
		"Most high mountains: yield hot spring water."
		"Canyons: rich in exposed ore, may lead to caves. If the land is carved into fantastical shapes, that's karst — caves there outnumber anywhere else."
		"Ocean: yields salt water; coasts yield unique coastal resources, and the sea yields ink sacs, whale blubber, and kelp. Coasts vary wildly from place to place — beaches to sea cliffs."
		"Walk to the frozen ends of the earth and you'll find endless ice sheets and glaciers — magnificent and nothing else. Pack provisions before setting out."
	]
	quest.61A70898D44DA38E.quest_subtitle: "Not so different from vanilla MC, really"
	quest.61A70898D44DA38E.title: "Biomes"
	quest.61AE320791B6E084.quest_desc: [
		"Process dried soybeans in a quern or stomping basin to make soybean paste."
	]
	quest.61B12BA8F0C66BF5.quest_desc: [
		"The pit kiln is a heating device that brings items inside to &eYellow-White****&f. Learn to build one by Pondering pottery."
		""
		"No pottery on hand? Then go do the quests along the stone shovel line."
	]
	quest.61B12BA8F0C66BF5.title: "Pit Kiln"
	quest.61EB56B64769566A.quest_desc: [
		"When you die, your nutrition isn't reset — but your items stay on a corpse at the death site, which won't vanish until you recover them."
	]
	quest.61EB56B64769566A.title: "Death Penalty"
	quest.621EBB2650EAE6B1.quest_desc: [
		"The refinery mainly makes biodiesel (mixing seed oil and ethanol), but it can blend other fluids for production too. Refining requires a catalyst — the catalyst isn't consumed, but nothing reacts without it."
		""
		"Two fluids enter the refinery's ends; the mixture exits the middle. Extract with pipes, or scoop it out with a container in the UI. The refinery has a redstone control panel to switch it on and off."
	]
	quest.621EBB2650EAE6B1.title: "Chemical Processing"
	quest.623782A2AD073C26.quest_desc: [
		"Washed sugarcane must be juiced in a quern, with an open barrel beneath it. The juice flows into the barrel while the pressed bagasse stays in the quern — bagasse works as fuel or compost."
		""
		"Boiling any sugarcane juice except clarified juice in a pot gives perishable sugar — the only sugar with a shelf life. Once spoiled, it's no longer usable as sugar."
	]
	quest.623782A2AD073C26.quest_subtitle: "&e5S&f-pressed cane juice"
	quest.623782A2AD073C26.title: "Juicing"
	quest.623B724AD16ACB18.quest_desc: [
		"Once Create is unlocked, the mechanical press replaces the hammer via \\\"sequenced assembly\\\" — andesite rocks appearing mid-recipe are intermediates; just keep pressing them."
		""
		"Note: machines cannot process heated metal. Let hot metal cool before sending it down the line."
	]
	quest.632844FAC1275EE7.quest_desc: [
		"Concrete utility poles have linked terminals at top and bottom; with pole-mounted brackets, they carry wires high into the air, across mountains and buildings."
		"For long-distance transmission remember the three moves: step up the voltage, raise poles, ground along the line. Higher voltage means less current for the same power — and less line loss."
	]
	quest.632844FAC1275EE7.quest_subtitle: "The grid crosses mountains"
	quest.632844FAC1275EE7.title: "Utility Poles"
	quest.633574148FBB5CBF.quest_desc: [
		"The fermenter is how you make ethanol (not drinkable) — from grain, fruit, or vegetables. Rotten produce works too."
		""
		"The fermenter's input face works with hoppers; the output takes pipes to other machines. Usually you can press its output face right against the refinery's input face, skipping pipes and pumps — saving materials and space."
	]
	quest.633574148FBB5CBF.title: "Fermentation"
	quest.63743588B8A5D119.quest_desc: [
		"Food cooked on a grill gains the \\\"Log-Grilled\\\" buff — a bigger shelf-life bonus than the oven gives."
	]
	quest.63743588B8A5D119.title: "Grill"
	quest.63B0A375259D2711.quest_desc: [
		"Wires can't plug straight into machines — connectors at both ends serve as terminals. A normal connector takes one wire; the double connector takes several and is the hub of wiring."
		"A circuit must close a loop: current leaves the positive pole, passes through the load, and returns to the negative. A single wire carries no power."
		"Name a connector with a name tag and its name shows when you point at it — when you're debugging a huge grid someday, you'll thank yourself."
	]
	quest.63B0A375259D2711.quest_subtitle: "Terminals"
	quest.63B0A375259D2711.title: "Connectors"
	quest.63D803AB50F9247D.quest_subtitle: "Granite, gneiss, schist, below y=20"
	quest.63D803AB50F9247D.title: "Native Silver"
	quest.644DD2F6BCFBDA31.quest_desc: [
		"A coal obtainable in the Nether. Burns like charcoal; its main use is building the Nether forge."
	]
	quest.648DA94A24E63FD6.quest_desc: [
		"Create — the romantic, rising tech mod — is already compatible with most TerraFirmaCraft recipes. Playing it, you'll throw most of TFC's recipes into automated production lines."
		""
		"If you've never played Create, this pack's quest line will help you along."
	]
	quest.648DA94A24E63FD6.title: "Welcome to Create"
	quest.64B8D6F8F9F15732.quest_desc: [
		"The mechanical bearing turns the glued area in front of it into a rotating contraption, spinning around the bearing's axis."
		""
		"Once powered, the bearing starts working, spinning the same way as the input. Rotating contraptions pass straight through blocking blocks."
	]
	quest.64B8D6F8F9F15732.title: "It's Spinning"
	quest.64D8DCED4F349CA2.quest_desc: [
		"Attach to the side of a container: right-click with an item in hand to store it; sneak-right-click to store everything in your inventory (excluding equipment, off-hand, and hotbar)."
		""
		"The item hatch has filter slots on its bottom — specify filtered items or insert filters there."
		""
		"The hatch automatically excludes assembled minecarts, shulker boxes, and shulker-like containers (e.g. sophisticated backpacks) — they won't be stored automatically."
	]
	quest.653422DB56395B12.quest_desc: [
		"The clutch is a block that connects or disconnects power under redstone control — while redstone-active, it stays disconnected."
	]
	quest.658F3DB91D05D43A.quest_desc: [
		"The garden cloche grows crops automatically. It needs power and water, and yields both crops and seeds. Add bone meal as fertilizer for 1.25x efficiency."
		""
		"This pack adds full support for TerraFirma-family crops: TFC crops and berry bushes, Firmalife spices and fruits, and Nether crops from Below TerraFirma all grow in the cloche. Wire up power and water, and your late-game farm is done."
	]
	quest.658F3DB91D05D43A.quest_subtitle: "Electric farming"
	quest.65A7A76B0E1D979E.quest_desc: [
		"This covers Create's unique logistics; for other logistics methods, see the \\\"Storage \\& Logistics\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.65A7A76B0E1D979E.title: "Logistics \\& Trains"
	quest.65EA9C50849C6157.quest_desc: [
		"Weld weak blue steel with black steel to get high-carbon blue steel, then work that into blue steel ingots."
		""
		"Blue steel is the highest tier-6 metal, making top-grade gear and weapons with some new recipes. Performance is close to red steel, with slightly more recipes."
	]
	quest.65EA9C50849C6157.quest_subtitle: "&bBlue is the color of indifference"
	quest.65EA9C50849C6157.title: "&9Blue Blues"
	quest.66407ACF80A57EDE.quest_desc: [
		"Mix dough with basil leaves (an herb), salt, and olive or soybean oil for pizza dough. Add tomato sauce, shredded cheese, and up to two meats or vegetables for a raw pizza, then bake it in the oven."
	]
	quest.66407ACF80A57EDE.title: "Does Pineapple Belong on Pizza?"
	quest.6641709BEA5CB4AB.quest_desc: [
		"The TerraFirma world has an Earth-like climate that directly shapes your life. Like Earth's, it's driven by season and geography."
		"Check the second tab on the right of your inventory for time and climate."
		"Temperature: driven by season, latitude, and time of day. Hottest in summer, coldest in winter; hotter the further south, colder the further north; hottest at noon, coldest at midnight. Note the hemispheres have opposite seasons — while you bundle up in the north, southerners are eating watermelon."
		"Humidity (rainfall): tied to geography — generally wetter in the south, near water, and at low altitude. Regions now also have wet and dry seasons: wet-season rainfall can far exceed the yearly average, while dry seasons may see no rain at all. When the wet season comes and how sharp the contrast is varies by region — learn your homeland's temper before farming."
		"Temperature and humidity affect crops, bushes, and fruit trees. In unsuitable conditions, their growth suffers — or they wither entirely."
	]
	quest.6641709BEA5CB4AB.quest_subtitle: "Also documented in middle-school geography textbooks"
	quest.6641709BEA5CB4AB.title: "Climate"
	quest.665E4D6991D4423F.quest_desc: [
		"Vanilla TerraFirmaCraft's storage blocks are frankly useless — fine with TFC alone, but overwhelmed inside a modpack."
		""
		"So this pack adds storage blocks to serve its tech mods. While introducing them, this chapter also covers logistics, to help you play those mods better."
	]
	quest.665E4D6991D4423F.title: "Storage \\& Logistics"
	quest.6683F85B13BEC586.quest_desc: [
		"The beehive keeps bees and produces honey and beeswax. It's made from a straw block, lumber, and honeycombs — it can hold up to a set number of combs inside."
		""
		"With suitable temperature and flowers nearby, each comb has a daily chance to attract a queen — maxing at 5% with fifty flowers around. One queen per comb at most."
		""
		"Every so often, a housed queen attempts two things: breeding and gathering honey."
	]
	quest.6683F85B13BEC586.quest_subtitle: "Buzz~ buzz~ buzz~"
	quest.6683F85B13BEC586.title: "Beekeeping"
	quest.66A9DD15750C952E.quest_desc: [
		"Stress is a rotational force produced by the spinning of generators — the stress sources. Four things to keep in mind:"
		""
		"1. How it's made  2. How it's transmitted  3. Rotation speed  4. Rotation direction"
	]
	quest.66A9DD15750C952E.title: "Power \\& Transmission"
	quest.66E91517B379FE16.quest_desc: [
		"The hopper upgrades the wooden funnel: five storage slots now, and two items per second."
	]
	quest.66E91517B379FE16.title: "Hopper"
	quest.673484CC693D61F0.quest_desc: [
		"You can't reach the End anytime soon — vent your anger on this one first."
	]
	quest.673484CC693D61F0.title: "&eChallenge: Slay the Wither"
	quest.67D2C6C98E9AF653.quest_desc: [
		"Finally, a bed. It passes the night normally and sets your spawn point. Nothing more."
	]
	quest.67D2C6C98E9AF653.quest_subtitle: "Good night, sleep tight"
	quest.67D2C6C98E9AF653.title: "A Warm Bed"
	quest.67E943030D84B61C.quest_desc: [
		"Crop water mainly comes from the farmland's soil moisture, judged simply by distance to a water block: closer is wetter, further is drier."
	]
	quest.67E943030D84B61C.title: "Moisture"
	quest.67FD3D45D45E06CB.quest_desc: [
		"All welding recipes take metal as input, heated to weldable temperature."
		""
		"Metal can be welded on an anvil one tier below its own — copper ingots weld on a stone anvil, for example."
		""
		"Place the heated metal in the anvil, make sure a hammer and flux are in, and hit the weld button (④) before it cools."
	]
	quest.67FD3D45D45E06CB.title: "Smithing Guide: Welding"
	quest.681C9D47F39B91A0.quest_desc: [
		"You are the Magellan of the TerraFirma world"
	]
	quest.681C9D47F39B91A0.title: "&eChallenge: Around the World"
	quest.683B5321229074F6.quest_desc: [
		"Wild crops grow in the TerraFirma world; breaking them drops some mature produce and seeds. Early on, this is your only source of seeds."
		"One more thing: small wild herbs only answer to a knife — harvest them with a knife in hand to get the goods; a hoe does nothing for them."
		""
		"Complete this quest to unlock the \\\"Farming Guide\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.683B5321229074F6.quest_subtitle: "magnet... oh sorry, wrong game"
	quest.683B5321229074F6.title: "Get Some Seeds"
	quest.683C3DDCD3FC40C5.quest_desc: [
		"Sneak-right-click with a backpack in hand to place it on the ground, where it works as a powerful storage block. With certain upgrades it can even serve as a fluid tank."
		""
		"&8Warning: looking at a placed backpack tanks your framerate!"
	]
	quest.684FD1CC8061A1BA.quest_desc: [
		"A single fluid tank stores 8000mB of one fluid, but buckets can't fill or drain it directly."
		""
		"Multiple tanks combine into one structure — up to 3 blocks wide and 30 blocks tall."
	]
	quest.684FD1CC8061A1BA.quest_subtitle: "The fluid tank"
	quest.689E0B54747D7F59.quest_desc: [
		"Highly oriented pyrolytic graphite powder is made in the squeezer: 8 graphite powder or coke powder into one."
	]
	quest.68B1EFDD124CFF4F.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, balloon envelopes are made from cloth — burlap, wool cloth or silk all work, dyeable as usual: one piece of cloth plus two sticks makes four envelopes. Fill the space a balloon encloses with hot air and it generates lift: place an adjustable burner right beneath the balloon, apply a redstone signal, and hot air fills it top-down — off the ground you go."
		"A jute field is the foundation of your balloon industry: soak jute into fibers and weave burlap — one field, one season, one balloon. Wool cloth works just the same (2 wool weave into 1 cloth), so shepherds lose nothing. Once you have Create machinery, arm a deployer with shears pointed at a sheep for automatic shearing."
		"Hot air must be enclosed by airtight blocks; blocks inside the balloon eat into its effective volume. Higher altitude means lower pressure and weaker lift — the balloon naturally hovers where lift meets gravity. Tune the burner's output to control your height."
		"Toss in haunted items to change the flame color — full ritual vibes."
	]
	quest.68B1EFDD124CFF4F.quest_subtitle: "Humanity's oldest aircraft"
	quest.68B1EFDD124CFF4F.title: "Hot Air Balloon"
	quest.68FAF5722D9330E6.quest_desc: [
		"The chest is an 18-slot container holding items of large size or smaller — one row less than vanilla. Like vanilla chests, two combine into a double chest."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the \\\"Storage \\& Logistics\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.68FAF5722D9330E6.quest_subtitle: "No hardcore mod lets chests escape the nerf"
	quest.68FAF5722D9330E6.title: "Chest"
	quest.691426FDDF1DBEE8.quest_desc: [
		"Trains — Create's uniquely powerful logistics — carry items, fluids, and mobs."
		""
		"A train is essentially a special moving structure, like a contraption minecart. But it's faster, runs more precisely, consumes no resources, and can drive itself."
		""
		"Special tracks let trains run in the Nether, and running off MC's main thread lets them travel through unloaded chunks. That makes trains extremely stable and accurate, boosting their hauling power further. Pity the machines aboard don't work in unloaded chunks."
	]
	quest.691426FDDF1DBEE8.title: "Trains"
	quest.697A86EBB3FDC50C.quest_desc: [
		"Graphite electrodes are pressed in the bottling machine: insert a rod mold and 4 portions of highly oriented pyrolytic graphite powder, then pump in 1000mB of creosote (electrodes can be enchanted with Unbreaking). Electrodes slowly wear out while the arc furnace runs — check and replace them regularly."
		"By the way: the powder can also be heated to brilliant white in a forge (bellows required) to make a HOPG ingot, but that is only an intermediate form — electrodes never need the ingot, and spare ingots can be crushed back into powder with no loss."
	]
	quest.69A8552ABEA84FCD.quest_desc: [
		"Smelting alloys means mixing metals in the right proportions. Bronze, for instance: 18 five-mB native copper powders plus 2 five-mB cassiterite powders smelt into 100mB of bronze (90% copper, right inside the 88%~92% window)."
		""
		"Load the metals into a small vessel in proportion, as when smelting copper. Hover over the vessel and it will tell you whether the mix makes an alloy. Once confirmed, fire it in a pit kiln."
		""
		"Get the ratio wrong and you'll smelt an unknown alloy instead. You can try to rescue it in a charcoal forge by correcting the ratio — but pour it into a mold, and that metal is wasted for good."
	]
	quest.69A8552ABEA84FCD.title: "Alloys"
	quest.69D9F9E88DEDCC2E.quest_desc: [
		"A cathedral's stained glass? No problem."
	]
	quest.69D9F9E88DEDCC2E.title: "&eChallenge: A Blaze of Color"
	quest.69F961197D5DCA72.quest_desc: [
		"The revolver is a ranged weapon that loads several kinds of ammunition. Firing it makes a huge noise that draws nearby hostiles."
		""
		"Its ammo needs the bullet blueprint and comes in standard and special types, crafted at the engineer's workbench. Different bullets do different things."
		""
		"The revolver accepts upgrades that improve its own performance."
	]
	quest.69F961197D5DCA72.quest_subtitle: "It's high noon..."
	quest.6A199E4C85A3D13F.quest_desc: [
		"The altitude sensor outputs redstone by elevation (air pressure), the speed sensor by velocity, and the attitude sensor by orientation — ranges and directions are set in their value panels."
		"They are the senses of autopilot: e.g. pair an altitude sensor with a receiver so the airship shuts off its burner once it reaches the set height."
	]
	quest.6A199E4C85A3D13F.quest_subtitle: "Instrument flight"
	quest.6A199E4C85A3D13F.title: "Flight Sensors"
	quest.6A4F03F6CAE9D73E.quest_desc: [
		"Never yank a high-voltage line barehanded. The HV switch handles normal on/off: place a connector one block away facing the switch and it works, controlled manually or by redstone."
		"The SF6 circuit breaker safely cuts heavy current during faults: input at the top, output at the bottom, closed by default — apply a redstone signal to trip it open."
	]
	quest.6A4F03F6CAE9D73E.quest_subtitle: "Pulling the breaker"
	quest.6A4F03F6CAE9D73E.title: "HV Switch \\& Circuit Breaker"
	quest.6A64F6EBAE7BFD8B.quest_desc: [
		"Pumping fluids long distance with the fluid pump needs fluid pipes — the pipes themselves have no distance limit."
	]
	quest.6A6AEEC2EE72BF27.quest_desc: [
		"Immersive Engineering is a mod about building multiblock machines, with the ultimate goal of the supreme smelter: the arc furnace. Along the way you'll unlock machines and items that improve your game."
		""
		"Complete this quest to unlock the \\\"Immersive Engineering\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.6A6AEEC2EE72BF27.title: "Immersive Engineering"
	quest.6A6C0FDCD2335D38.quest_desc: [
		"Netherite actually underperforms red and blue steel — but it's so ubiquitous that we chose red-blue steel for the recipes."
	]
	quest.6ACB2CD1D0982CA2.quest_desc: [
		"The spout injects fluids into items without any power, but needs a depot or belt two blocks below it."
		""
		"With it, you can automatically fill items on a belt — fluid-filling recipes on an assembly line."
	]
	quest.6ACB2CD1D0982CA2.quest_subtitle: "Filled to the brim"
	quest.6B327EF0395DA47B.quest_subtitle: "Granite and diorite deep underground"
	quest.6B327EF0395DA47B.title: "Cryolite"
	quest.6B370BF364CDDA3E.quest_desc: [
		"The programmable gearbox sequences rotation over time — precisely controlling how far a contraption moves or how far it turns."
	]
	quest.6B4A1551D821D424.quest_desc: [
		"In the current version, base TerraFirmaCraft reworked beekeeping heavily — harder, yet poorly rewarded."
	]
	quest.6B4A1551D821D424.quest_subtitle: "Stay tuned"
	quest.6B4A1551D821D424.title: "Work in Progress"
	quest.6B58C0FBF30A5BFD.quest_desc: [
		"Copper smelting needs usable copper feedstock. You can use a gold pan — knapped from clay like other pottery and hardened by heat. Hold it and right-click any gravel, then stand in water and hold right-click for a chance at native copper powder."
		""
		"You can also hunt for ore nuggets scattered on the surface: native copper, malachite, and tetrahedrite nuggets are the usable copper ones."
	]
	quest.6B58C0FBF30A5BFD.title: "Finding Copper"
	quest.6B782E8668D1B1DC.quest_desc: [
		"The blast furnace needs up to 68 wrought iron sheets — but only 20 to start with, and 60 of those 68 can later be replaced by chromium sheets."
		""
		"You can also craft blast furnace insulation from three wrought iron sheets and one flux — though that doesn't reduce your total sheet usage."
	]
	quest.6B782E8668D1B1DC.quest_subtitle: "Keep smelting, keep forging"
	quest.6B782E8668D1B1DC.title: "More Wrought Iron"
	quest.6BA53B79C2386CC4.quest_desc: [
		"Smithing means recipes performed on an anvil: regular smithing and welding. Welding is simple; smithing without aid is hard."
		""
		"If you still can't do it after this chapter — or simply don't want to learn — look for helper tools, like the smithing-assist resource pack bundled with this modpack."
	]
	quest.6BA53B79C2386CC4.title: "Smithing Guide"
	quest.6BF33599AF371658.quest_desc: [
		"The contact redstone signal generator detects contraption positions — one on a contraption and one placed normally emit a redstone signal whenever they dock."
	]
	quest.6C2A997579F144FB.quest_desc: [
		"Glue works almost exactly like slimeballs, and also joins some TFC-exclusive recipes."
		"Classic recipe: 600 mB limewater + 1 bone meal, sealed in a barrel for about 6 minutes. Once you have Create, a Mechanical Mixer does it instantly."
		"Tip: sealed-barrel recipes do not show up when you inspect a single item in JEI - browse the full recipe list, or use EMI to look them up directly."
	]
	quest.6D0D57C8EED694B0.quest_desc: [
		"Heat flux to get lime. Besides mixing with fresh water for limewater, it's used in glassmaking, papermaking, and some building materials."
	]
	quest.6D0D57C8EED694B0.quest_subtitle: "CaO"
	quest.6D1264B9FF3D4E23.quest_desc: [
		"Salt a flatbread shell, smash it into corn chips, and combine with tomato sauce, shredded cheese, and any meat for nachos."
	]
	quest.6DD8702EF10DC5C2.quest_desc: [
		"Hold a walking stick in your main or off hand to become immune to slowing from grass, snow, and the like."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the \\\"Exploration Guide\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.6DFA1AB53E305B80.quest_desc: [
		"Cheese effectively raises your dairy nutrition. Making it requires killing cows, musk oxen, yaks, goats, or sheep for their drop: rennet."
		""
		"Seal rennet with milk in a barrel for liquid curd; seal that with cheesecloth for curd items. Craft curd with salt, or seal it with brine, to make six kinds of cheese wheels — identical except in name."
		""
		"A cheese wheel has infinite shelf life, even placed on the ground. To eat, right-click it with a knife to cut off a quarter — the cut slices do spoil."
		""
		"One more thing: leave a whole cheese wheel in a valid cellar (16°C or below — see the cellar quest) and it ages by itself, from fresh to aged to vintage, and slices cut from it keep much longer. Cellars detect themselves now — no climate station required."
	]
	quest.6DFA1AB53E305B80.title: "Cheese"
	quest.6DFB6BDC60580B5E.quest_desc: [
		"Place two straw blocks in a row, then a large hide on top — that's the straw bed. It can't pass the night, but it does set your spawn point."
	]
	quest.6DFB6BDC60580B5E.title: "Straw Bed"
	quest.6E0D1DF72B94ADC9.quest_desc: [
		"The mechanical mixer runs many recipes and needs a basin two blocks below it."
		""
		"It stirs certain items into new things — making ore slurries, for instance — and runs every shapeless recipe; with a blaze burner assisting, it can even brew potions."
	]
	quest.6E0D1DF72B94ADC9.quest_subtitle: "Relax — dizziness is normal"
	quest.6E0D1DF72B94ADC9.title: "Mixing"
	quest.6F3B051A9D730DA5.quest_desc: [
		"Like the campfire, it only takes low-temperature fuel. Its strength is heat retention, effectively raising fuel efficiency; its weakness is a bloated multiblock with no UI. Mainly for baking bread, though it can heat other items too."
	]
	quest.6F3B051A9D730DA5.title: "Oven"
	quest.6F4B5AB478CE713E.quest_desc: [
		"The chain drive is a fairly freeform transmission — two wheels neither too near nor too far link up with a chain."
		""
		"With a wrench you can ride along the chain, zipline-style."
	]
	quest.6F70765067E7AAF1.quest_desc: [
		"Boil it in a pot, or make tomato sauce mixture and boil it in the stainless steel vat."
	]
	quest.6FC10036FFFE31D7.quest_desc: [
		"Boil corn kernels in limewater, then seal the product with water for a while to get nixtamalized corn."
	]
	quest.6FD979AE52D97E48.quest_desc: [
		"Campfires, pit kilns and other heat sources raise your temperature. These sources stack."
	]
	quest.6FD979AE52D97E48.title: "Making Fire"
	quest.70295CA9D4E03DDA.quest_desc: [
		"The wheel seat is the suspension that mounts tires onto a physics structure. A redstone signal from above brakes with more friction; one from the side steers."
		"Four wheel seats, one portable engine, one steering wheel — your first off-roader is complete."
	]
	quest.70295CA9D4E03DDA.quest_subtitle: "Where four-wheel drive begins"
	quest.70295CA9D4E03DDA.title: "Wheel Seat"
	quest.703BA870985FA0C5.quest_desc: [
		"Once you can build a campfire and a bed, you need a suitable site for your base — a good base decides how fast and how comfortably you progress. A proper site generally needs:"
		""
		"1. Fresh water nearby — ideally a long river."
		""
		"2. Forest close by, but with a large clearing at hand."
		""
		"3. Rock type (judge by the rocks on the ground) best be calcium-rich sedimentary rock — dolomite, chalk, marble."
		""
		"4. Average yearly temperature of 15-25°C, with 20-22°C ideal."
		""
		"5. Ground dirt of \\\"loam\\\" rather than \\\"mud\\\"."
		""
		"New players should finish this quest before starting Chapter 2, even though it unlocks much earlier."
	]
	quest.703BA870985FA0C5.title: "Establishing a Base"
	quest.70513B8852F6B525.quest_desc: [
		"Afterwards, the chocolate paste must be dried into edible chocolate."
	]
	quest.70513B8852F6B525.title: "Chocolate"
	quest.706A3B314141D990.quest_desc: [
		"Cocoa beans can be made into chocolate."
	]
	quest.7080738BD3CA6DEA.quest_desc: [
		"The toolbox mentioned earlier is recognized as a storage block — but you can't open it while it's on a contraption."
	]
	quest.70858B757E28F524.quest_desc: [
		"Put on the aviator goggles and look at any power component to see stress, airflow, air pressure — every flight stat — right on your HUD. A must for pilots."
		"The mounted potato cannon is the block form of the potato cannon: feed it rotation to charge, fire with a redstone signal, sustain the signal for continuous fire, and it even auto-reloads. Ring your airship with them and you're a flying fortress."
	]
	quest.70858B757E28F524.quest_subtitle: "Potato turrets are an anti-air necessity"
	quest.70858B757E28F524.title: "A Pilot's Romance"
	quest.7089417845BA2E11.quest_desc: [
		"Animal husbandry is your main source of meat, eggs, milk, and wool. It takes a well-stocked larder — rotten food counts, since most livestock will eat it."
		"The new TFC brings new neighbors: bison roam temperate grasslands in herds and ram people as readily as moose; seals sun themselves by the sea and drop whale blubber. As for rats — in cold, arid, and tropical regions their grain-stealing posts are taken over by lemmings, jerboas, and mongooses."
		"Beware: penning large numbers of livestock in one area causes irreversible lag in your game or even the server. Practice planned parenthood."
	]
	quest.7089417845BA2E11.quest_subtitle: "I like pigs. Dogs look up to us. Cats look down on us. Pigs treat us as equals. — Winston Churchill"
	quest.7089417845BA2E11.title: "Animal Husbandry"
	quest.70B1AC12C3B73185.quest_desc: [
		"The gearbox connects linear stress in four directions — opposite faces spin in opposite directions."
		""
		"A vertical version exists, made by rotating with a wrench or by crafting."
	]
	quest.70B1AC12C3B73185.quest_subtitle: "Interesting internals"
	quest.70DFA9BB33B8B524.quest_subtitle: "Extrusive rock above y=40"
	quest.70DFA9BB33B8B524.title: "Native Copper"
	quest.711B685C4DC7E982.quest_desc: [
		"The loom weaves thread into cloth: wool yarn, spider silk, cotton thread, pineapple thread, linen fiber, and jute fiber can all be woven. Wool yarn weaves into wool cloth, which weaves further into wool; pineapple cloth is actually a leather variant."
	]
	quest.711B685C4DC7E982.quest_subtitle: "Slender hands at work"
	quest.711B685C4DC7E982.title: "The Loom Clatters"
	quest.7125F7DE94A46FA7.quest_desc: [
		"The axe deals slashing damage with bonus efficiency on wooden blocks. TFC axes fell whole trees — breaking the logs above the one you target."
	]
	quest.7125F7DE94A46FA7.title: "Stone Axe"
	quest.715669E7D546E425.quest_desc: [
		"Combine seven copper double ingots in a crafting table, arranged in the anvil shape, to make a copper anvil. It is a tier I anvil: forging copper ingots and welding copper-alloy double ingots both happen on it. Double ingots are welded from two ingots of the same metal on any stone anvil with flux."
	]
	quest.715669E7D546E425.quest_subtitle: "The anvil that starts it all"
	quest.7182903ED2EA8F35.quest_desc: [
		"The steam boiler produces colossal stress, but building one is a real chore."
		""
		"Build an nxmxn fluid tank tower, place blaze burners at its base as the heat source, pipe in water, and mount steam engines with shafts connected on top."
		""
		"Output depends on the tower's size, water input rate, and the number and burn state of the blaze burners. A top-tier steam boiler can output &l&c294912 su&r&r of stress!"
	]
	quest.7195F732DEE35696.quest_desc: [
		"For logistics, a belt is a depot that rotates: it carries items placed on it, in the direction it spins."
		""
		"If no device accepts items at a belt's end, they fly off as drops. Another belt or a depot there takes them over. A blocking block stops the flow."
		""
		"Andesite and brass funnels placed over a belt pull items off automatically."
	]
	quest.7195F732DEE35696.quest_subtitle: "Possibly Create's strongest block"
	quest.7195F732DEE35696.title: "Belt Logistics"
	quest.71B0E775AAEE1B13.quest_desc: [
		"For storing large volumes of wine, use the large vessel — it holds more liquid than a barrel. To store wine bottle and all, use the wine rack."
	]
	quest.71B0E775AAEE1B13.title: "Storing Wine"
	quest.71DE0C4DC2E26005.quest_desc: [
		"Create's mailbox shines in multiplayer: with cardboard packages, you can mail items to other players over any distance."
		""
		"Pack items into a cardboard package with the packager, write the recipient's address, and drop it in the mailbox to send."
	]
	quest.71DE0C4DC2E26005.quest_subtitle: "Guaranteed delivery"
	quest.71DE0C4DC2E26005.title: "Express Mail"
	quest.72843FF131D446B7.quest_desc: [
		"The prospector's pick was covered briefly in Chapter 3 — in short, you find a vein's center from the boundary between \\\"large\\\" and \\\"huge\\\" readings."
		""
		"A cruder method: if ore nuggets appear on the surface, a matching vein certainly lies below."
		""
		"Later in this quest line you'll meet three extra prospecting tools. Pricey, but used well they find veins much faster."
	]
	quest.72843FF131D446B7.title: "Prospecting"
	quest.7346528C14F14C00.quest_desc: [
		"TFC's mechanical power isn't as creative as the Create mod's, but it still improves life in its own way."
		""
		"For most players it mainly assists ore processing — so in this pack it's been moved up to the Copper Age."
	]
	quest.7346528C14F14C00.title: "TerraFirma's Mechanical Power"
	quest.73B1158E0411628B.quest_desc: [
		"The valve handle and hand crank both generate stress when right-clicked; sneak-clicking reverses direction. The only thing they consume is your hunger."
		""
		"Their output is low — good for manually switching certain machines."
	]
	quest.73B13479C0974BB1.quest_desc: [
		"The blaze burner is a multi-purpose block with two crafting routes: go to the Nether, craft an empty one from netherrack, and catch a blaze — or forge an empty one from wrought iron double ingots and heat it to white-hot."
		""
		"Its normal state is \\\"burning\\\", fed with anything that has a \\\"fuel\\\" recipe in JEI. Liquid fuels like creosote work too, delivered by fluid pipes."
		""
		"Certain special fuels put the burner into \\\"superheated\\\" mode, unlocking more functions — feed it a blaze cake or biodiesel."
	]
	quest.73B13479C0974BB1.quest_subtitle: "Create's one and only designated workhorse"
	quest.73B13479C0974BB1.title: "Catching a Blaze"
	quest.73BBB17D0DB1E4FC.quest_desc: [
		"The mechanical pump moves fluids through pipes and needs power. The arrow on top shows its direction."
		""
		"One pump moves fluid up to 16 blocks; speed scales with rotation speed."
	]
	quest.73D9CB8C59B7F6A6.quest_desc: [
		"Mining takes knowledge — at minimum, which rock layers your ore generates in."
		""
		"It takes patience — sometimes ore hunting lasts hours."
		""
		"It takes luck — with bad luck, hours yield nothing."
		""
		"And if you truly can't stand it anymore, it takes assistance — install an X-ray mod, if you're not on someone else's server."
		""
		"Either way, here are some tips. Good luck."
	]
	quest.73D9CB8C59B7F6A6.title: "Miner's Guide"
	quest.7433FA5BE0DC68F5.quest_desc: [
		"Bowls serve soup from the pot, or make salads."
		""
		"Right-click with an empty bowl in hand to make a salad. Like soup, salad has its own shelf life and inherits 75% of its ingredients' total nutrition — but the same materials make four bowls of soup versus one salad."
		""
		"A bowl becomes dirty after one use; a later quest teaches you to wash bowls."
	]
	quest.743AA1D336A9629C.quest_desc: [
		"Livestock won't approach you on their own — you have to bring them home. Sneak-look at livestock and black hearts show on screen; those are your targets. Many ways to catch them: lead them with a rope, or lure them along with their favorite food."
		""
		"For pens, fences work best. Most livestock can hop one-block-high obstacles, and poultry can clear over three — keep that in mind."
	]
	quest.743AA1D336A9629C.quest_subtitle: "Within my grasp — where would you run?"
	quest.743AA1D336A9629C.title: "No Escape"
	quest.7462F6172057CEDB.quest_desc: [
		"Eating ice cream lowers body temperature, with a touch of nutrition. Combine the three ice creams with fruit for a grand sundae."
		""
		"Note: some ice cream names display wrongly in the tooltip — a bug awaiting the mod author's fix."
	]
	quest.7462F6172057CEDB.title: "Ice Cream"
	quest.746A9E679F0E48FA.quest_desc: [
		"The greenhouse lets your crops grow year-round, ignoring season and latitude. It grows fruit trees, crops, and bushes."
		""
		"The new greenhouse no longer needs a weather station — the system auto-detects qualifying enclosed spaces: up to 24 blocks horizontally and 8 vertically, with at least half the roof made of sky-visible glass."
		""
		"Three essentials, all required: an &4enclosed space&r, a &4roof of which over half is sky-visible glass&r, and &4planters placed inside&r. An empty house won't grow anything — crops go in planters."
		""
		"\\\"Glass\\\" here is broad: vanilla stained glass, TFC poured glass, and the greenhouse block's roof and wall panels all count. But note — roof blocks must see the sky directly; anything stacked above voids them."
		""
		"More glass roofing means a warmer interior: base temperature starts at 4°C and a full glass roof reaches 44°C. Wall insulation (thermal resistance) decides how stable the temperature stays. Yield trails farmland, but maturity is faster — a greenhouse at scale can even beat open fields."
	]
	quest.746A9E679F0E48FA.title: "Greenhouse"
	quest.7499A6AE4621A389.quest_desc: [
		"Create enables automatic smithing — no more clicking at an anvil forever."
	]
	quest.7499A6AE4621A389.title: "Automated Smithing"
	quest.7501D3AEC6E52B13.quest_desc: [
		"Once Create is unlocked, the fan replaces the sluice for ore washing — just toss the feedstock onto an airflow that has passed through water."
	]
	quest.75045CB20541CA03.quest_desc: [
		"The brass funnel upgrades the andesite funnel: a full stack per output, freely adjustable input/output amounts, and item filtering."
	]
	quest.75045CB20541CA03.quest_subtitle: "Often the chief suspect behind TPS drops"
	quest.75045CB20541CA03.title: "Brass Funnel"
	quest.752983EAD0DDBF03.quest_desc: [
		"The weighted ejector moves items across distance — its target must be set before placement."
		""
		"Once powered, it launches entities and items above it. If anything blocks the arc, they won't reach the target."
	]
	quest.752983EAD0DDBF03.quest_subtitle: "It can't launch crow's feet away"
	quest.7529C31878D646B6.quest_desc: [
		"Belts transmit stress perpendicular to their shafts — horizontally, vertically, or at 45°."
		""
		"Right-click between two parallel shafts to install one; it drives every shaft mounted inside it at once."
	]
	quest.75307F48C0278496.quest_desc: [
		"Making red and blue steel means TFC's main line is over — but this pack's content isn't. Your ultimate goal: advance Aeronautics and Cosmonautics, build a rocket, and land on the Moon!"
		""
		"You're equally free to do other things — a fully automated ore line, a Create train network, or... completing every achievement?"
	]
	quest.753C2B6BEDE760E6.quest_desc: [
		"Copper freshly poured into a mold may still be molten — wait, or throw it into water to cool it."
		""
		"Once a mold cools below the melting point, you can take out its contents: sneak-right-click with it in hand, or craft it in the crafting grid."
		""
		"Copper tool heads combine with sticks or branches just like stone tool heads — except metal tools need no extra binding material."
	]
	quest.753C2B6BEDE760E6.title: "Your First Copper"
	quest.7543C21A5ED4064D.quest_desc: [
		"TFC's Nether is tweaked to fit the base mod. You'll find rocks of every rock type on the ground, and crimson/warped fungi are replaced by crimson and warped wood. Beyond that, little has changed."
		""
		"Note that Nether rock layers still collapse — except netherrack."
		""
		"The Nether's lava seas explode violently. Best not get too close."
	]
	quest.7543C21A5ED4064D.quest_subtitle: "This mod is in early development and its content is modest — thanks for understanding"
	quest.7543C21A5ED4064D.title: "Nether, Vanilla vs Ours"
	quest.75513C79E446A03F.quest_desc: [
		"Green beans and tomatoes need sticks stuck beside them to grow properly."
		""
		"Rice must be planted in farmland with one block of standing water."
		""
		"Watermelons and pumpkins need a free block beside them to bear fruit."
		""
		"Red and yellow bell peppers are picked with right-click rather than harvested with left-click."
		""
		"Grapes grow in a unique way — consult the field guide."
	]
	quest.75513C79E446A03F.title: "Crops Needing Special Care"
	quest.756262F78A02A4B8.quest_desc: [
		"The basket is both a storage block and a logistics block. It holds a chest's worth of capacity and ignores item size and weight."
		""
		"A basket has an open face, up by default, oriented by how you place it. It automatically sucks up drops within one block of that face."
	]
	quest.75A03C25A18922C3.quest_subtitle: "Tropical highlands, surface, above 18°C, over 300mm rainfall"
	quest.75A03C25A18922C3.title: "Kaolinite"
	quest.75A6E4F55999EF2B.quest_desc: [
		"Any flour plus a container of water crafts into two flatbread dough; baking gives flatbread with twice the dough's shelf life."
	]
	quest.75A6E4F55999EF2B.quest_subtitle: "Not exactly refined-looking"
	quest.75ADB32D28D01951.quest_desc: [
		"Shafts transmit stress in a straight line — along the shaft's direction."
		""
		"Cogwheels also transmit sideways, perpendicular to the shaft. Two small cogwheels can mesh side by side."
		""
		"Gears and shafts can be encased in andesite casing."
	]
	quest.75ADB32D28D01951.title: "Sideways \\& Straight Connections"
	quest.761A2980CF36CC0E.quest_desc: [
		"The rope pulley turns the glued area directly beneath it into a contraption and moves it vertically. A contraption it moves stops the moment a block obstructs it."
		""
		"When another device moves the rope pulley, its attached contraption moves along."
		""
		"Use the config panel above it to control when the contraption re-solidifies."
	]
	quest.761B5E1EB307786B.quest_desc: [
		"Two cogwheels meshed sideways always spin in opposite directions — useful for reversing rotation."
	]
	quest.761B5E1EB307786B.title: "Gear Reversal"
	quest.763725046017AABA.quest_desc: [
		"Campfire heat alone can't fire pottery or smelt metal — you need a device called the pit kiln. One pit kiln takes 8 logs and 8 straw."
	]
	quest.763725046017AABA.title: "Pit Kiln"
	quest.764432C063391A2C.quest_desc: [
		"Bugs you might hit include but aren't limited to:"
		"- Sudden crashes or freezes mid-game, then being unable to re-enter the world"
		"- Finding odd recipes, or unbalanced, unreasonable ones"
		"- Serious compatibility bugs"
		"- Bugs that block progression entirely"
		""
		"Report bugs on our Discord:"
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Join our Discord\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://discord.gg/Fc7v5EXmkK\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
	]
	quest.764432C063391A2C.quest_subtitle: "We fix player-reported bugs as fast as we can"
	quest.764432C063391A2C.title: "Feedback \\& Suggestions"
	quest.76A888D663A57A86.quest_desc: [
		"The crafting table — your best friend, no different from vanilla."
		""
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the \\\"Crafting Guide\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.76A888D663A57A86.quest_subtitle: "Hopefully it won't take you 25 days to make this"
	quest.76A888D663A57A86.title: "Crafting Table"
	quest.76AE9CD057733C01.quest_desc: [
		"The display link sends an attached block's info to displays — handy for decorating factories and the like."
		""
		"The most-used displays are the flap display and the nixie tube. Make sure your display is long enough."
	]
	quest.76AE9CD057733C01.title: "Info Display"
	quest.76D47D6D1E129FDA.quest_desc: [
		"The cooking pot is the block for cooking dishes, and must sit on a stove."
		""
		"Pot dishes follow fixed recipes: meet one and it starts cooking by itself. Put wooden bowls in the pot to serve. Dishes have their own nutrition and shelf life, unrelated to the ingredients you put in."
	]
	quest.76D47D6D1E129FDA.quest_subtitle: "Pre-made meals (not really)"
	quest.76DC471C7BADA161.quest_desc: [
		"Crushing wheels crush items with high efficiency — some recipes inherited from the quern, others exclusive."
		""
		"To use them, place two crushing wheels one block apart, spinning in opposite directions. A virtual block called the crushing wheel controller appears between them — the core of the pair."
		""
		"Input and output directions depend on the wheels' spin. You can toss items in, or use the controller for input and output."
	]
	quest.76DC471C7BADA161.title: "A Pair of Big Fellas"
	quest.7781AB49727EB18C.quest_desc: [
		"If you can overlook that mining it yields rocks and can trigger cave-ins, it's actually decent for building."
	]
	quest.7781AB49727EB18C.title: "Natural Rock"
	quest.77D3DFE790706C4E.quest_desc: [
		"Goat hide can be sewn into goat-hide gear at the sewing table — your first insulation set."
		""
		"Once you have leather, switch to leather gear."
	]
	quest.77D3DFE790706C4E.quest_subtitle: "Clip-clop, caw-caw"
	quest.7824ECE738C254DA.quest_desc: [
		"Roof frames are made from lumber and sticks, and come in slab and stair shapes too."
	]
	quest.7825FFB55A09E054.quest_desc: [
		"Step one: smash ore into rocky ore chunks with a hammer."
	]
	quest.7825FFB55A09E054.quest_subtitle: "Ore washing, step one"
	quest.7825FFB55A09E054.title: "Hammer Time"
	quest.783269DF5A7A2183.quest_desc: [
		"Heating masa dough gives tortillas — heat them once more in an oven for flatbread shells."
	]
	quest.78CC31E2A5D6CC74.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have a steel ingot, this chapter opens automatically."
	]
	quest.78E37868E67448FF.quest_desc: [
		"Mesh a large cogwheel with a small one and the small one spins at double speed."
	]
	quest.78E37868E67448FF.title: "Gear Shifting"
	quest.78F298F669A621AE.quest_desc: [
		"Chests can't hold tools — that's where the tool rack comes in. Wall-mounted, four tools per rack."
	]
	quest.78F298F669A621AE.title: "Tool Rack"
	quest.78FFB948EC6DF56A.quest_desc: [
		"The accumulator backpack powers the devices you carry. Fit a battery into it at the engineer's workbench first."
	]
	quest.790918B6292256FE.quest_desc: [
		"Place a rail, put the cart assembler on it, and put any minecart on the rail. When redstone-activated, the assembler turns the glued area above into a contraption and mounts it on the cart, creating a contraption minecart. Inactive, it re-solidifies the structure on the cart."
		""
		"A moving contraption minecart carries its contraption along, and the structure can phase through blocks."
		""
		"Right-click with a wrench to pick up the cart; it keeps its original minecart functions — a furnace minecart still eats fuel to speed up."
		""
		"The config panel on the assembler's side controls whether the moving structure rotates."
	]
	quest.790918B6292256FE.quest_subtitle: "Little cart, big moving structure"
	quest.791B4E8780BEA31C.quest_desc: [
		"Key point: this pack's rockets do NOT burn lava! The fuel is Immersive Engineering's biodiesel (high-power biodiesel is even better), and the oxidizer is plain water. Pump each into the engine pipes on the hull."
		"Build your fuel base like this: place two hose anchors, then right-click them in sequence with a fluid hose in hand to draw a flexible line whose ends auto-level. That's your fuel line from pad to tank."
	]
	quest.791B4E8780BEA31C.quest_subtitle: "What rockets drink"
	quest.791B4E8780BEA31C.title: "Fuel \\& Oxidizer"
	quest.7932CF2B21C63A6A.quest_desc: [
		"The alternator turns Create's rotation into electricity. Simple structure: a rotor, stator magnets around it, and brushes to draw out the current. Feed it rotation and it generates."
		"Voltage rises with speed — a bare unit easily outputs over a hundred volts, which would burn out a light bulb instantly. Next we'll test with the simplest load; transformers come shortly."
		"Hold W for the Ponder tutorial — a full build demo is inside."
	]
	quest.7932CF2B21C63A6A.quest_subtitle: "A rotor spins inside a stator"
	quest.7932CF2B21C63A6A.title: "Alternator"
	quest.79336C37B1AB604C.quest_desc: [
		"In this modpack, different times and environments make different air temperatures. You tolerate a certain range; beyond it, heat or cold builds up, eventually causing status effects and damage."
		""
		"Excess heat disorients: shrinking view distance, blurred vision, and a randomly drifting camera."
		""
		"Excess cold weakens the body: slower mining and movement, reduced attack knockback, and half your max HP."
		""
		"To avoid all this, use items that change the ambient temperature or widen your tolerance. Or find this mod's config page in game settings and tune it so it can't affect you at all."
	]
	quest.79336C37B1AB604C.title: "Cold Sweat"
	quest.793F53C4B462F2C6.quest_desc: [
		"The oven — a fine multiblock for cooking. Compared to a campfire, it holds high heat much longer."
		""
		"Knap clay into three blocks: oven top, oven base, and oven chimney. The base is the core; tops sit directly above it, several in a row. The chimney goes behind the base, any height. The left, right, and back faces of base and top need brick-type blocks for insulation — chimneys work too."
	]
	quest.793F53C4B462F2C6.quest_subtitle: "A fine solution for the integrated kitchen"
	quest.793F53C4B462F2C6.title: "Oven"
	quest.7959D79EC0E70740.quest_desc: [
		"Most crafting recipes are 3x3 and need a crafting table."
		""
		"The chopping board processes certain items: place an item with a board recipe on it and right-click with the matching tool."
	]
	quest.7959D79EC0E70740.title: "Two Work Blocks"
	quest.795D9C428C6E5193.quest_desc: [
		"Graphite is needed elsewhere too — gather as much as you can, at least an inventory's worth."
	]
	quest.79677EAC27182F25.quest_desc: [
		"Queens carry different traits:"
		""
		"Cold hardiness: better low-temperature tolerance"
		"Productivity: faster honey production"
		"Mutant: stronger trait inheritance by offspring"
		"Fertility: higher chance of breeding"
		"Crop affinity: lets the hive fertilize nearby farmland"
		"Natural healing: spawns flowers around the hive"
		"Calmness: lowers the chance bees attack you after harvest"
		""
		"A queen carries a random subset when she moves in; breeding has a chance to pass traits down. Higher trait levels are stronger. Beware, though — a queen with too much Mutant may give offspring genetic diseases, making them unable to produce honey."
	]
	quest.79677EAC27182F25.title: "Bee Traits"
	quest.796AEB66DF6C4865.quest_desc: [
		"Train signals mainly guard crossings and stretches with multiple trains — used well, they prevent collisions."
		""
		"The train observer emits a redstone signal when a train passes, handy for coordinating other devices."
	]
	quest.796AEB66DF6C4865.title: "Advanced Train Control"
	quest.79A04CC6D7668085.quest_desc: [
		"Run obsidian through crushing wheels for obsidian powder — the material for sturdy sheets, the core of any train system."
	]
	quest.79A04CC6D7668085.quest_subtitle: "Unbreakable — but train crashes still wreck things"
	quest.79A04CC6D7668085.title: "Train Basics"
	quest.79A6AFA8ADE287D0.quest_desc: [
		"The external heater heats with electricity and pairs with crucibles. Place crucibles on any of its five faces — front, back, left, right, top — to heat them."
		""
		"It can bring a crucible to brilliant white (brilliant white actually has sub-levels, and the external heater reaches the top one). Recommended whenever you need a really hot melt — much less hassle than babysitting a charcoal forge."
	]
	quest.79A6AFA8ADE287D0.quest_subtitle: "What's a charcoal forge?"
	quest.7A4DA3A53A991C89.quest_desc: [
		"All drawers except ender drawers can be unified under the storage controller. Place the controller, right-click it with the linking tool to record it, then right-click drawers to bind them. Upgrades on the controller extend the binding range."
		""
		"Insert into or extract from the whole drawer network through the controller; controller extensions bound to it work the same."
		""
		"The configurator sets individual drawer states — e.g. locking a drawer to only accept items it already stores."
	]
	quest.7A4DA3A53A991C89.title: "Advanced Drawers"
	quest.7A6BEFCF3EC358AC.quest_desc: [
		"The saw runs cutting recipes, often for wooden blocks. Use it to process logs further."
	]
	quest.7A6BEFCF3EC358AC.title: "Saw"
	quest.7AB085673037FF4A.quest_desc: [
		"The torsion spring transmits rotation within a set angle range and springs back to its start angle when input stops. The angle limit is set in its value panel; a comparator reads the current angle."
		"Use it for recoil mechanisms, suspension — or a catapult. The latter is obviously the more important use."
	]
	quest.7AB085673037FF4A.quest_subtitle: "The romance of physics"
	quest.7AB085673037FF4A.title: "Torsion Spring"
	quest.7AB3B0971A26532F.quest_desc: [
		"Some items, when placed inside certain working blocks called \\\"heat sources\\\", slowly rise in temperature until they match the source — this is heating. Such items usually transform into other items or fluids at specific temperatures."
		""
		"In TerraFirmaCraft, temperature tiers are color-coded, roughly gray – red – orange – yellow – white, low to high."
		""
		"Heat sources need certain items to work — items labeled \\\"burns up to a given temperature for a duration\\\". Collectively: fuel."
	]
	quest.7AB3B0971A26532F.title: "Heating \\& Fuel"
	quest.7AC9CE65945FF732.quest_desc: [
		"The tree tap is forged from a wrought iron sheet on a tier-3 anvil (hit last, upset for the two steps before that). Mount it on the middle of a natural trunk at least three blocks tall and place an upward-facing barrel directly below; when conditions are right, sap will start dripping into the barrel."
		""
		"Maple and birch yield sugar sap only in spring at -4°C to 6°C, around when the snow begins to melt. Hevea produces latex year-round above 14°C; rubber figs work from 6°C up, but at half the rate. Latitude, altitude, season and time of day all shift the temperature, so choose your grove wisely."
		""
		"Only naturally grown logs can be tapped. Sugar sap boils down into syrup, a fine sweetener; latex heated with sulfur powder in a mixer vulcanizes into rubber bars — the stuff of belts, hose pulleys and other machine parts."
	]
	quest.7AC9CE65945FF732.quest_subtitle: "An IV drip for trees"
	quest.7AC9CE65945FF732.title: "Tree Tap"
	quest.7AD5BC6414AFE439.quest_desc: [
		"Bellows push a charcoal forge or campfire beyond its fuel's temperature cap. The holed face must aim at the air block above the forge, or at the campfire itself."
		""
		"Right-click the bellows to pump once — the forge's heat gain and fuel consumption double for a few seconds, reaching peak temperature. Once the boost lapses, the forge cools back down from white-hot."
	]
	quest.7AD5BC6414AFE439.quest_subtitle: "Effective air exchange"
	quest.7AD5BC6414AFE439.title: "Strong Winds Blowing"
	quest.7B071B5BED46039A.quest_desc: [
		"Docking connectors work in pairs: extended connectors auto-align, and once fully aligned they lock rigidly, transferring items and fluids both ways. Retract either side to separate. A comparator reads the docking progress."
		"Ship docking, carriage coupling, automated freight stations — all rely on this pair."
	]
	quest.7B071B5BED46039A.quest_subtitle: "The ground edition of the kiss in space"
	quest.7B071B5BED46039A.title: "Docking Connector"
	quest.7B0CE0C43D0C5FA7.quest_desc: [
		"If a pipe's output opens only to air, fluid reaching it sprays out as particles, forming a fluid source in that block after a while."
		""
		"Lava sprayed this way makes cobblestone on touching water or waterlogged blocks — consuming neither lava nor water, so it works as a cobble generator. Mill that cobble and bulk-wash it for a 10% chance of iron nuggets — not high yield; whether it's worth a dedicated line is your call."
	]
	quest.7B0CE0C43D0C5FA7.quest_subtitle: "Essentially an iron farm"
	quest.7B0CE0C43D0C5FA7.title: "Cobble Generator"
	quest.7B2F1F1B385A6B97.quest_desc: [
		"Circuits are diagnosed by measurement: the ammeter goes in series to read current, the voltmeter in parallel across two points to read voltage. Wire them wrong and you'll get bad readings — or a burnt meter."
		"If you can't bring yourself to cut wires, craft a clamp meter instead: clip it onto a wire to read current size and direction."
	]
	quest.7B2F1F1B385A6B97.quest_subtitle: "An electrician's basic training"
	quest.7B2F1F1B385A6B97.title: "Ammeter \\& Voltmeter"
	quest.7B339888D26E793E.quest_desc: [
		"Forge wrought iron into the engineer's hammer and engineer's wire cutters — Immersive Engineering's basic tools."
		""
		"The hammer builds multiblock structures and does some hammering work. The cutters make metal plates and wires."
	]
	quest.7B60B2649CFF790C.quest_desc: [
		"The hearth provides cooling or heating — even both at once — as long as fuel and refrigerant last."
		""
		"Redstone from the left or back activates heating; from the bottom or right, cooling."
		""
		"Once activated, the hearth needs up to a minute to warm up, shown as the warmth or chill effect level rising gradually."
		""
		"A hearth can affect a total volume of up to 12,000 blocks, with a maximum radius of 96 blocks. But it only runs in an enclosed room."
	]
	quest.7B91F6170388E9D8.quest_desc: ["Toss bauxite straight into a crucible to melt out aluminum. Beware its high 1550°C melting point — a charcoal forge without bellows caps at 1415°C, so keep the bellows pumping to push past 1550°C (the heat bar reads brilliant white). Then pour the metal into ingot molds through a channel. Aluminum ingots mainly go into batteries and wires."]
	quest.7B91F6170388E9D8.quest_subtitle: "Sedimentary \\& metamorphic rock at any height, more at depth"
	quest.7B91F6170388E9D8.title: "Bauxite"
	quest.7BC7AB9444785C70.quest_desc: [
		"The scythe deals slashing damage, and above all replaces the knife for breaking plants: it clears a 3x3x3 area of plants in one swing, losing durability at the same rate."
	]
	quest.7BE07429076DD5A5.quest_desc: [
		"Now the main event. Catenary brackets auto-attach to adjacent utility poles, stringing the catenary above the rails. Electrify the catenary (positive to the wire, negative to a ground rod, about 2500V), then fit your train with a pantograph and an electric motor —"
		"Wooo — the electrified train departs! The pantograph can be dyed, powered trains change their sound, and placing certain blocks nearby switches the sound style."
	]
	quest.7BE07429076DD5A5.quest_subtitle: "Railway electrification"
	quest.7BE07429076DD5A5.title: "Catenary \\& Pantograph"
	quest.7BE7CAB908F1EB40.quest_desc: [
		"The basin mainly assists other machines. It stores nine items and two fluids of up to 1000mB, and all six faces accept input and output. It also auto-outputs to certain blocks placed diagonally below it."
		""
		"A recipe filter slot on its side sets a target product to avoid recipe confusion."
		""
		"Some recipes require a burning blaze burner beneath the basin."
	]
	quest.7BF9BE06D63A303D.quest_desc: [
		"Knap fire clay into unfired fire bricks, fire them into fire bricks, and craft those with mortar for fire brick blocks."
	]
	quest.7BF9BE06D63A303D.quest_subtitle: "The 80% that wasn't fireproof is gone"
	quest.7BF9BE06D63A303D.title: "Absolutely Fireproof"
	quest.7C09A11E0000ED01.quest_desc: [
		"Titanium is the key metal of Create: Aeronautics — no rockets without it. Its veins are very rare, generating in diabase, basalt, diorite, and granite at y=-60 to 30."
		""
		"Surface indicators of titanium are rare too. The reliable way is locating the vein with a prospecting rod, then setting up a mineral drill and letting Create pump it dry for you."
	]
	quest.7C09A11E0000ED01.quest_subtitle: "Rare veins in diabase, basalt, diorite, and granite"
	quest.7C09A11E0000ED01.title: "Titanium Ore"
	quest.7C0A57E11B3D9A24.quest_desc: [
		"Bored of physics structures? Time to build something scream-worthy."
		""
		"Find an open plot, drive in two coaster anchors, then right-click them in sequence with coaster track in hand — a smooth spline track auto-connects the two points. More anchors, wilder curves."
		""
		"Right-click track with a wrench to bring up curve handles, and drag to fine-tune slope and arc; hold Alt while placing to disable smoothing for sharp, angular bends."
		""
		"Tired of the color? Right-click track with dye to recolor it; scrape it back with an axe if you regret it."
	]
	quest.7C0A57E11B3D9A24.quest_subtitle: "Stake first, connect later"
	quest.7C0A57E11B3D9A24.title: "Coasters: Laying Track"
	quest.7C0FA3B0CBA1DA56.quest_desc: [
		"Fruit spoils quickly, but it has a unique step: drying on the drying mat. Note that drying fails in rain, snow, or at night."
		""
		"Dried fruit follows the brine → pickle → preserve route, though its shelf life still trails other foods. If you can, seal it in vinegar."
	]
	quest.7C0FA3B0CBA1DA56.title: "Fruit"
	quest.7D0409D7EA05406D.quest_desc: [
		"Only for smelting wrought iron. Feed ratio: two charcoal per 100mB of iron."
	]
	quest.7D4CB2C7344BFAAC.quest_desc: [
		"The magnetic stabilizer damps against the ambient magnetic field, canceling angular momentum when active. Fly out of the atmosphere without one and you will learn what a washing machine feels like."
		"The hologram console projects a scaled hologram of the surrounding cosmos; tap the adjustment points to zoom in and out."
		"After launch, watch the hologram: your trajectory is a parabola and its apex is your orbital insertion point. Fire again at the apex to raise the orbit into a circle — the periapsis must clear the atmosphere, or you have merely launched a very expensive firework."
	]
	quest.7D4CB2C7344BFAAC.quest_subtitle: "Don't spin — read the map"
	quest.7D4CB2C7344BFAAC.title: "Magnetic Stabilizer \\& Holo-Table"
	quest.7D5E480E38E98AD5.quest_desc: [
		"Powered redstone magnets attract or repel each other: opposite poles attract, like poles repel, and attracting magnets try to align."
		"Use them for soft-docking vehicles, magnetic levitation displays — or simply to yoink a friend's ship over."
	]
	quest.7D5E480E38E98AD5.quest_subtitle: "Opposites attract"
	quest.7D5E480E38E98AD5.title: "Electromagnet"
	quest.7D9E434665E86F03.quest_desc: [
		"Dairy animals are goats, cows, and yaks. All eat grain; goats also eat fruit and vegetables; only yaks refuse rotten food."
		""
		"Besides breeding, they can be milked. All three milks share recipes, but the animals differ in milking and aging cycles."
	]
	quest.7D9E434665E86F03.title: "Dairy Animals"
	quest.7DBE6817E1F6E30F.quest_desc: [
		"The spring links two blocks elastically: wrench in hand, right-click to tune stiffness; spring in hand, right-click to set rest length. Suspension, shock absorption, catapults — none work without it."
		"By the way: to move a finished boat or cart, don't dream of hauling it barehanded — no such trick exists in this world. Build an engine, hang balloons, rig a winch. Let power do the talking."
	]
	quest.7DBE6817E1F6E30F.quest_subtitle: "Softness overcomes hardness"
	quest.7DBE6817E1F6E30F.title: "Spring"
	quest.7E07F5E0C5A3983A.quest_subtitle: "Extrusive rock, near the surface"
	quest.7E07F5E0C5A3983A.title: "Hematite"
	quest.7E16777BC2F51A44.quest_desc: [
		"Place 27 coke oven bricks in a 3x3x3 cube and right-click the center of any face with the engineer's hammer — that's the coke oven. It turns logs into charcoal with 250mB of creosote, or bituminous coal and lignite into coke with 500mB of creosote."
		""
		"Every face of the coke oven accepts fluid and item input/output."
	]
	quest.7E2FC20911AAC17A.quest_desc: [
		"Heating kaolinite yields kaolinite powder at a 20% chance — the other 80% of the time you get nothing. Given the huge demand for kaolinite, batch-heat it in small vessels in a pit kiln."
	]
	quest.7E2FC20911AAC17A.quest_subtitle: "20% is your lie"
	quest.7E4A47E018C581AD.quest_desc: [
		"Stress is the energy Create's machines run on. It's unique to Create, so it needs unique devices to transmit."
		""
		"Completing this quest unlocks the \\\"Stress \\& Transmission Devices\\\" side chapter."
	]
	quest.7E4A47E018C581AD.title: "Stress \\& Transmission"
	quest.7E668B651B6954CB.quest_desc: [
		"The arc furnace is the pinnacle of metal smelting in this pack. Enormous power draw buys you nearly every smelting recipe. Some recipes also make slag."
		""
		"It draws 4096FE/t — exactly one diesel generator's output. Like the diesel generator, it has three power inputs."
		""
		"The arc furnace needs graphite electrodes to work — three slots inside."
		""
		"In this pack, the blast bricks it needs are replaced by fire brick blocks. The huge demand of 27 fire brick blocks calls for solid kaolinite reserves."
	]
	quest.7E668B651B6954CB.quest_subtitle: "Remember to swap graphite electrodes now and then!"
	quest.7E668B651B6954CB.title: "The Hottest Topic"
	quest.7E8A3623D862BC62.quest_desc: [
		"The bone needle is the essential tool for the sewing table. Load it with a needle, thread, and cloth (wool or burlap) to sew banner patterns and armor trim smithing templates by following the pattern."
		""
		"Note: hides and leather can't go into the sewing table — sewing only accepts cloth. To process hides, follow the tanning line instead."
		""
		"Once in the Metal Age, you can cast metal fish hooks and make a fishing rod. Fishing steps are in the book — or skip the formalities and dive in to grab fish directly."
	]
	quest.7E8A3623D862BC62.quest_subtitle: "A true primitive man"
	quest.7E8A3623D862BC62.title: "Bone Work"
	quest.7EDA53565EA26940.quest_desc: [
		"TerraFirma's forests do slowly spread, but that can't keep up with a player's massive log demand. If the forest near home isn't large, start planting trees now."
	]
	quest.7EDA53565EA26940.title: "Trees"
	quest.7EEC0AB8CE8326C4.quest_desc: [
		"Alpacas, musk oxen, and sheep drop sheepskin; craft it with a knife for wool. Wool plus a spindle makes wool yarn. Wool yarn, like sinew string, is a kind of thread — further processing requires copper tools."
	]
	quest.7F29BD740D749BDB.quest_desc: [
		"The green bar right of your health is hunger — you need more food than vanilla to fill it. While it's not full, your max HP shrinks slightly."
		""
		"The blue bar under hunger is thirst: restore it by drinking fresh water or beverages. Early on you can right-click fresh water sources to drink, but salt water doesn't help — it gives the Thirst debuff."
		""
		"Carrying extremely large, very heavy items makes both hunger and thirst drain faster."
	]
	quest.7F29BD740D749BDB.title: "Food \\& Water"
	quest.7F3BD13A6D3468CF.quest_desc: [
		"Sputnik is a simple satellite: once in orbit it keeps its chunk loaded forever, streams back biome color data, and can dock with a computer to map the stars."
		"Cable a computer to the satellite and it becomes a peripheral: getPosition() for coordinates, getOrbitalPeriod() for the orbital period, getDistanceToPlanet() for altitude, getBiomeName() for the biome below — a complete telemetry station."
		"Make it your rocket's first payload — light, useful, the perfect start to a space program."
	]
	quest.7F3BD13A6D3468CF.quest_subtitle: "The first artificial satellite"
	quest.7F3BD13A6D3468CF.title: "Sputnik"
	quest.7F5295A9A2EBF122.quest_desc: [
		"Copper broadens your tool set, sparking new materials and facilities. Most of this pack's playable content opens to you from this chapter, in the side chapters. Explore freely to improve your quality of life."
		""
		"In this chapter you'll use copper tools to make new blocks and gear, mine more ores, and finally make at least one of the three copper alloys — bismuth bronze, bronze, and black bronze."
	]
	quest.7F5295A9A2EBF122.quest_subtitle: "Come learn alloy smelting"
	quest.7F5295A9A2EBF122.title: "Chapter 3 — Chapter Goals"
	quest.7F53EF08F17732CE.quest_desc: [
		"Wires have resistance: the longer the run and the higher the current, the bigger the loss (loss = resistance × current²). The fix is the same as in real life: step voltage up for transmission, down for use."
		"First make a transformer core and set the coil turn ratio on both sides, then assemble the transformer — the turn ratio is the voltage ratio. Radiators around the core, or immersion in transformer oil, raise its rated power; run beyond that and it overloads."
		"The Ponder tutorial has a full demo — strongly recommended before you build."
		"Getting transformer oil: mix plant oil with water in a heated mixer basin, then scoop it up with a TFC wooden bucket — that filled bucket is what the transformer recipe accepts."
	]
	quest.7F53EF08F17732CE.quest_subtitle: "The translator of voltage"
	quest.7F53EF08F17732CE.title: "Transformer"
	quest.7FD6A364CBAA7533.quest_desc: [
		"The power loom weaves cloth automatically — see JEI for its construction. Its operation is a bit involved, so let's go through it."
		""
		"Take its power-input side as the left: the front has an item output port, and the right a spindle rack holding up to 8 spindles."
		""
		"First make wound spindles from the matching thread — wool cloth takes wool yarn spindles, for instance. Then hold 16 of the same thread and right-click the grille in the machine's middle; these threads aren't consumed. Finally, place the remaining thread on the rack at the machine's lower front. With enough thread, the power loom starts working."
		""
		"Each run of the loom takes 32 threads (48 for jute). Take the finished cloth by sneak-right-clicking the lower rack on the back, or place a container at mid-back. Spent wound spindles eject as drops from the front output — or into a container placed there."
	]
	quest.7FD6A364CBAA7533.quest_subtitle: "I love Jennie"
	quest.7FD6A364CBAA7533.title: "Power Loom"
	quest.7FE1A1E9B7570F36.quest_desc: [
		"This chapter opens automatically once you have any copper item."
	]
	quest.7FEDA6C95FF9F710.quest_desc: [
		"If you really want to make jam, the stainless steel vat speeds things up, and the canning table helps you can in bulk."
		""
		"Just place the canning table next to the vat, with its port facing the vat."
	]
	quest.861DE4C8F2AE1637.quest_desc: [
		"Pair the boring head bearing with rock-milling wheels and you get a walking mobile tunnel-borer: the wheels auto-stick to each other, breaking every block in range at once, drops flowing into containers on the structure; when they're full it stops."
		"Its output speed is a quarter of the input, in reverse; the more blocks to dig, the slower it goes — add more bearing sets to share the load."
	]
	quest.861DE4C8F2AE1637.quest_subtitle: "The Foolish Old Man simulator"
	quest.861DE4C8F2AE1637.title: "Tunnel-Boring Drill"
	quest.862220D6E1F46D6D.quest_desc: [
		"Sputnik is a simple artificial satellite: once in orbit, it permanently loads its chunk, syncs back biome color data, and can dock with computer mods to map the stars."
		"Make it your rocket's first payload — light, genuinely useful, the perfect start to a space program."
	]
	quest.862220D6E1F46D6D.quest_subtitle: "The first artificial satellite"
	quest.862220D6E1F46D6D.title: "Sputnik"
	quest.87D844347B78253A.quest_desc: [
		"Drive a train and feel the changes Simurail brings."
		""
		"(This mod has little documentation for now — explore its features in game.)"
	]
	quest.87D844347B78253A.title: "Experience Simurail"
	quest.939562E355C42578.quest_desc: [
		"The redstone accumulator stores an analog signal that rises or falls over time: input at the back adds, input at the side subtracts, and the rate can be set as slow as one hour."
		"The inductor makes its output smoothly follow the input. They are the logic blocks of vehicle automation — cruise control, auto-hover."
	]
	quest.939562E355C42578.quest_subtitle: "The art of analog signals"
	quest.939562E355C42578.title: "Accumulator \\& Inductor"
	quest.9D483B5771954B7D.quest_desc: [
		"The levitating stone (floating crystal) lets a physics structure ignore gravity: with enough of them the structure hovers in place; at low speed it drags against movement, at high speed the drag fades. It only holds altitude, never gains it — so pair it with propellers or balloons."
		"Key point: in this pack it comes from the Moon. After the landing, crush lunar soil into moon dust, heat-mix it with zinc nuggets and water into a levitating mixture, then crystallize with heat. It's the ultimate material after the Cosmonautics chapter — meet it here first."
	]
	quest.9D483B5771954B7D.quest_subtitle: "A stone from the stars"
	quest.9D483B5771954B7D.title: "Levitating Stone"
	quest.9F1E878C9C32B164.quest_desc: [
		"The magnetic stabilizer damps via ambient magnetic fields — once active, it cancels a vehicle's angular momentum and suppresses spin. Fly out of the atmosphere without one and you'll learn what a tumble-dryer feels like."
		"The holo-table projects a scaled hologram of the surrounding cosmos; tap points to zoom. Glance at it before launch — at least you'll know where you're flying."
	]
	quest.9F1E878C9C32B164.quest_subtitle: "Don't spin — read the map"
	quest.9F1E878C9C32B164.title: "Magnetic Stabilizer \\& Holo-Table"
	quest.B51D1AA532DD20C3.quest_desc: [
		"The altitude sensor outputs redstone by elevation (air pressure), the speed sensor by velocity, and the attitude sensor by orientation — ranges and directions are set in their value panels."
		"They are the senses of autopilot: e.g. pair an altitude sensor with a receiver so the airship shuts off its burner once it reaches the set height."
	]
	quest.B51D1AA532DD20C3.quest_subtitle: "Instrument flight"
	quest.B51D1AA532DD20C3.title: "Flight Sensors"
	quest.B9170ED5EB200EC6.quest_desc: [
		"Powered redstone magnets attract or repel each other: opposite poles attract, like poles repel, and attracting magnets try to align."
		"Use them for soft-docking vehicles, magnetic levitation displays — or simply to yoink a friend's ship over."
	]
	quest.B9170ED5EB200EC6.quest_subtitle: "Opposites attract"
	quest.B9170ED5EB200EC6.title: "Electromagnet"
	quest.BBB8CF5DA64DD8E5.quest_desc: [
		"Pre-launch checklist: titanium-alloy hull, liquid engine, ample biodiesel and water, vectoring plus RCS, magnetic stabilizer, space helmet and jetpack. All in place?"
		"Ignition — hold your thrust. The moment the sky outside turns from blue to black, you've arrived."
		"Reminder: the lander is a separate physics structure — plan your landing and return vehicles before launch."
	]
	quest.BBB8CF5DA64DD8E5.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to space"
	quest.BBB8CF5DA64DD8E5.title: "Breaching the Atmosphere"
	quest.C3DC82F23C65DB41.quest_desc: [
		"Simurail brings more realistic simulation to Create's railway system — trains behave closer to real railways."
		""
		"It's an enhancement of the base train system; best experienced after mastering train basics."
	]
	quest.C3DC82F23C65DB41.quest_subtitle: "Truer trains"
	quest.C3DC82F23C65DB41.title: "Simurail"
	quest.C508BE630F5C75D4.quest_desc: [
		"The steam vent is the industrial upgrade of the burner: hooked to a steam boiler, it inflates balloons with steam instead of hot air. Like the steam engine, it needs enough heat, water, and boiler capacity."
		"Multiple vents can feed one balloon in parallel, but the boiler's power tier must keep up. More lift, more class — standard issue for the airship age."
	]
	quest.C508BE630F5C75D4.quest_subtitle: "Boiler-powered flight"
	quest.C508BE630F5C75D4.title: "Steam Vent"
	quest.C7D9C85D78E2D691.quest_desc: [
		"Electric pumps draw water; resistance heaters supply heat — the grid ends at these honest, working appliances."
		"Electrically driven pumps and heat sources mean your fluid lines and heating jobs are done hauling fuel forever. That's the true meaning of electrification."
	]
	quest.CDFE9A0EE4467945.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, balloon envelopes are made from cloth — burlap, wool cloth or silk all work, dyeable as usual: one piece of cloth plus two sticks makes four envelopes. Fill the space a balloon encloses with hot air and it generates lift: place an adjustable burner right beneath the balloon, apply a redstone signal, and hot air fills it top-down — off the ground you go."
		"A jute field is the foundation of your balloon industry: soak jute into fibers and weave burlap — one field, one season, one balloon. Wool cloth works just the same (2 wool weave into 1 cloth), so shepherds lose nothing. Once you have Create machinery, arm a deployer with shears pointed at a sheep for automatic shearing."
		"Hot air must be enclosed by airtight blocks; blocks inside the balloon eat into its effective volume. Higher altitude means lower pressure and weaker lift — the balloon naturally hovers where lift meets gravity. Tune the burner's output to control your height."
		"Toss in haunted items to change the flame color — full ritual vibes."
	]
	quest.CDFE9A0EE4467945.quest_subtitle: "Humanity's oldest aircraft"
	quest.CDFE9A0EE4467945.title: "Hot Air Balloon"
	quest.CEF0C8F877152B8F.quest_desc: [
		"The typewriter is the core of the wireless redstone system: two linked typewriters pass redstone signals across any distance, and once active they take over movement controls and every assigned key."
		"Sneak-right-click to open the config screen; in binding mode, press any key to bind it to a wireless frequency. Remote-pilot an airship in the sky from the ground — or the other way around."
	]
	quest.CEF0C8F877152B8F.quest_subtitle: "The age of wireless remote control"
	quest.CEF0C8F877152B8F.title: "Linked Typewriter"
	quest.D4717D6FCB1EFBE0.quest_desc: [
		"Copper leg thrusters burn compressed air for creative-style flight; press Z to toggle the inertia damper. Double efficiency in water, quadruple in space — it's essentially a repurposed underwater thruster."
		"Copper anchoring boots give you faint gravity while standing on blocks — walk stairs normally on a weightless station, and they double as diving boots."
	]
	quest.D4717D6FCB1EFBE0.quest_subtitle: "Cheap for a reason"
	quest.D4717D6FCB1EFBE0.title: "Copper Mobility Gear"
	quest.D808071082A3E14F.quest_desc: [
		"The wheel seat is the suspension that mounts tires onto a physics structure. A redstone signal from above brakes with more friction; one from the side steers."
		"Four wheel seats, one portable engine, one steering wheel — your first off-roader is complete."
	]
	quest.D808071082A3E14F.quest_subtitle: "Where four-wheel drive begins"
	quest.D808071082A3E14F.title: "Wheel Seat"
	quest.F2502E73F2C8C024.quest_desc: [
		"The smart propeller auto-pitches along a single axis, striving to keep the prop facing upward; the gyroscopic propeller bearing keeps the prop vertical at all times — the key to building helicopters. A helicopter on a plain propeller bearing will flip itself over for you."
		"Placed facing downward, the gyroscopic bearing also stabilizes top-heavy structures; a redstone signal resets the tilt to zero."
	]
	quest.F2502E73F2C8C024.quest_subtitle: "Self-righting"
	quest.F2502E73F2C8C024.title: "Smart Propeller"
	quest.F330DDFC884A370D.quest_desc: [
		"This is the modpack's final chapter: build a real rocket, breach the atmosphere, and land on the Moon."
		"A rocket is not an item but an engineering program: titanium-alloy hull, liquid engines, fuel and oxidizer supply, attitude control and staging — and finally the spacesuit and satellites. This chapter walks you through each step in the order real rockets are built."
		"Prerequisites: the physics structures of the Aeronautics chapter and Create automation — a rocket is itself an enormous physics structure."
	]
	quest.F330DDFC884A370D.quest_subtitle: "Destination: the sea of stars"
	quest.F330DDFC884A370D.title: "Cosmonautics"
	quest.F427343F00ADE53B.quest_desc: [
		"Adjust your orbit, line up on the Moon, decelerate, descend. Remember the landing legs, remember to kill your velocity — the Moon has no atmosphere; braking is all engine retro-burn."
		"The moment your boots touch lunar soil, this modpack's journey reaches its end."
		"Don't toss the regolith — haul it home and crush it into moondust to craft floating stone, and your airships enter the true age of anti-gravity."
		"The return trip is worry-free: the rocket brings you back to the overworld, and the landing point is clamped to a sane range around spawn — no world-wide scavenger hunt. The real challenge was never coming home; it's daring to leave."
		"This is the final achievement of TerraFirma: Rebirth 4.1. Congratulations, astronaut."
	]
	quest.F427343F00ADE53B.quest_subtitle: "One small step for a man"
	quest.F427343F00ADE53B.title: "Moon Landing"
	quest.F7A35070CA5E5CA6.quest_desc: [
		"Wooden and andesite propellers mount on propeller bearings: spin to make thrust, reverse the spin (or use a wrench) to reverse the thrust."
		"Mind the air pressure: the higher you fly, the thinner the air and the weaker the thrust. With engineer's goggles on, you can see a propeller's thrust and airflow directly."
	]
	quest.F7A35070CA5E5CA6.quest_subtitle: "The shape of wind"
	quest.F7A35070CA5E5CA6.title: "Propellers"
	quest.F7BDE8E6DF156D2D.quest_desc: [
		"Mount the helm and throttle lever on a vehicle and you can drive it yourself: hold right-click to grab the helm and move the mouse to steer — sneak-turn for 45° steps. Drag the throttle with right-click for precise analog control of engine output."
		"A comparator behind the helm reads the steering angle. Remember to set the bearing mode right — don't let the structure turn back into blocks mid-drive."
	]
	quest.F7BDE8E6DF156D2D.quest_subtitle: "Got your driver's license?"
	quest.F7BDE8E6DF156D2D.title: "Helm \\& Throttle"
