	chapter.7B2E000000000100.title: "Brewing Guide"
	quest.7B2E000000000001.quest_desc: [
		"Wild grapevines drape from tree trunks in forests where the average temperature stays above 5°C."
		"Purple, red, white and green varieties each favor their own climate. Take the whole vine when you find one — it is the seed of your future vineyard."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000001.quest_subtitle: "Where the vineyard begins"
	quest.7B2E000000000001.title: "Treasure Under the Vines"
	quest.7B2E000000000002.quest_desc: [
		"Three wild vines weave into twelve trellises. Place a trellis over dirt or grass, then right-click the single trellis with a wild vine in hand to plant it."
		"Need to move it? Right-click with shears to recover the vine intact, and the trellis reverts to normal."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000002.title: "Trellis Training"
	quest.7B2E000000000003.quest_desc: [
		"Purple: 15–28°C, humidity 63+, fruits in fall. Red: 20–32°C, humidity 82+, fruits in summer."
		"White: 12–26°C, humidity 60+, fruits in fall. Green is the hardiest: -20–30°C, humidity 56+, fruits in summer."
		"Check the grape's \\\"Climate Requirement\\\" in JEI for this table; aim Jade at a trellis to see live suitability."
		"Wrong climate only stalls the vine — it never withers. And inside a greenhouse or cellar, grapes ignore the season entirely. Build one and enjoy off-season harvests."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000003.quest_subtitle: "Four grapes, four tempers"
	quest.7B2E000000000003.title: "Read the Sky, Grow the Grape"
	quest.7B2E000000000004.quest_desc: [
		"Once grape clusters ripen beneath the trellis, right-click to pick them. Grapes count as fruit: eat them, juice them, or brew them."
		"Set up extra trellises — winemaking eats through your harvest fast."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000004.title: "Harvest Time!"
	quest.7B2E000000000005.quest_desc: [
		"Five pieces of lumber make a pressing tub. Toss grapes in and stomp away (right-click) — each grape yields 125 mB of matching juice."
		"Juice can be drunk straight, scooped up with a wooden bucket, or stored in a barrel."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000005.title: "The Pressing Tub"
	quest.7B2E000000000006.quest_desc: [
		"Hold an empty wooden bucket and right-click the tub to draw out your pressed juice. Keep the four colors in their own buckets — no mixing flavors."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000006.title: "Juice by the Bucket"
	quest.7B2E000000000007.quest_desc: [
		"Bottles come from TFC glassblowing: place an olivine glass batch on the blowing table and work it in the order Blow, Blow, Pinch, Saw."
		"You will go through plenty of bottles later — blow a few extra while you are at it."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000007.title: "Empty Bottles"
	quest.7B2E000000000008.quest_desc: [
		"Two TFC barrels, a log and some lumber assemble into the Kaleidoscope brewing barrel."
		"Fill it with juice, load empty bottles, and wait: a bottle ferments in 2400 ticks. The barrel ages through seven grades — the longer you wait, the richer and stronger the wine becomes."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000008.quest_subtitle: "Let time do the work"
	quest.7B2E000000000008.title: "The Brewing Barrel"
	quest.7B2E000000000009.quest_desc: [
		"Tap the barrel and take your wine! Sneak-right-click to set a bottle on the ground, then right-click to stack more, up to four per pile — that is how tavern shelves are stocked."
		"Take a sip: purple wine grants Haste, perfect for a hard day's work."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000009.title: "First Vintage"
	quest.7B2E00000000000A.quest_desc: [
		"Two ways to go beyond the basics: add sixteen of any flower to the barrel for flower wine, or sixteen ice blocks for ice wine."
		"Spirits brewed in TFC barrels — beer, cider, whiskey, rye whiskey, corn whiskey, vodka, rum and sake — can all be bottled in the brewing barrel too."
		"Smith a cast iron sheet on a tier-2 anvil into a tap, fit it on the barrel, and pouring a drink gains some ceremony."
	]
	quest.7B2E00000000000A.quest_subtitle: "Flower wines, ice wines and spirits"
	quest.7B2E00000000000A.title: "A Bouquet of Flavors"
	quest.7B2E00000000000B.quest_desc: [
		"Lash a wild vine to a compass and it will point you toward undiscovered wild grapevines nearby (recipe: compass + any wild grapevine)."
		"A real time-saver when hunting down all four varieties."
	]
	quest.7B2E00000000000B.title: "Vine-Seeking Compass"
	quest.7B2E00000000000C.quest_desc: [
		"Bar counters, stools, sofas, cabinets, glassware holders, chalkboard menus, warm string lights... the Kaleidoscope set has every wooden fitting a tavern needs."
		"Build a little tavern of your own, line the racks with your vintages, and welcome travelers in from the road."
			"Kaleidoscope's pots, steamers, cutting boards, brew barrels, taps and bar stools all work on Create contraptions — a food truck or a flying tavern, your call."
]
	quest.7B2E00000000000C.title: "Open Your Own Tavern"
	quest.7B2E000000000020.quest_desc: [
		"Eight sticks around a single plank make one sturdy wheel. Wheels are shared by every cart, so keep a few spare."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000020.title: "Wheels Rolling"
	quest.7B2E000000000021.quest_desc: [
		"Two wheels and a few planks make a hand cart: 27 stacks of storage, pulled by your own two hands, and dirt cheap."
		"A moving-day miracle available since the Copper Age (chests need a saw) — right-click the handles and drag it along."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000021.title: "The Hand Cart"
	quest.7B2E000000000022.quest_desc: [
		"Seven planks and two wheels; hitch a horse, donkey or mule and let it pull."
		"Two seats aboard: the driver up front, and room behind for one more passenger or animal. Fly a banner for extra style."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000022.title: "The Animal Cart"
	quest.7B2E000000000023.quest_desc: [
		"Fit the plow with a hoe to till, a shovel to stamp dirt paths, or an axe to strip logs. The reaper needs a driver and mows down every crop it passes. The seed drill holds 9 stacks of seeds and plants as it goes."
		"With all three hitched up, one farmer can tend fields of any size."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000023.quest_subtitle: "Plow, reaper and seed drill"
	quest.7B2E000000000023.title: "The Field Trio"
	quest.7B2E000000000024.quest_desc: [
		"The supply cart swallows 54 stacks, seats one, and is animal-drawn with banner support like its cousins."
		"For long hauls, ore runs and moving day, it carries twice the load of a hand cart."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000024.title: "The Supply Cart"
	quest.7B2E000000000025.quest_desc: [
		"A TFC boat is crafted from five TFC planks. Place it on water and right-click to hop in — the best budget ferry of the early game."
		"Want to haul cargo by water? Hold a TFC chest and right-click a boat already floating on water, and it upgrades into a chest boat with a full chest of storage."
		"Don't bother looking up vanilla boat or chest boat recipes — vanilla planks don't exist in this world; those recipes are leftovers. TFC boats are the way."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000025.quest_subtitle: "Boats & Chest Boats"
	quest.7B2E000000000025.title: "Waterway Transport"
	quest.436FA5779CCC1FE4.quest_desc: [
		"The kiln is a multiblock structure for firing items in bulk: its heart is a firebox, walled in with clay bricks or fire bricks (clay bricks are far cheaper). The firebox must be fully enclosed, with a grate on top to let the heat rise into the chamber."
		""
		"The simplest build: firebox at the bottom, a grate above it, clay bricks on all four sides, and a fireproof door for access — that's a minimal working kiln."
		""
		"Below bright red the firebox heats 64 blocks at once; above bright red, 128. If the structure is broken mid-heating, all progress is lost and it must be resealed — and if the temperature drifts from the set point, the timer restarts."
		""
		"Tip: hook a bellows up to the firebox, like in the picture, to push the temperature higher. The fireproof door costs cast iron sheets — if you can't afford one yet, just brick the wall up solid and break a block whenever you need access."
		""
		"How to run it: load the chamber with pottery, molds or unfired bricks, seal the kiln shut, fill the firebox with fuel and light it (a bellows heats it faster), wait out the timer, then open up and collect your goods. Full details live in the \\\"Kilns\\\" entry of the TFC field guide."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quest/kiln.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
	]
	quest.436FA5779CCC1FE4.quest_subtitle: "Batch firing, up to 128 at a time"
	quest.436FA5779CCC1FE4.title: "The Kiln \\& Firebox"
	quest.5E1A2B3C4D5E6F70.quest_desc: [
		"Mud bricks are the cheapest cellar walls: right-click dirt with a jug or barrel of fresh water to get mud, mix in straw to craft wet mud bricks, and lay them out to harden for a day (rain stops the drying)."
		""
		"Four bricks craft into one mud brick block — insulation on par with stone, and the whole chain needs no metal tools. You can stockpile every wall block for your cellar before your first copper pick."
		""
		"For mass production, wet mud bricks dry in a smoking rack, or let a Create Encased Fan blow over fire to dry a whole stack at once."
	]
	quest.5E1A2B3C4D5E6F70.quest_subtitle: "Insulation without a single ingot"
	quest.5E1A2B3C4D5E6F70.title: "Mud Bricks \\& Cellar Walls"
	quest.7D3E4A5B6C7D8E9F.quest_desc: [
		"This pack runs TFC: Real World — the world is not random, it is our planet. Continents, oceans, elevation and Köppen climate zones all come from real geographic data (Equal Earth projection)."
		""
		"By default you spawn near the real coordinates of Beijing, China (39.9°N, 116.4°E). Temperature and rainfall vary realistically with latitude: colder toward the poles, hotter toward the equator, and season length follows latitude too."
		""
		"Tip: the Earth is round — keep heading north and you really will reach the North Pole. Mark waypoints in JourneyMap before any expedition, and plan your way home first."
	]
	quest.7D3E4A5B6C7D8E9F.quest_subtitle: "You spawn on the coordinates of Beijing"
	quest.7D3E4A5B6C7D8E9F.title: "A Real World"
	quest.7B2E000000000026.quest_desc: [
		"The music sheet is the heart of Music Maker: one paper, one ink sac and one feather. Hold the sheet and right-click to open the composer — beats run left to right, pitch runs bottom to top. Left-click a cell to place a note; click again to remove it."
		""
		"The toolbar sets tempo (BPM) and measure interval; ▶ previews, ■ stops. Press N to show neighboring sheets — keep several sheets side by side in your hotbar and they chain into one long song."
		""
		"When the piece is done, hit \\\"Sign and Close\\\": a signed sheet can no longer be edited, but it carries your name. Craft a signed sheet together with a blank one to clone copies for your bandmates."
		""
		"{\\\"text\\\":\\\"▶ Mod page \\& video demo (CurseForge)\\\",\\\"clickEvent\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"open_url\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/music-maker-mod\\\"},\\\"underlined\\\":true,\\\"color\\\":\\\"aqua\\\"}"
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000026.quest_subtitle: "Ink on paper, and it becomes a song"
	quest.7B2E000000000026.title: "Sheets \\& Composing"
	quest.7B2E000000000027.quest_desc: [
		"A score needs players. Every instrument in this pack is reworked to TFC materials: TFC planks and sticks for the body, wool yarn for strings, copper/gold/wrought-iron rods for the metal voices. Guitars, banjos, violins, cellos, flutes, oboes, saxophones, trumpets, French horns, xylophones, chimes, sansulas, cymbals... search xercamusic in JEI for every recipe."
		""
		"Hold an instrument and right-click to jam live: click the keys or drumheads in the play GUI. Grab some friends, one instrument each, and you've got a band."
		""
		"In the composer you can lock a preview instrument to hear your piece in its voice while writing."
		""
		"Two special members: the Redstone Guitar and Redstone Piano sound off when powered by redstone. And the Voice of God — forged from a gold sheet, a diamond, an emerald and a French horn — is the most extravagant instrument in the pack, bar none."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000027.quest_subtitle: "Fifteen instruments, every one sings"
	quest.7B2E000000000027.title: "The Instrument Workshop"
	quest.7B2E000000000028.quest_desc: [
		"The music box is an automatic player: insert a signed sheet, then right-click it or feed it a redstone pulse and it plays the piece — in whatever instrument voice you previewed while composing."
		""
		"The metronome emits redstone pulses at its set tempo: use it to keep several music boxes in sync, or to keep time for your live band."
		""
		"Advanced trick: give several music boxes different voices of the same song and you've built an automatic orchestra. Add a redstone clock and your base can chime its anthem on the hour."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000028.quest_subtitle: "Let the village hear your song"
	quest.7B2E000000000028.title: "Music Box \\& Metronome"
	quest.7B2E00000000002A.quest_desc: [
		"Create: Towed teaches livestock to haul moving structures: leash a cow, horse or other large animal to a physicalized vehicle or contraption and it will drag it along."
		""
		"A harvester too heavy for a horse cart? A rolling base? Give a pair of sturdy oxen a try. Just leave them some room on the slopes."
	]
	quest.7B2E00000000002A.quest_subtitle: "Even an ox can pull a train"
	quest.7B2E00000000002A.title: "Animal Towing"
	quest.7B2E00000000002B.quest_desc: [
		"Aviator's Goggles plus a Contraption Diagram make the Schematician's Goggles. Wearing them switches on a drafting view: the world renders in blueprint outlines, and any physicalized structure you look at (ships, airships) shows its center of mass with its force groups — lift, drag, thrust, gravity — drawn as colored vectors."
		""
		"Will the airship flip? Is the center of mass stable? One look tells you. Right-click while holding them, or use the keybind (search \\\"Schematician\\\" in Controls), to toggle the drafting view."
	]
	quest.7B2E00000000002B.quest_subtitle: "See the forces and the center of mass"
	quest.7B2E00000000002B.title: "Schematician's Goggles"
	quest.7B2E00000000002C.quest_desc: [
		"Create: Copycats+ brings a full family of skinnable structural blocks: copycat blocks, slabs, stairs, slopes, fences, doors, cogwheels, fluid pipes... Place one, then right-click it with any full block to copy that block's texture."
		""
		"Hide your machinery inside stone walls, or run shafts in rare woodgrain — copycats do it all. Recipes mostly cost TFC zinc ingots; search copycats in JEI for the full roster."
	]
	quest.7B2E00000000002C.quest_subtitle: "A thousand faces for one block"
	quest.7B2E00000000002C.title: "Copycat Blocks"
	task.7B2E000000000102.title: "Please read the following, then click Confirm"
	task.7B2E000000000105.title: "Please read the following, then click Confirm"
	task.7B2E000000000108.title: "Please read the following, then click Confirm"
	task.7B2E000000000110.title: "Please read the following, then click Confirm"
	quest.7B2E000000000040.title: "Home Computer"
	quest.7B2E000000000040.quest_subtitle: "A stone chassis with a Lua soul"
	quest.7B2E000000000040.quest_desc: [
		"Smooth rock for the chassis, redstone for the circuits, a glass pane for the screen — your first computer is born."
		"Right-click to boot into CraftOS. Type help for commands, programs to see what ships with it."
		"Type lua, then print(\"Hello, TFCR!\") to say hi to yourself."
		"Computers have no hard drive. Programs survive a reboot, but for real storage you want a disk drive and floppy disks."
	]
	task.7B2E000000000140.title: "Craft a Computer"
	quest.7B2E000000000041.title: "Disk Drive"
	quest.7B2E000000000041.quest_subtitle: "A hard drive for your computer"
	quest.7B2E000000000041.quest_desc: [
		"A disk drive lets a computer read and write floppy disks — programs and files included."
		"Floppy disks are crafted from paper, redstone dust and dye. Sixteen dyes, sixteen colors — sort away."
		"Insert a disk and use copy to back up your code; label set gives the disk a name."
	]
	task.7B2E000000000141.title: "Disk Drive"
	task.7B2E000000000142.title: "Any Floppy Disk"
	quest.7B2E000000000042.title: "Monitor"
	quest.7B2E000000000042.quest_subtitle: "Bigger is better"
	quest.7B2E000000000042.quest_desc: [
		"A single monitor works with a right-click, but place several of the same tier together and they merge into one big screen."
		"Use the monitor command to output to it: monitor right hello lights up the monitor on the right."
		"Advanced monitors (gold trim) support color and touch — tap the screen and your program receives the event."
	]
	task.7B2E000000000143.title: "Monitor"
	task.7B2E000000000144.title: "Join two or more monitors into one big screen"
	quest.7B2E000000000043.title: "Printer"
	quest.7B2E000000000043.quest_subtitle: "Put words on paper"
	quest.7B2E000000000043.quest_desc: [
		"The printer puts text on paper: load paper and dye, write with edit on a computer, then run the print program."
		"Printed pages can be bound into books for your shelves — movable type, TerraFirma style."
	]
	task.7B2E000000000145.title: "Printer"
	quest.7B2E000000000044.title: "Pocket Computer"
	quest.7B2E000000000044.quest_subtitle: "A computer in your pocket"
	quest.7B2E000000000044.quest_desc: [
		"A computer shrunk to pocket size, ready anywhere. The golden apple in the recipe is its battery and shell — don't ask, it's technology."
		"Equip it with a wireless modem and remote-control your whole base network from your pocket."
	]
	task.7B2E000000000146.title: "Pocket Computer"
	quest.7B2E000000000045.title: "Turtle"
	quest.7B2E000000000045.quest_subtitle: "A robot that does the work for you"
	quest.7B2E000000000045.quest_desc: [
		"A turtle is a computer on tracks: write a program and it will mine, chop, farm and build for you."
		"A turtle only earns its keep with a proper tool — normal turtles take red steel tools, advanced ones blue steel. They answer only to those who have mastered the deepest forge fire."
		"Type excavate 5 in a turtle and it digs a 5x5 pit on its own; see help for more programs."
		"Turtles burn fuel: put coal or charcoal in their inventory and type refuel."
	]
	task.7B2E000000000147.title: "Turtle"
	task.7B2E000000000148.title: "Fuel a turtle and type refuel once"
	quest.7B2E000000000046.title: "Wired Network"
	quest.7B2E000000000046.quest_subtitle: "Hook everything up"
	quest.7B2E000000000046.quest_desc: [
		"Cables and wired modems link peripherals into a network: attach a modem to the side of a disk drive or monitor, right-click to activate, then cable it back to the computer."
		"Once networked, the disks in the drive can be read remotely by the computer."
	]
	task.7B2E000000000149.title: "Networking Cable"
	task.7B2E00000000014A.title: "Wired Modem"
	quest.7B2E000000000047.title: "Wireless Modem"
	quest.7B2E000000000047.quest_subtitle: "Messages through the air"
	quest.7B2E000000000047.quest_desc: [
		"Wireless modems network computers through the air. Both ends need one, and the normal tier has limited range."
		"The advanced wireless modem, built around a ghast tear, reaches across dimensions — true long-range communication in the TerraFirma world."
		"Open rednet.open(\"right\") on both computers, then rednet.send on one and rednet.receive on the other to pass messages."
	]
	task.7B2E00000000014B.title: "Wireless Modem"
	quest.7B2E000000000048.title: "Source & Target Blocks"
	quest.7B2E000000000048.quest_subtitle: "Let Create machines talk"
	quest.7B2E000000000048.quest_desc: [
		"CC:C Bridge is the bridge between Create and computers."
		"A target block with a Display Link feeds rotation speed, stress and fluid levels to the computer; a source block does the reverse, letting the computer write text back onto Display Links."
		"Time to build a live dashboard for your steam engines."
	]
	task.7B2E00000000014C.title: "Source Block"
	task.7B2E00000000014D.title: "Target Block"
	quest.7B2E000000000049.title: "RedRouter & Animatronic"
	quest.7B2E000000000049.quest_subtitle: "Circuits that move — just for fun"
	quest.7B2E000000000049.quest_desc: [
		"The RedRouter block lets a computer read and write redstone signals directly — flip an entire wall of lamps with one API call."
		"The Scroller Pane is a little dial for picking numbers; computers can read and set it, perfect as a control knob."
		"The Animatronic is a pure toy: drive its body and face from a computer and stage your own puppet show."
	]
	task.7B2E00000000014E.title: "RedRouter Block"
	task.7B2E00000000014F.title: "Scroller Pane"
	task.7B2E000000000150.title: "Animatronic"

	quest.7B2E000000000051.title: "Flight Computer"
	quest.7B2E000000000051.quest_subtitle: "Give your rocket a brain"
	quest.7B2E000000000051.quest_desc: [
		"ComputerCraft is natively wired into Cosmonautics: connect a computer to a rocket engine and it becomes your flight computer."
		"Method cheat sheet: setThrust() or throttle() for the throttle; setComputerGimbal() to take over the vector nozzle; isIgnited() for ignition state; getFuelTicks() to estimate remaining burn time."
		"Trigger staging separators through the redstone API and you can script a fully automatic launch: ignition, gravity turn, coast, circularization burn, booster separation — all in one go."
		"For more peripheral methods, type lua and check help, or revisit the computer quests in the Utilities chapter."
	]
	task.7B2E000000000151.title: "Any Computer"
	task.7B2E000000000152.title: "Read a live thrust value from an engine with a computer"
	quest.7B2E00000000004A.quest_desc: [
		"CC:Sable builds four aeronautics APIs into every computer — no peripheral needed, ready on boot. Carry a computer aboard a physics-simulated airship and it reads the vessel's live state."
		""
		"&6aero&f — atmospheric data: getAirPressure(pos) for air pressure, getGravity(), getMagneticNorth(), and getUniversalDrag()."
		""
		"&6sublevel&f — physics-structure state (only returns readings while the computer is on a physicalized ship or airship): getVelocity(), getAngularVelocity(), getCenterOfMass(), getMass(), getInertiaTensor() — and setName() to christen your vessel."
		""
		"&6matrix / quaternion&f — math libraries for attitude solving; the rom also ships an advanced_math module with a PID controller, statistics and higher math functions."
		""
		"Typical build: an advanced pocket computer with a wireless modem, relaying altitude, speed and attitude live — or go hardcore and write a PID loop to auto-trim a balloon. Type &6help aero&f or &6help sublevel&f in-game for the full docs."
	]
	quest.7B2E00000000004A.quest_subtitle: "Give your airship a brain"
	quest.7B2E00000000004A.title: "Fly-By-Wire Computer"
	quest.5D23F7FDFBBEEA10.quest_desc: [
		"Feed rotational power into a gyroscope and it constrains your vessel's attitude, resisting roll and pitch — the stabilization core of any large airship or ship."
		""
		"Mind the new physics — it no longer behaves like older versions:"
		"· Flywheels have spin-up inertia: they take a dozen seconds to reach full speed after power is applied, not instant;"
		"· Effectiveness scales with RPM: full power at 128 RPM (tuned down from the default 256 in this pack), proportionally weaker below;"
		"· One gyro only covers so much moment of inertia — big hulls need several in parallel. If the tooltip says &6Underpowered&f, add more units."
		""
		"Read the tooltip for live status: Off / Unstable / Underpowered / Steady / Level."
		""
		"Old rule stands: never bolt one onto a rocket — a locked attitude makes every vector thruster useless."
	]
	quest.5D23F7FDFBBEEA10.quest_subtitle: "Steady as she spins"
	quest.5D23F7FDFBBEEA10.title: "Gyroscope"
	quest.7B2E000000000050.quest_desc: [
		"Magic is within reach: a book, a block of red wool, three obsidian and two wrought iron plates assemble into an enchanting table."
		"Surround it with bookshelves — any TFC wooden bookshelf powers it, but only while it holds books: each stored book adds half a point of enchanting power, a full 6-book shelf matches three vanilla shelves, and five full shelves unlock the strongest enchantments."
		"Enchanting costs experience and powder: any crushed gem powder works as fuel (lapis lazuli still works too). XP comes from mining — richer ore grades drop more."
		"All TFC metal gear can be enchanted: copper, the bronzes, wrought iron, steel and black steel — red and blue steel take enchantments best."
		"Five exclusive enchantments: Piercing, Crushing and Slashing Protection (armor, mutually exclusive, five levels each); Slow Aspect (weapon, slows whatever you hit); Hunting (weapon, heavy bonus damage against predators)."
	]
	quest.7B2E000000000050.quest_subtitle: "Wrought iron stand, gem powder spark"
	quest.7B2E000000000050.title: "Enchanting Table"
}